</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SECURITY NUMBER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Social Security Number is a government-issued identifier necessary for borrowers to qualify for a loan, ensuring their creditworthiness."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Social Security Number is a unique identifier required for all borrowers to validate identity and taxation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Social Security Number is a unique identifier required for borrowers, ensuring they have valid identification for loan processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d77c56c7ef7f25742c687f6ad137c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce8ebe270f2feee194ded8e3d4becdb2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 275}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT SCORE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Credit Score is a numerical expression based on the analysis of a borrower's credit files, indicating creditworthiness and used by lenders to make approval decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Credit Score is a numerical expression of a borrower's creditworthiness, crucial for determining eligibility for loans and other financial products."&lt;SEP&gt;"A credit score is a numerical representation of a person's creditworthiness, based on a range of criteria, which lenders use to evaluate the risk of offering a loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Score is a numerical representation of a borrower's creditworthiness, derived from their credit history and used by lenders in evaluating loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Score is a numerical representation of a borrower's creditworthiness, influencing their ability to qualify for loans and the terms offered."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61ba5485d92daa30adf4ee02bfab7d8a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 275}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraisals are assessments of property value that are required during the mortgage lending process to ensure the loan amount aligns with the property's worth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisals involve the process of evaluating a property's value based on established standards and guidelines, including measuring living areas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COOPERATIVE PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cooperative Properties are residential buildings owned by a corporation, in which residents own shares in the corporation rather than owning their individual units outright."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cooperative Properties are residential buildings owned by a corporation. Residents own shares in the corporation rather than owning individual units outright, providing a unique ownership structure for housing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cooperative Properties are residential buildings where a corporation owns the property and residents purchase shares rather than owning the real estate outright, eligible for certain loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 133}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 387}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANUFACTURED HOMES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Manufactured Homes are defined as dwellings built on a permanent chassis and attached to a permanent foundation system, subject to specific underwriting guidelines for mortgage eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes are prefabricated homes that must meet specific standards, including foundation requirements, to qualify for loans offered by Flagstar Bank."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes are prefabricated houses that can be eligible for certain loans but are subject to different eligibility criteria than traditional homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes are prefabricated structures built typically in a factory setting and brought to a site for residential occupancy, subjected to specific financing requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes are prefabricated structures that are built in a factory and can be transported to a location, which may not always be eligible for all loan types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes are prefabricated structures that are built to be transportable, often less expensive than traditional houses, and come with various regulations concerning loans and appraisals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes refer to residences that are built off-site and transported to locations, which may be ineligible for certain loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes refer to residential structures built off-site that meet specific regulatory requirements, notable in trade equity discussions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured homes are factory-built structures that are subject to specific guidelines for appraisal, location, and mortgage requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4de71275bc933c2c228984f601d0e0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32546641e2f2fec0a52f658ed70fc338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 383}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ONE-CLOSE CONSTRUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"One-Close Construction is a loan product that combines the construction and permanent financing into a single mortgage, simplifying the financing process for borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"One-Close Construction refers to a streamlined financing option for home buyers that allows them to close on both the purchase of a lot and the construction of a home in a single transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMESTYLE RENOVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Homestyle Renovation is a loan product allowing borrowers to finance both the purchase price and renovation costs into one mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homestyle Renovation is a loan product that allows borrowers to finance renovations alongside the purchase or refinance of a home."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homestyle Renovation is a specific mortgage product offered by Fannie Mae which allows financing for both home purchase and renovations within the same loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH LTV REFINANCE MORTGAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High LTV Refinance Mortgages allow homeowners to refinance their properties with a high loan-to-value ratio, though these may have restrictions or be suspended."&lt;SEP&gt;"High LTV Refinance Mortgages are loans that allow refinancing with a high loan-to-value ratio, although they may have specific qualifiers such as current suspension by GSEs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FREDDIE LPA ACE +PDR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Freddie LPA ACE +PDR is a risk assessment technology used to determine eligibility for loans, specifically in appraisals, but is noted as not eligible in this context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGE OF ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Age of Assets refers to the time frame for which financial documents and account statements must be dated, impacting mortgage eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age of Assets refers to the time frame within which financial documents must be current, ensuring accurate assessment during the mortgage application process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 292}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLOOD INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Flood Insurance is a policy that protects property owners against losses due to flooding, which is noted as a requirement for properties in certain designated areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flood Insurance is a specific type of coverage designed to protect homes and businesses from water damage, especially in areas prone to floods, ensuring financial security for property owners."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flood Insurance is a specific type of insurance required to protect against water damage in certain property types, particularly those in flood-prone areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flood Insurance is a type of insurance that protects against property damage from flooding, referenced in the underwriting guidelines as a necessary consideration for certain properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefb0ad4148eab93b794bfdc3eb3eac7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 133}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 388}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECOND HOMES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Second Homes are properties that are not the primary residence of the owner but are used for vacation or leisure, usually financed differently than primary residences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Homes are properties used as additional residences, which also have designated LTV/CLTV thresholds for refinancing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Homes are residential properties that individuals own in addition to their primary residence, often subject to specific minimum credit score requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Homes refer to additional residential properties owned by an individual, which may have different eligibility stipulations compared to primary residences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Homes refer to properties that are not primary residences but are used for vacation or leisure, often associated with specific financing requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Homes refer to residential properties that are not the primary residence of the homeowner, generally subject to different financing terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-645973893eaf0e8d2eb4a7822c3fe6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 133}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 387}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INVESTMENT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Investment Properties are real estate assets owned by individuals as an investment, subject to specific underwriting requirements and escrow processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Properties are real estate assets purchased for rental income or capital gain, requiring specific loan conditions outlined in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Properties are real estate assets that are purchased with the intention of earning a return through rental income or appreciation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Properties are real estate holdings that are owned with the intention of generating income, whether through rental income or resale."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Properties are real estate properties purchased with the aim of generating income through rental or resale."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Properties are real estate properties that are purchased to generate income, often subject to specific financial assessments and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Properties are real estate that is bought with the intention of earning rental income or appreciation, key in determining loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Properties consist of real estate bought primarily for rental generation or capital gain, subject to specific loan criteria mentioned in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Properties refer to properties that the borrower does not occupy and are considered for rental income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Properties refer to real estate owned for generating rental income or resale, rather than for personal use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment properties are real estate acquired primarily for generating profit, through rental income or resale, often involving specific financing options tailored to real estate investors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment properties are real estate owned for rental income or capital appreciation, subject to stricter lending requirements as outlined in the guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment properties refer to real estate purchased for profit-generating purposes, which have specific LTV/CLTV requirements in refinancing options."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12708616563afb36a31ad3cf8523241b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46cceddf672b67421d8f87a3665f1ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-645973893eaf0e8d2eb4a7822c3fe6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 133}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 387}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;3-4 UNIT RENOVATION LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"3-4 Unit Renovation Loans are financing options specifically designed for the purchase and renovation of multi-unit properties containing three to four residential units."&lt;SEP&gt;"3-4 Unit Renovation loans are specifically designed for properties with multiple units that require renovation, which must meet certain underwriting frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 275}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ONE-CLOSE CONSTRUCTION LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"One-Close Construction Loans enable borrowers to finance the construction of a new home and convert it to a permanent mortgage in a single transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"One-Close Construction loans are a financing method that combines land purchase and home construction into a single mortgage product, facilitating streamlined processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FREDDIE MAC QUARTERLY ACCOUNT STATEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Freddie Mac Quarterly account statements are required documents proving the status of financial accounts, critical for the appraisal and loan qualification process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 292}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGENCY PRODUCTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Agency Products refer to mortgage products that are backed by government-sponsored enterprises, ensuring certain standards and protections for lenders and borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agency products refer to financial products offered by government-sponsored enterprises like Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, which are designed to facilitate home loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANUAL UNDERWRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Manual underwriting is a process where loan applications are evaluated without automated underwriting systems, relying on human judgment, and is noted as not permitted for the loans mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 354}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COASTAL BARRIER RESOURCES AREA (CBRA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Coastal Barrier Resources Areas (CBRA) are designated regions that are protected from development and certain lending practices due to environmental sensitivities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coastal Barrier Resources Areas (CBRA) are designated zones where certain types of development and lending are restricted due to environmental concerns."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 133}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 388}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OTHERWISE PROTECTED FLOOD AREA (OPA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Otherwise Protected Flood Areas (OPA) are regions that require special considerations and are prohibited for loans as indicated in the underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 133}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 388}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDOS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Condos refer to condominium units subject to specific loan policies, including limitations on the percentage of units that Flagstar can lend in any project."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condos, or condominiums, are individually owned units within a larger property, commonly featuring shared amenities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 453}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEPOSITORY ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Depository Accounts include demand deposits, savings accounts, and certificates of deposit, which can be used fully for determining income streams in mortgage qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depository Accounts include various types of bank accounts where funds can be held, such as checking and savings accounts, essential for verifying borrower assets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depository Accounts refer to accounts that hold funds and are to be verified during the mortgage process for eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depository Accounts refer to financial accounts held at banks or financial institutions where funds are deposited, allowing account holders to manage and withdraw their money."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depository accounts are bank accounts from which funds must be verified as part of the loan application process, required to be updated within a specified timeframe."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depository accounts refer to accounts held in financial institutions where funds are stored and verified for mortgage qualification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-452a34dee684e3a93929cc44930deb38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a9a7e59e34af57946c09cfa07672f92</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 291}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENOVATION AND CONSTRUCTION PRODUCTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renovation and Construction Products involve financing documents and guidelines for home renovation and building projects, offered by Freddie Mac but not available through Flagstar."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4d4f9535ffe4c256b83a381ed8c6791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDOMINIUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Condominium is a type of housing where individuals own their units while sharing common areas with other residents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condominiums refer to residential complex properties where individual units are owned by residents and can be subject to certain lending restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 152}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTIONAL LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Conventional Loan refers to a mortgage that is not insured or guaranteed by the government, typically involving stricter credit requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Insurance is a financial product required in certain mortgage transactions, ensuring lenders are protected against borrower default."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a financial product that protects lenders from potential defaults on loans, as outlined in the guidelines for its coverage determination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a policy that protects lenders against losses from mortgage defaults, often required for loans with low down payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a product required for certain loans, which cannot have escrow waivers when required by the lender."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a type of insurance designed to protect the lender against losses due to borrower default."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a type of insurance that protects lenders against the risk of borrower default."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance refers to a policy that protects lenders against losses due to borrower default, thus promoting risk management in mortgage lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed0db69e97fa62c70a7cb29c5e75fe07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-241759937af28f9856986aac2ee15cb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
