<node id="&quot;POWER OF ATTORNEY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Power of Attorney (POA) is a legal document that allows one person to act on behalf of another in legal or financial matters, specifically in relation to mortgage transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Power of Attorney is a legal document allowing one individual to act on behalf of another, noted for its specific use limitations within mortgage transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Power of Attorney is a legal document that allows one person to act on behalf of another, particularly in situations where the principal is unable to sign documents themselves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Power of Attorney is a legal document that allows one person to act on behalf of another, with specific guidelines related to its use mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Power of Attorney refers to a legal document allowing one person to act on behalf of another in legal transactions, with specific stipulations for its use in financial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Power of Attorney refers to a legal document authorizing one person to act on behalf of another in legal or financial matters, with specific requirements for transactions."</data>
