</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-OUT REFINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Cash-Out Refinance is a type of mortgage refinancing where the borrower takes out additional money against their home's equity, typically used for funding other expenditures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a financial event where a borrower refinances their mortgage for more than the amount owed, taking the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a financial transaction where a homeowner refinances their mortgage for more than they owe and takes the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a mortgage product that allows homeowners to refinance their existing mortgage for more than they owe and take the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a mortgage refinancing option that allows for borrowing against the equity of a property, resulting in cash for the homeowner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a refinancing option that allows borrowers to take out a new mortgage for more than the amount owed on their existing mortgage, taking the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a type of mortgage transaction that allows property owners to take equity out of their property, typically associated with manufactured homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out Refinance is a financial transaction where a borrower takes out a new mortgage for more than they owe, receiving the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out Refinance is a mortgage refinancing option that allows homeowners to take out a new loan for more than they owe on their existing loan, cashing out the difference."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out Refinance is a mortgage transaction where the borrower refinances an existing mortgage for more than they owe, taking the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out Refinance is a transaction that allows homeowners to refinance their mortgage for more than they owe, taking out the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out Refinance is described as a specific type of refinancing event where a borrower takes additional funds beyond paying off debts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out refinance involves refinancing a loan for more than what is owed, allowing borrowers to take out the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out refinance is a financial transaction that allows homeowners to refinance their existing mortgage while extracting equity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out refinance refers to a financial transaction where a borrower takes out a new mortgage for more than owed and receives the excess in cash, restricted under the guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out refinance refers to a refinancing transaction where the borrower takes out a new mortgage for more than the amount owed on the existing mortgage, receiving the difference in cash."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e912b60195be8ca87a44127ef55d282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b41d8874999d184a44ade7d9217e24a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458b7b4c2fb6c14a263231eb6f3f6192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6843059eea11d10d23493c39af4afd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-241759937af28f9856986aac2ee15cb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
