<node id="&quot;LAND TRUSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Land Trusts are legal entities that hold title to real estate property for the benefit of the trust's beneficiaries, often used to manage property ownership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Land Trusts refer to specific types of property ownership mechanisms that are deemed ineligible in Freddie Mac's guidelines for mortgage transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Land Trusts/Community Land Trusts are organizations involved in holding land for community benefits, but are noted as ineligible for certain financing under Freddie Mac guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-241759937af28f9856986aac2ee15cb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10b21d56993c3c6bc0aa80dd4168911&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 352}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 544}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLOSING IN TRUST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Closing in Trust outlines the guidelines for how loans can be secured under living revocable trusts, showing the legal frameworks that govern property transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing in Trust refers to a legal arrangement in property transactions that requires validation through an attorney opinion letter to meet agency warranties."</data>
