<node id="&quot;EFFECTIVE DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Effective Date is the specific date at which the appraisal analysis is based, marking the conditions of the real estate market at that time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Effective Date refers to the date on which a document, contract, or commitment becomes valid and enforceable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Effective Date refers to the date when a document, such as a title commitment, is valid and under which its terms are applicable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Effective date refers to the date when a title commitment begins to be valid and enforceable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d10b21d56993c3c6bc0aa80dd4168911&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d864e2754e1d5a70d89033bc8babcdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cb7303f4ec7884e602c27628160dc28</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 515}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GAP LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Gap Letter is a document provided by a title insurer that extends the validity of a title commitment under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Gap Letter is a document provided by a title insurer to extend coverage if a title commitment exceeds a certain timeframe, ensuring ongoing protection."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gap letter is a letter provided by a title insurer when a title commitment exceeds a set duration, granting additional time validly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gap Letter is a document provided by a title insurer that extends the validity of a title commitment beyond the original commitment date, ensuring coverage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46cceddf672b67421d8f87a3665f1ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10b21d56993c3c6bc0aa80dd4168911&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d864e2754e1d5a70d89033bc8babcdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cb7303f4ec7884e602c27628160dc28</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 514}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMUM REPRESENTATIVE CREDIT SCORE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimum Representative Credit Score is the lowest credit score that a borrower must have to qualify for certain loan conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minimum Representative Credit Score refers to the lowest credit score acceptable for various mortgage transactions, a crucial criterion in borrower qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46cceddf672b67421d8f87a3665f1ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10b21d56993c3c6bc0aa80dd4168911</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 435}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LTV (Loan-to-Value Ratio) is a financial term used by lenders to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, impacting financing terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV refers to Loan-to-Value ratio, a financial term used to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV stands for Loan-to-Value ratio, a financial term that describes the ratio of a loan to the value of the property purchased."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV stands for Loan-to-Value, a financial ratio that compares the amount of the loan to the appraised value of the property being purchased."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV, or Loan-to-Value ratio, is a financial term that compares the amount of a loan to the value of the asset purchased, often expressed as a percentage."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV, or Loan-to-Value ratio, is a financial term used by lenders to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV, or Loan-to-Value ratio, is a financial term used to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, crucial in mortgage lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV, or Loan-to-Value ratio, is a financial term used to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, indicating the risk involved for lenders."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV, or loan-to-value ratio, is a financial term used to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, influencing underwriting and eligibility for mortgages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46cceddf672b67421d8f87a3665f1ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10b21d56993c3c6bc0aa80dd4168911&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-164ff18d322608d7342cc1d0619c9f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 179}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 445}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLAGSTAR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Flagstar is a financial institution involved in mortgage lending and servicing, providing guidelines and policies related to mortgage transactions and power of attorney."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is a financial institution involved in purchasing mortgages made to natural persons, indicating its role in the mortgage industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is a financial institution that has discretion in determining loan occupancy status based on its current and/or best use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is a financial institution that has specific policies regarding escrow waivers and lending practices for various types of properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is a financial institution that offers a variety of mortgage products and services, including appraisal review and underwriting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is a financial institution that offers mortgage financing and has discretion over determining property classifications and occupancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is a financial institution that provides banking and mortgage services, with specific guidelines for underwriting and asset verification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is a financial institution that requires appraisals to be ordered in compliance with specific guidelines, particularly the Appraiser Independence Requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is a financial institution that reserves the right to request inspections or reports regarding environmental risks associated with properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is a lending institution involved in underwriting loans, specifically mentioned in the context of refinancing transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is an organization that will not approve loans with unexpired rights of redemption unless specific conditions are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flagstar is identified as an institution that requires evaluation of a borrower's credit history to determine eligibility for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3fe3f1cf3ad46c315af5250198974ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce8ebe270f2feee194ded8e3d4becdb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a05e768a9b64dd897dab3f97a6c234a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46cceddf672b67421d8f87a3665f1ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0ff713c7eebcf293485e860ba8cc6a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4de71275bc933c2c228984f601d0e0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNITED STATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The United States is the country where non-U.S. citizen borrowers must be legally present to obtain loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is the country whose regulations and standards influence the nontraditional credit requirements for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States is a location where account funds must be located in a regulated financial institution, emphasizing its regulatory relevance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46cceddf672b67421d8f87a3665f1ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-452a34dee684e3a93929cc44930deb38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 187}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 469}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GREEN CARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Green Card is a document that grants permanent resident status to immigrants in the United States, with specific guidelines for its documentation and renewal."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Green Card is an immigration document that indicates a non-U.S. citizen's permanent residency status in the United States."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46cceddf672b67421d8f87a3665f1ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3fe3f1cf3ad46c315af5250198974ab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 228}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VISA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A VISA is an official document allowing a non-U.S. citizen to enter or remain in the United States under specified conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A VISA is an official document that allows foreign nationals to enter, stay, or work in the United States under specified conditions, requiring compliance with legal documentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46cceddf672b67421d8f87a3665f1ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9f00ed91955a5d8af076ae0a21e6a69</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 227}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 528}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EAD CARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An EAD (Employment Authorization Document) Card grants work authorization to eligible non-citizens in the United States and is subject to expiration and renewal conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An EAD Card is an Employment Authorization Document that allows non-U.S. citizens to work in the United States."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46cceddf672b67421d8f87a3665f1ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9f00ed91955a5d8af076ae0a21e6a69</data>
