<node id="&quot;HPML&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HPML refers to Higher-Priced Mortgage Loans, which are subject to specific compliance procedures that exclude them from escrow waiver eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 356}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conventional Underwriting refers to the risk assessment process used by lenders in evaluating mortgage applications, which can include rental income considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting refers to the standard process used by lenders to evaluate loan applications and borrower's creditworthiness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7a01c4d224477788cf5c6bfd6ccc84e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 104}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 342}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN-TO-VALUE RATIO (LTV)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan-to-Value Ratio (LTV) is a financial term used by lenders to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, which impacts eligibility for escrow waivers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 356}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HAZARD INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hazard Insurance is a property insurance that covers damages to buildings and their contents, essential for mortgage underwriting according to specified requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hazard Insurance is a type of insurance that covers losses due to damages to property and is managed through the escrow account for some properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hazard insurance provides coverage for financial losses due to property damage or destruction, which is often a requirement for mortgage loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefb0ad4148eab93b794bfdc3eb3eac7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECOND HOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Second Home is a residential property that is not the primary residence of a borrower and has certain loan product conditions associated with it."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Second Home is defined as a property located a reasonable distance from the borrower's principal residence, meant for personal use and not available for rental purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Second Home is defined as a property that the borrower owns in addition to their principal residence, typically used for vacations or seasonal living."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home is an additional property owned by a borrower that is not their primary residence, eligible under certain lending criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to a property that is not the owner's primary residence and has specific mortgage qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to a property that is not the primary residence but is owned for leisure or investment purposes, and it has specific funding restrictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to a property that is not the primary residence but is used for leisure or vacation purposes and often subject to specific mortgage guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to a property that is not the primary residence of the borrower, which may have different escrow requirements under Flagstar Bank guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to a residential property that the borrower does not use as their primary residence, subject to different financial requirements than main residences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second home refers to an additional residence that a borrower owns and uses occasionally, distinct from their primary residence and assessed under specific conditions for lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3fe3f1cf3ad46c315af5250198974ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c392c46c8ab1fb7407628dd97c6f2c74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12708616563afb36a31ad3cf8523241b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0ff713c7eebcf293485e860ba8cc6a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-164ff18d322608d7342cc1d0619c9f0f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 307}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIAL ESCROW WAIVER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Partial Escrow Waiver is a specific type of request to waive escrow requirements only for certain types of insurance, as allowed by underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 356}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL ESTATE TAXES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORM_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Real Estate Taxes are taxes assessed on real property by local governments, which are typically managed through the borrower's escrow account."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate Taxes are taxes imposed on real property by the government, used to fund local services and infrastructure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 505}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLOSING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Closing is the final step in a real estate transaction where the property ownership is officially transferred to the buyer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing is the final step in a real estate transaction, wherein ownership of the property is transferred to the buyer after compliance with financing conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing is the final step in the mortgage process where the loan is officially completed and funds are disbursed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing refers to the final step in a property transaction where the ownership of the property is transferred to the buyer, subject to various escrow requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0ff713c7eebcf293485e860ba8cc6a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909c805f10bec3b9745cd64c1852b1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATORY LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulatory Law encompasses the rules and guidelines established by authorities that govern the conduct of lenders, including escrow provisions and waivers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b7e863cbccfa45dfb855f96b39c4e7be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 356}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Underwriting is the process of evaluating loan applications to determine risk and eligibility based on various financial and property-related factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting refers to the process of evaluating a borrower's creditworthiness and the property's value before approving a loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting refers to the process of evaluating the creditworthiness of a borrower and the risk of insuring or financing a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 357}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRUST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Trust is a fiduciary arrangement allowing a third party to hold assets on behalf of beneficiaries, which can be revocable or irrevocable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trust is a fiduciary arrangement allowing a third party to hold assets on behalf of beneficiaries, which can also serve as an acceptable donor of gift funds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trust refers to a fiduciary relationship where one party holds property for the benefit of another, governed by a trust document that outlines the terms of the trust."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trust refers to a legal arrangement where one party holds property for the benefit of another, affecting how a Power of Attorney may be utilized in mortgage transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fd7a30043bf2ff61e50fbd6141d212&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 212}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Properties refer to real estate assets being evaluated for value, including houses, parcels of land, and commercial buildings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Properties refer to real estate holdings that may be financed through mortgages, including primary residences and investment properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction refers to the process of building or renovating a property, which may involve specific financing considerations under various lending programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-OUT TRANSACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cash-out Transactions are instances where a borrower refinances or takes a loan resulting in cash being extracted from the property’s equity, impacting the terms of subordinate financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out Transactions involve taking out a new mortgage for more than what is owed on the property, allowing the borrower to access cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out Transactions refer to a financial process that allows borrowers to refinance their mortgage and take out extra funds based on equity, subject to approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out transactions are refinancing scenarios where a borrower takes out a new mortgage for more than the existing loan balance, receiving the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out transactions refer to a type of mortgage refinancing where a borrower takes out a new loan for more than they owe on their original loan, receiving the difference in cash."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOC. #5351&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Doc. #5351 refers to a specific document that outlines the guidelines and requirements for borrowers owning multiple financed properties under the Fannie Mae program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOC. #5719&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Doc. #5719 refers to a specific document detailing regulations for financing second homes and investment properties under the Homestyle Renovation program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOC. #5717&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Doc. #5717 outlines the guidelines for One-Close Construction loans, pertinent to borrowers looking to finance property development and purchase simultaneously."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137</data>
