<node id="&quot;FINANCED PROPERTIES LIMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financed Properties Limit refers to the maximum number of properties that a borrower can finance simultaneously under various mortgage programs, as imposed by lenders like Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7705559d232d0e6b4978eff8d1e8b137</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MILITARY SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Military Service refers to the duty of individuals serving in the armed forces, which affects their ability to be present during loan closing and allows for the use of a power of attorney in such cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 532}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE TRUST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Trust refers to a legal entity where property is held for the benefit of specific individuals, and under which a power of attorney may be employed if authorized by the trust agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELIGIBLE CIRCUMSTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Eligible Circumstance defines specific scenarios under which a Borrower may utilize a power of attorney, such as hardship or military deployment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PURCHASE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Purchase Agreement is a legal document that outlines the terms of a real estate transaction, which must be signed by all parties involved, including when utilizing a power of attorney."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 53}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ATTORNEY IN FACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Attorney in Fact is an individual designated to act on behalf of another in legal matters, particularly in transactions involving powers of attorney."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 61}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Loan is a financial product offered by banks or lending institutions that involves borrowing money, which must be repaid with interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Loan is a sum of money that is borrowed and expected to be paid back with interest, often used in the context of mortgage transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Loan is a sum of money that is borrowed and expected to be paid back with interest, which is central to the transaction processes discussed in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Loan is a sum of money that is borrowed, often subject to interest, and must be repaid according to agreed terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A loan is a sum of money borrowed by an individual or organization, generally to be paid back with interest over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"A loan is a sum of money borrowed that is expected to be paid back with interest, significant in the context of mortgages and refinancing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to borrowed funds that are expected to be paid back with interest, essential for purchasing real estate, with various types such as conventional and investment loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to the amount of money borrowed by the individual for purchasing property, subject to credit analysis and approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to the borrowed amount of money that the borrower must repay, which requires a thorough appraisal assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan represents a sum of money that is borrowed and is expected to be paid back with interest, often used for purchasing real estate or covering expenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ae330f51f478e78f1b91957f17dcdec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 273}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;E-SIGNED POA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"e-signed POA refers to a power of attorney document that is signed electronically, which is allowed by Freddie Mac under certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HARDSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hardship refers to specific circumstances that prevent the borrower from being present at the loan closing, thereby allowing the use of a power of attorney."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCE EMERGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Circumstance Emergency describes a situation that requires immediate attention or action, qualifying a borrower to utilize a power of attorney."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 53}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PURCHASE AND RATE-AND-TERM REFINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Purchase and Rate-and-Term Refinance describes specific types of loans that are eligible for the use of a power of attorney under Freddie Mac guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY MEMBER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Family Member is an individual related to the borrower who may serve as an agent in power of attorney transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family Member includes relatives such as parents, siblings, or children of the borrower, who may be involved as agents or in the legal aspects of the mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family member refers to an individual who is related by blood or marriage, eligible to act as an attorney-in-fact under Freddie Mac guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1cb7303f4ec7884e602c27628160dc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 61}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORGED SIGNATURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Forged Signatures refer to signatures that are falsified or unauthorized, which must match in the power of attorney and the loan file to meet legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 53}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOMINEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Nominee is a designated person who may act in a specific role, often occurring in financial transactions, and may be involved in power of attorney considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TITLE INSURANCE COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Title Insurance Company is a financial service organization that ensures the validity of title documents and may be involved in transactions where power of attorney is used."&lt;SEP&gt;"Title Insurance Company provides insurance that protects lenders and buyers against loss due to defects in a title to a property, crucial in mortgage transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 61}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Lender is a financial institution or entity that provides loans to borrowers, expecting payments over time including principal and interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lender is a financial institution or individual that provides financing for the purchase or refinancing of property, responsible for ensuring compliance with guidelines before loan sales."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lender is a financial institution that provides funds to borrowers for mortgages, requiring thorough documentation of income and assets for approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lender is a financial institution that provides loans to borrowers, evaluating their qualifications for loan transactions, including power of attorney use."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lender is an individual or institution that provides funds to borrowers, typically in the form of loans with agreed-upon repayment terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lender is an institution or person that provides funds to borrowers, expecting to be repaid with interest over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lender is an institution or individual that provides loans to borrowers, often associated with specific underwriting guidelines for mortgage transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lender refers to an institution or individual that provides funds to borrowers with the expectation of being repaid, typically with interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lender refers to any entity or organization that provides loans or financing to individuals or businesses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lender represents the financial institution or individual providing the financing for the lease or purchase of solar panels, involved in the DTI calculations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Lender is a financial institution or entity providing loans and is responsible for assessing the terms related to properties with solar panels in loan agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Lender is a financial institution or individual that provides funds to the borrower for the purpose of securing a mortgage or loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Lender is an institution or entity that provides mortgage loans, which must adhere to established underwriting guidelines when assessing borrower applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Lender is the financial institution that provides mortgage loans to borrowers, setting specific conditions and terms for repayment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lender is a financial institution or individual providing loans to borrowers, responsible for evaluating loan applications and compliance with mortgage guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0d9684317720eb42eaa206a9f3cc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76dfd0d1478f77acd572a51bf4e3956a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 276}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POWER OF ATTORNEY (POA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Power of Attorney is a legal document that allows one person to act on behalf of another in legal or financial matters, particularly in mortgage transactions as described in the document."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 61}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHORT SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Short Sale is a real estate transaction in which a property is sold for less than the balance remaining on the mortgage, requiring lender approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Short Sale is a mortgage resolution event where a property is sold for less than the mortgage amount, affecting future lending eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Short Sale is a process where a property is sold for less than the amount owed on its mortgage, typically to avoid foreclosure, and includes specific recovery timeframe considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Short Sale refers to a real estate transaction where a property is sold for less than the amount owed on the mortgage, requiring specific guidelines and procedures to handle fees and approvals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Short Sale refers to the sale of a property for less than the amount owed on the mortgage, requiring the lender's approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 476}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Assets are resources owned by a borrower that can be used to cover debts or investment purposes, critical in the evaluation of loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets encompass various financial resources, including stocks and mutual funds, that can be used to assess a borrower's financial standing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets in this context refer to the cash deposits and resources that a borrower must substantiate to complete a mortgage transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets in this context refer to the financial resources available to a borrower, which may include savings, investments, and properties that can be liquidated for cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets refer to any owned properties or resources that can be sold or liquidated to provide funds in home purchases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets refer to any resources owned that have economic value, which in the context of this document includes retirement accounts subjected to qualification requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets refer to resource items owned by borrowers that can be liquidated or used to satisfy financial requirements in a loan process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets refer to the financial resources that borrowers may use to qualify for loans, including funds in accounts and life insurance policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets refer to the properties or resources owned by the borrower, which can affect their financial evaluation during mortgage assessment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67964fc288da88f7bb3defef1f29177&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 290}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Closing Disclosure is a document that outlines the final details of the mortgage loan terms, including loan terms, monthly payments, and closing costs, which borrowers receive prior to closing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Disclosure is a crucial document in the real estate transaction process, detailing financial terms and costs associated with the loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Disclosure is a document that outlines all the final costs, fees, and terms in a real estate transaction before closing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Disclosure is a document that outlines the final details of a mortgage loan, including the loan terms, monthly payments, and closing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Disclosure is a document that outlines the terms of a mortgage, including the details of gift funds provided for the transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Disclosure is a document that provides details about the final terms of a mortgage loan, including all closing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Disclosure is a document that provides final details about a mortgage loan, including the loan terms, closing costs, and other essential information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Disclosure is a financial document provided to the borrower that outlines the final terms of the mortgage and any associated fees before closing the transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Disclosure is a standardized form that provides details on the mortgage loan terms, monthly payments, and closing costs to the borrower prior to finalizing the loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Closing Disclosure is a document that provides a detailed account of the financial transaction between the buyer and seller in real estate, including any gifts of equity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 457}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITING MANAGER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Underwriting Manager is responsible for approving the underwriting process for loans, ensuring compliance with standards and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Manager is a professional responsible for approving or denying mortgage applications based on the guidelines set forth by lending institutions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d77c56c7ef7f25742c687f6ad137c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 519}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOA FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HOA Fees are costs associated with Homeowners Associations, subject to certain conditions that classify their payment as abatement or contributions."&lt;SEP&gt;"HOA Fees are costs associated with homeownership in communities governed by a Homeowners Association, which cover maintenance and amenities."&lt;SEP&gt;"HOA Fees refer to Homeowners Association fees that cover maintenance and services in a community, which may affect the financial assessments for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 277}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Transaction refers to the overall process of buying, selling, or financing real estate, involving various financial elements and legal agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transaction here refers to the entire process of securing a mortgage or loan, which includes various fees, documentation, and approvals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transaction in this context refers to the process of exchanging a mortgage for a loan, including any refinancing-related activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transaction refers to any financial exchange between parties, particularly in the context of buying or refinancing property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL ESTATE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Real Estate Agent is a licensed professional who represents buyers or sellers in real estate transactions, providing guidance and support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate Agent is an individual licensed to negotiate and assist in the purchasing, selling, or leasing of properties, sometimes with a vested interest in the transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate Agent refers to a professional who assists in buying and selling properties, often linked to transaction-related employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate Agents are professionals who assist clients in buying, selling, or renting properties, providing expertise and guidance throughout the transaction process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATE LIEN HOLDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subordinate Lien Holder is a creditor holding a lien on a property that is below the senior lien in priority, often involved in short sale negotiations or fee payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;U.S. VESSEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"U.S. Vessel refers to a naval or military ship operated by the United States, indicating a context where certain transactions and processes involving the government or military may occur."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER’S SPOUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower’s Spouse is the individual who is related to the borrower through marriage and may have an interest in the mortgage transaction, capable of acting as an agent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 61}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOMESTIC PARTNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Domestic Partner is a person in a long-term committed relationship with the borrower, having similar rights and responsibilities concerning the mortgage transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Domestic Partner refers to an individual in a committed relationship with a borrower, defined for the purpose of qualifying for financial assistance in real estate transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 61}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TITLE POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Title Policy is an insurance document that assures the legality and validity of the title being transferred in a real estate transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHORT SALE PROCESSING FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Short Sale Processing Fees refers to the charges associated with the administration and negotiation of a short sale, which are to be disclosed to all parties involved in the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payments are the transactions made by borrowers to fulfill their financial obligations, which include amounts paid, outstanding balances, and historical payment behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payments denote the financial transactions made by the borrower or involved parties concerning various fees required during the mortgage transaction process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payments refer to amounts paid periodically to settle debts or contribute towards a loan or mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payments refer to the amounts paid periodically by a borrower towards the mortgage, influencing the overall cost and repayment terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payments refer to the amounts that borrowers are required to pay towards their mortgage, with specific requirements for timeliness impacting eligibility for programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 195}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 478}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Down Payment is an initial upfront portion of the total amount due on a purchase, typically expressed as a percentage of the purchase price."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Down Payment is an upfront payment made by the borrower at the closing of a real estate transaction, representing a portion of the purchase price."&lt;SEP&gt;"A down payment is a portion of the total purchase price that is paid upfront when securing a loan, contributing to reduced loan amounts and affecting mortgage terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A down payment is an initial payment made by a borrower towards the purchase price of a home, typically expressed as a percentage of the total cost."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment is an upfront payment made by the borrower toward the purchase price of the property, essential for loan approvals and transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment is the initial payment made when purchasing a property, typically a percentage of the purchase price, impacting overall financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment is the initial upfront payment made by a borrower to secure a mortgage, which is deducted from the total eligible assets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment is the initial upfront payment made when purchasing a home, usually expressed as a percentage of the total property price."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment is the portion of a purchase price that is paid upfront, with the rest financed through a mortgage loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment refers to the initial upfront amount paid by a buyer, influencing mortgage terms and financial agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment refers to the initial upfront portion of the total amount due, paid by the borrower when securing a mortgage to purchase property, impacting the LTV calculation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment refers to the initial upfront portion of the total amount that a borrower must pay when purchasing a manufactured home, which establishes equity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Down Payment is an upfront payment made by the borrower when purchasing a home, often a percentage of the total purchase price."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Down Payment is the initial amount of money that a borrower must pay upfront when purchasing a property, which directly affects loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Down Payment is the initial upfront portion of the total purchase price of a property, which must be paid by the borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Down Payment refers to the initial upfront portion of the purchase price paid by the buyer at the time of purchase, influencing mortgage terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d30aff8ce4b53c163b59f9369ea58842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc03d45e68c4df0463506aff2ba2a679&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67964fc288da88f7bb3defef1f29177&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32546641e2f2fec0a52f658ed70fc338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-164ff18d322608d7342cc1d0619c9f0f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 303}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELINQUENT TAXES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delinquent Taxes refer to unpaid taxes owed by the property owner, which can influence the mortgage approval process and short sale negotiations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 277}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN ORIGINATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Loan Originator is a professional who helps borrowers apply for and obtain mortgage loans, responsible for ensuring compliance with guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Originator refers to a professional who assists borrowers in the process of applying for loans and helps in closing transactions, often working for the lender."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Loan Originator is the individual or entity responsible for initiating the mortgage loan process on behalf of the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 351}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCURRENT FIRST LIEN MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Concurrent First Lien Mortgage represents the primary mortgage against a property that coexists with additional lien mortgages, such as home equity lines of credit (HELOC)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECONDARY LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Secondary Lien refers to a loan secured against a property that has already been encumbered by a primary mortgage, representing a lower priority in terms of claims against the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HELOC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Home Equity Line of Credit (HELOC) allows homeowners to borrow against the equity in their property, serving as a flexible credit option for various financial needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC stands for Home Equity Line of Credit, a revolving line of credit secured by the equity in a borrower's home."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC stands for Home Equity Line of Credit, which is a loan allowing homeowners to borrow against their home equity, often used in mortgage refinancing."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC, or Home Equity Line of Credit, is a financial product allowing borrowers to access funds based on the equity of their home, with associated monthly payment obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC, or Home Equity Line of Credit, is a type of loan where a homeowner borrows against the equity in their home, often used for flexible financing options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Home Equity Line of Credit (HELOC) is a financial product that allows borrowers to access funds secured by their home equity, often used for various financial needs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD-PARTY ASSET REPORTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third-Party Asset Reports are documentation provided by approved service providers to verify assets for mortgage qualifications, crucial in the underwriting process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BANK PRINTOUTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bank Printouts are official transaction histories provided by financial institutions to detail account activity, acceptable as part of the loan verification process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 187}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 468}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSET DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Asset Documentation is the collection of statements and proofs required to verify a borrower's financial assets during loan underwriting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Asset Documentation refers to the necessary paperwork that details a borrower's financial assets, used to verify their ability to secure a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 291}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VERIFICATION OF DEPOSIT FORM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Verification of Deposit Form is a document used to confirm a borrower's bank balances and account activities as part of the mortgage application process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 187}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 468}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY BANK STATEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Monthly Bank Statements are regular summaries provided by financial institutions detailing transactions, balances, and other account activity over a monthly period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 187}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 468}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUARTERLY STATEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Quarterly Statements are summaries of financial activity over a three-month period provided by institutions, often used to assess a borrower's financial status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 187}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 468}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VERIFICATION OF SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Verification of Source of Funds involves confirming the origin of finances presented by applicants in loan applications to ensure legitimacy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 291}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWED FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrowed Funds refer to money acquired through loans or credit sources that may influence a borrower's financial health during qualification assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowed Funds secured by assets can be utilized for loan qualification, reflecting the return on equity, which may include various forms of collateral."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIGNATURE REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Signature Requirements are the specific authentiation protocols that must be followed on documents involved in financial transactions to ensure legitimacy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL PORTFOLIO ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial Portfolio Accounts typically refer to accounts that manage investments across assets such as stocks, bonds, and other financial securities for investors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 247}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCOUNT BALANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Account Balance is the amount of money currently available in a financial account, reflecting deposits, withdrawals, and fees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT/CLOSING REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Settlement/Closing Requirements are procedures detailing the required signatures for various parties involved in a property transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Settlement/Closing Requirements are specific conditions and steps that must be fulfilled during the finalization of a real estate transaction to ensure proper transfer of ownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3fe3f1cf3ad46c315af5250198974ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Seller refers to an individual or entity that is selling real estate or property, engaging in transactions involving local real estate markets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Seller refers to the individual or entity that sells a property, often bearing certain costs during the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LARGE DEPOSIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Large Deposit usually refers to a significant sum of money placed into an account, which may raise questions regarding its source during the loan process."&lt;SEP&gt;"A large deposit is defined as a significant single deposit that surpasses a certain percentage of the total monthly qualifying income for the loan, requiring documentation to verify its source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Large Deposit refers to an unusually high amount of money deposited into a bank account, which may require additional scrutiny during the loan approval process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-164ff18d322608d7342cc1d0619c9f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 247}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrowers are defined as natural persons who apply for credit to qualify for loan eligibility, reflecting the social aspect of financial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals applying for a mortgage loan, often seeking guidance on homeownership education and counseling for better financial decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals or entities seeking loans, typically in real estate transactions, and must meet various financial criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals or entities that seek loans, in this context specifically referring to those obtaining mortgages for real estate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals or entities that seek to obtain money from a lender, typically in the form of a loan, for various purposes such as purchasing a home or funding a project."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals or entities who take out loans, such as Texas Home Equity loans, and must comply with specific eligibility requirements outlined in lending regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals seeking loans, whose employment history and income stability are assessed to qualify for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals seeking to purchase a home, utilizing various financial products and programs to facilitate their homeownership journey."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals who take out loans, needing to adhere to guidelines regarding tax identification and occupancy of their properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce8ebe270f2feee194ded8e3d4becdb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f066acdedf5a2cb0d5c7abb401d7c950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a05e768a9b64dd897dab3f97a6c234a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32546641e2f2fec0a52f658ed70fc338</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 494}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REQUIREMENTS FOR QUALIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Requirements for Qualification refer to the criteria that borrowers must meet to secure a loan, including financial documentation, credit history, and asset verification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 494}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCURRENTLY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Concurrently indicates actions or processes happening at the same time, often used in financial contexts to denote simultaneous transactions or agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OUTSTANDING LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Outstanding Loans are loans that have been issued but not yet fully repaid by the borrower, affecting their creditworthiness and financial evaluation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"POA stands for Power of Attorney, a legal document that grants one individual the authority to act for another, particularly in financial or legal matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"POA, or Power of Attorney, is a legal document that allows one individual to act on behalf of another in legal or financial matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cb7303f4ec7884e602c27628160dc28</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSET TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Asset Types are classifications of various forms of assets that can be considered for loan qualification, such as checking accounts, savings accounts, or investment accounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Asset Types in the context refer to various classifications of financial assets that can be used for down payment and closing costs during mortgage transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIGNATURE REQUIREMENTS FOR POA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Signature Requirements for POA detail the specific protocols to be followed to validate a Power of Attorney document for legal transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;U.S.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The U.S. is referenced as a location concerning various types of VISA classes and employment authorization documents (EADs)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. refers to the United States, where specific regulations and financial practices are applicable to its mortgage and financial systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7feb44cc17f2e0c5783ac3ce2285717a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 276}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VERIFICATION OF DEPOSIT FORM 1006 OR 1006(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Verification of Deposit Form 1006 or 1006(S) is a financial document used to verify the activity in a borrower's depository accounts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 301}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-ON-HAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cash-On-Hand indicates the physical currency held by the borrower, which is generally not accepted as a source of funds for mortgage transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 291}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business Assets refer to the assets owned by a business that can be used in the qualification process for securing a mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business assets are resources and properties owned by a business that can affect its financial health, crucial for verification in the mortgage process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LARGE DEPOSITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Large Deposits are defined as significant, unusual sum of money added to an account that may require evaluation in the context of mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VERIFICATION OF DEPOSIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Verification of Deposit is the process of confirming the financial activity and balance in a borrower's bank accounts, crucial for mortgage approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Internet is a global network that connects computers, allowing users to access and download information including online account and portfolio statements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Internet is a technological tool used by brokers to gather contact information and verify employment for the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec242ee203576a6a4b76efbe5458e782</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VERIFICATION OF DEPOSIT GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Verification of Deposit Guidelines encompass the rules and criteria used by lenders to assess a borrower’s financial accounts and verify their authenticity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 276}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCOUNT BALANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Account Balances refer to the current amount of money held in a financial account, which is relevant when determining a borrower’s financial status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS TAX RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business Tax Returns are official documents that report the income, profits, and expenses of a business, used in the financial assessment for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business tax returns are documents submitted to the IRS that report a business's income, expenses, and other financial information for tax purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business tax returns are financial statements that provide an overview of a business's income, expenses, and profitability, crucial for lender assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 255}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSONAL TAX RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Personal Tax Returns are official papers that report an individual's income and tax obligations, often reviewed by lenders during loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 255}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Financial Statement is a summary of the financial status of a borrower or business, including income, expenses, and assets, used for qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;P&amp;L STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A P&amp;L Statement, or Profit and Loss Statement, details a company's revenues, costs, and expenses over a specific period, aiding in financial assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDIVIDUAL DEVELOPMENT ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Individual Development Accounts (IDAs) are savings accounts designed to help borrowers accumulate funds for purchasing a home, often with matching contributions from nonprofit agencies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 496}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NONPROFIT AGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nonprofit agencies offer assistance by providing matching funds to borrowers' savings in individual development accounts, helping facilitate home purchases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 496}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIFE INSURANCE POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A life insurance policy is a financial product that can allow the policyholder to borrow against its cash value for financial needs such as closing costs in real estate transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 494}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SAVINGS FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Savings Funds are pooled savings arrangements that help individuals accumulate funds for significant purchases like homes, particularly for those without conventional banking access."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 495}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDING REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Funding requirements pertain to the stipulations and guidelines that need to be satisfied by borrowers to secure financial assistance for home purchases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 496}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LTV/CLTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LTV (Loan-to-Value) and CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) are financial ratios used by lenders to assess risk in lending, measuring the ratio of a loan to the value of the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV (Loan-to-Value) and CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) are financial ratios used to assess the risk of a borrower adjusting payments relative to their loan amounts and property value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-645973893eaf0e8d2eb4a7822c3fe6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 131}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POOLED SAVINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pooled savings refers to financial arrangements where multiple individuals contribute to a common fund, often utilized to achieve larger savings goals like home purchases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 495}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documentation Requirements are criteria that must be met to provide evidence of income or employment for the purposes of securing loans or financial products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements are the specific forms and types of proof needed to process financial requests or claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements are the specific papers and confirmations necessary for securing a mortgage, particularly relevant when dealing with temporary leaves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements encompass the necessary paperwork that borrowers must provide to verify their eligibility for employer assistance and loan programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements outline the necessary paperwork needed for verification of RSU income, including vesting schedules and payout evidence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements outline the necessary paperwork needed to secure a loan, essential for verifying ownership and loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements outline the necessary paperwork required to validate a borrower's eligibility for a mortgage, including financial histories and income calculations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements refer to the necessary evidence and statements needed to verify income for mortgage applications, particularly in terms of Social Security and royalties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements refer to the necessary paperwork that must be provided for verification in various legal and financial processes, particularly in loan underwriting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements refer to the specific criteria and records needed to substantiate claims for benefits or loan qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements refer to the specific financial and employment information that must be provided by the Borrower for loan qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements refer to the specific materials and forms needed to substantiate a borrower's income and eligibility for a loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements refer to the specific paperwork needed to substantiate a Borrower's employment and income for loan processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation requirements are necessary protocols that must be followed to verify financial transactions and compliance within the loan process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation requirements consist of the necessary paperwork that borrowers must provide to verify their eligibility and financial standing when applying for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation requirements refer to the specific papers needed to substantiate a borrower's claims and eligibility during the mortgage application process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d411e3f303846f3eb00356498af7761f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ed1a879d48c49b16f42ce89ae56d954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909c805f10bec3b9745cd64c1852b1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ae330f51f478e78f1b91957f17dcdec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14fb0d3aaa293edfdf71f855df5bd9ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VESTED BALANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Vested balance refers to the amount in an account that has become the property of the borrower and does not require repayment or restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 494}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POOLED SAVINGS ARRANGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pooled Savings Arrangement refers to a system where multiple individuals contribute to a collective fund to save for specific expenses, providing a disciplined way to accumulate funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETIREMENT ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Retirement Accounts are long-term savings accounts offered with tax advantages, which can also factor into asset calculations for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Retirement Accounts such as IRAs and 401(k)s can be utilized for loan qualification, providing tax advantages and potential funds for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 324}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STOCKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stocks are financial instruments that represent an ownership share in a company, providing potential dividends and capital gains, often featured in investment accounts like IRAs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stocks represent ownership in a corporation and can be liquidated or used as collateral for loans, depending on their vesting status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stocks represent ownership shares in a company, allowing investors to participate in its financial success and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stocks represent shares of ownership in a company and can be considered financial assets when used as collateral for loans or investments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stocks represent shares of ownership in companies and are included in the asset calculations for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bc03d45e68c4df0463506aff2ba2a679&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a9a7e59e34af57946c09cfa07672f92</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 90}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BONDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bonds are fixed income instruments used by borrowers to raise capital, which can also be considered in asset calculations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bonds are fixed-income securities that can also serve as a source of funds, depending on their maturity and vesting conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a9a7e59e34af57946c09cfa07672f92</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 90}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUTUAL FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mutual Funds are investment programs funded by shareholders that trade in diversified holdings, which are assessed in the mortgage asset evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutual Funds are investment vehicles that pool money from many investors to purchase a diversified portfolio of stocks, bonds, or other securities, commonly held in retirement accounts like IRAs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutual Funds are investment vehicles that pool money from multiple investors to purchase a diversified portfolio of stocks or bonds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutual Funds are investment vehicles that pool money from multiple investors to purchase securities, providing diversified exposure to stocks and bonds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bc03d45e68c4df0463506aff2ba2a679&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a9a7e59e34af57946c09cfa07672f92</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 90}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRUST ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Trust Accounts hold assets for the benefit of another person, and funds from such accounts can be eligible sources for loan qualification subject to verification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DU is an automated underwriting system that provides lenders with guidelines and requirements to streamline the mortgage qualification process."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU refers to Desktop Underwriter, a software system used by lenders to assess the risk of loan applicants based on credit information and underwriting guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU refers to Desktop Underwriter, a technology used for evaluating mortgage applications and verifying borrower income and employment information."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU, or Desktop Underwriter, is a technological tool used in the mortgage underwriting process to evaluate loan applications and determine eligibility based on automated underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2eef4940eec1ef97062f77d3efe4074e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LPA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LPA (Loan Product Advisor) is a tool used by lenders to evaluate mortgage loan options and assess borrower eligibility for different programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"LPA refers to Freddie Mac's Loan Product Advisor system, aimed at streamlining the loan application process through automated assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"LPA stands for Loan Product Advisor, a technology used in conjunction with DU for mortgage assessment and risk evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"LPA stands for Loan Product Advisor, a tool used by lenders to evaluate loan applications and streamline the underwriting process based on submitted documentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"LPA stands for Loan Product Advisor, a tool used for assessing mortgage applications and determining eligibility based on borrower information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial Assets encompass various forms of wealth, including savings accounts, stocks, bonds, and other investment vehicles that can be leveraged for loan qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial Assets encompass various instruments like stocks and bonds that can be used as collateral for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial Assets include various forms of value or monetary resources that can be liquidated, assessed during loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VESTED STOCK OPTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Vested Stock Options are employee benefits that provide the right to purchase company shares at a predetermined price and may be considered eligible for loan qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-VESTED RESTRICTED STOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-vested Restricted Stock refers to shares that are not yet owned outright by the employee and are not acceptable as a source of funds for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-vested restricted stock refers to company shares granted to employees that are not freely transferable until certain conditions are met, thus often ineligible for mortgage consideration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c392c46c8ab1fb7407628dd97c6f2c74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 89}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 320}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL ESTATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Real Estate encompasses the business of buying, selling, and managing properties, which includes diverse sectors like residential and commercial real estate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate encompasses the buying, selling, and leasing of land and buildings, representing a major sector in the economy connected to ownership and investment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate is an industry involving the buying, selling, and renting of land and properties, significant in economic transactions and income qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate is property consisting of land and the buildings on it, which can also serve as collateral for loans and affect borrower qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate is the sector of the economy that involves the buying, selling, and management of property, significantly impacting mortgage dealings and refinancing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate refers to property consisting of land and the buildings on it, significant in the context of loans and mortgage obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate refers to the industry involved in the buying, selling, and leasing of land and properties, including residential and commercial buildings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate refers to the property market context in which the solar panel agreements are evaluated, including financing and ownership structures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909c805f10bec3b9745cd64c1852b1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1955da1ebc911d30ff778d5b9e719028&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 414}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documentations refer to the necessary paperwork and records that must be provided to verify a borrower's financial status and loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 325}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WITHDRAWALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Withdrawals involve taking funds out of an account, and their conditions must be documented when qualifying a borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 325}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMALL BUSINESS ADMINISTRATION (SBA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Small Business Administration is a U.S. government agency that provides support to small businesses, including administering low-interest disaster relief loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 315}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEDERAL EMERGENCY MANAGEMENT AGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Federal Emergency Management Agency is a government agency that coordinates disaster response and provides assistance to those affected by natural disasters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 315}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRIDGE LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bridge loans are short-term loans secured by real estate properties, allowing borrowers to finance a new home purchase before selling their current home."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 415}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISASTER RELIEF GRANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disaster relief grants are financial aids provided to individuals affected by natural disasters to assist in immediate housing needs and repair costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 315}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISASTER RELIEF LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disaster relief loans are low-interest loans aimed at helping individuals recover from uninsured property losses due to natural disasters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 315}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER ASSISTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer Assistance refers to programs designed to support employees with down payments and closing costs associated with home purchases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employer assistance refers to financial support from an employer for down payments or closing costs associated with mortgage loans for employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 313}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT CARD FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Credit card financing allows borrowers to pay certain fees during the loan application process using their credit cards, impacting their debt-to-income ratio."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRIDGE OR SWING LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bridge or swing loans are short-term loans secured by a borrower's current home, allowing the use of proceeds for purchasing a new property before selling the existing one."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Monthly Payments refer to recurring amounts paid towards debts or obligations, essential for calculating debt responsibilities of borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monthly payments refer to the regular payments made towards a loan, which do not need to be categorized as long-term debt when qualifying a borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 415}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL RESERVES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial Reserves refer to additional savings that a borrower must have to cover unforeseen expenses after purchasing a home."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial Reserves refer to the funds needed to cover monthly liabilities, including mortgage payments, for a specific duration as required by underwriting guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial reserves are funds that a borrower must maintain to cover potential costs, including those associated with a mortgage application or loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f01d27887cb1edc56efdd9355e2cbba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 416}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN QUALIFICATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan qualification requirements are the criteria and documentation needed to assess a borrower's eligibility for a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 415}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraisal fees are costs incurred for estimating the value of a property, which may be charged to borrowers during the loan application process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 301}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Settlement Statement is a detailed document that outlines the final costs of a real estate transaction, including fees, commissions, and expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Settlement Statement is a document outlining the details of a real estate transaction, required for loan processing to prove the cash investment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Settlement Statement is a document that outlines the financial details of a real estate transaction, including the purchase price and financing information."&lt;SEP&gt;"A settlement statement is a document that outlines the financial details of a property transaction, including costs and proceeds related to closing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Settlement Statement is a document detailing the final terms of a real estate transaction, including costs and dates, essential for confirming property acquisition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Settlement Statement is a document that outlines the final details of a real estate transaction, including the purchase date of a property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Settlement Statement is a document that outlines the financial aspects of a property transaction, showing the breakdown of costs, proceeds, and related expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Settlement Statement is an official document detailing the final terms of a real estate transaction, including costs and fees, used to verify property acquisition."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Settlement Statement documents the details of a real estate transaction, providing necessary verification for appraisers regarding property sales."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d30aff8ce4b53c163b59f9369ea58842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10ce55972cf12e21fd77796ab69a96ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb02bde5abfff1b16d83434416df7465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 172}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 426}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIABILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Liabilities refer to the total amount of financial obligations a borrower has, which is critical in assessing their ability to secure a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 415}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Real Property is land and any structures attached to it, which must be legally classified as such for a manufactured home to be eligible for certain loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Property refers to land and any permanent structures affixed to it, significant in discussions about solar panel ownership and agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Property refers to land and any permanent structures on it, including homes and buildings, which can be impacted by the presence of solar panels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Property refers to land and anything permanently attached to it, which can encompass a wide variety of physical assets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Property refers to the legal definition of land and improvements on it, particularly as it pertains to taxes and appraisal of manufactured homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real property refers to land and any buildings or improvements on it, which serve as collateral for loans like mortgages and HELOCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real property refers to land and any structures attached to it, recognized under legal rights and regulations, and important in mortgage and leasing contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32546641e2f2fec0a52f658ed70fc338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb9a9047b04f55e775ab1675823f162</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SECONDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Seconds is a down payment assistance program provider that offers educational courses related to homeownership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds is a product that allows for secured second mortgages under specific eligibility criteria for home financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds refers to down payment assistance programs that support home buyers in acquiring necessary funding for their home purchases, often requiring associated educational courses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-AFFILIATED CREDIT UNION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer-Affiliated Credit Union is a financial institution associated with an employer that can provide assistance funds directly to employees for home purchases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 313}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE RELOCATION PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee Relocation Program is an initiative that supports employees who are moving for work-related reasons, including financial assistance for housing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee Relocation Programs are initiatives that assist employees in moving for work, affecting financial responsibilities for closing costs and payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 314}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNSECURED LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unsecured Loan refers to loans that do not require collateral and can be used for various expenses, including down payments for homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 313}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER CONTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower Contribution Requirements refer to the guidelines that determine the minimum financial contribution required from borrowers in a mortgage process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 313}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMUM BORROWER CONTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimum Borrower Contribution Requirements refer to the specified amount that borrowers must provide when applying for financial assistance in home buying."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 306}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEBT-TO-INCOME RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Debt-to-Income Ratio (DTI) measures an individual's monthly debt payments in relation to their monthly gross income, relevant in assessing financing for solar panel leases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial guideline assessing a borrower's ability to manage monthly payments and repay debts, crucial in the loan approval process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial measure that compares an individual's monthly debt payments to their monthly gross income to assess repayment capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial measure that compares an individual's total monthly debt payments to their gross monthly income, which lenders use to assess borrowing risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial measure used to evaluate an individual's ability to manage monthly debt payments relative to their income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial measure used to evaluate an individual's ability to manage monthly payments and repay debts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial metric used by lenders to evaluate a borrower's ability to repay a loan, comparing total monthly debt payments to gross monthly income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial metric used to assess a borrower's ability to manage monthly payments and repay debts, calculated as a percentage of total monthly debt payments against gross income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial metric used to measure the proportion of a borrower's income that goes toward paying debts, important for loan approvals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a measure used by lenders to evaluate a borrower's ability to manage monthly payments and repay debts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial metric used by lenders to measure a borrower's monthly debt payments against their gross monthly income, crucial for loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0610be8f2c48d2ab9263a9d9aea08a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61ba5485d92daa30adf4ee02bfab7d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 32}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER ASSISTANCE FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer Assistance Funds are monetary resources provided by employers to assist employees with down payments or closing costs for purchasing homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 307}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INVESTMENT PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Investment Property denotes a property purchased primarily for the purpose of generating rental income, as opposed to personal use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property is a property acquired primarily for rental income rather than as a primary residence, requiring specific documentation for mortgage qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property is a property acquired with the primary goal of generating rental income or for capital appreciation, which may have different funding criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property is a type of property purchase considered for generating income or profit, with specific eligibility restrictions for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property is a type of real estate owned with the intention of generating rental income, subject to certain financial guidelines and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property refers to a type of real estate bought primarily for generating rental income or holding for resale, with specific underwriting guidelines for financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property refers to real estate acquired with the intention of generating a return on investment, typically through rental income or resale."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property refers to real estate property that is purchased with the intention of earning a return on the investment, either through rental income or capital gain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property refers to real estate that is bought for generating rental income rather than for personal use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property refers to real estate that is purchased with the intent to earn income, rather than for personal use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment Property refers to real estate that is purchased with the intention of generating income, typically through rental income or appreciation in value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Investment property refers to real estate owned for generating rental income, which has specific requirements related to appraisals and financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3fe3f1cf3ad46c315af5250198974ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-164ff18d322608d7342cc1d0619c9f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10ce55972cf12e21fd77796ab69a96ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b454650a6e8dde5a93325db30813c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb02bde5abfff1b16d83434416df7465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 307}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECURED SECOND MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Secured Second Mortgage is a type of financing that requires collateral to secure the loan, typically the home itself, which may have specific eligibility criteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG-TERM DISABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Long-Term Disability is a condition that affects a person's ability to work for an extended period, influencing repayment conditions on employer-provided loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long-Term Disability refers to insurance policies that provide income support to individuals who are unable to work due to injury or illness for an extended period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1955da1ebc911d30ff778d5b9e719028</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 281}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REDUCTION-IN-FORCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reduction-in-Force refers to a process by which a company terminates a number of employees to cut costs, affecting employment contracts related to loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 281}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNSECURED LOAN TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unsecured Loan Terms specify the conditions of repayment and obligations associated with loans that do not require collateral."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 313}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER'S EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower's Employment refers to the status and conditions of employment that can affect eligibility for various loan programs and repayments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9e3a88db0855762e0cc4e584fc3462d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMALL BUSINESS ADMINISTRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Small Business Administration (SBA) is a U.S. government agency that provides support to small businesses through loans and grants, especially relevant during COVID-19."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Small Business Administration (SBA) is a government agency that provides support to small businesses, including loans secured by property that must be considered subordinate financing in loan calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COVID-19&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"COVID-19 refers to the global pandemic that has impacted businesses and introduced specific financial assistance programs like the SBA loans and grants."&lt;SEP&gt;"COVID-19 refers to the global pandemic that impacted mortgage payments, causing changes in how missed payments are treated."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 197}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMBINED LOAN-TO-VALUE RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Combined Loan-to-Value Ratio (CLTV) refers to a metric that calculates the ratio of all loans secured by a property against its value, important for assessing borrower eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 104}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 346}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCING CONCESSIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financing Concessions are financial contributions made by interested parties in a transaction to benefit borrowers and influence financing terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financing Concessions are payments or credits related to property acquisition or financing terms that can assist borrowers in managing their costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financing concessions are incentives provided by sellers to buyers, such as reduced interest rates or covering closing costs, impacting overall sales agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financing concessions refer to incentives provided to the buyer by the seller or lenders to facilitate the sale, affecting the transaction's financial terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 86}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES CONCESSIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Concessions are contributions provided by interested parties that, while beneficial to borrowers, are not integral to the financing transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sales Concessions refer to incentives offered by sellers to buyers, which can influence the perceived value of properties in real estate appraisals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sales Concessions refer to non-realty items or cash provided by sellers that must be accounted for in sale price calculations during underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 179}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 444}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREPAID FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Prepaid Fees refer to costs that borrowers must pay in advance in mortgage transactions, typically considered part of the closing costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 301}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERESTED PARTY CONTRIBUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interested Party Contributions (IPC) are funds or benefits provided by parties involved in real estate transactions that can assist the borrower but must adhere to certain limitations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 316}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSONAL UNSECURED LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Personal Unsecured Loans are loans given to individuals without requiring collateral, which are considered ineligibly as reserves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Personal Unsecured Loans are loans that are not backed by collateral and are excluded from the asset calculations for mortgage qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Personal Unsecured Loans are types of loans that do not require collateral, which are generally not accepted as sources of funds for mortgage transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a9a7e59e34af57946c09cfa07672f92</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 89}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 322}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT ASSISTANCE PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROGRAM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Down Payment Assistance Programs are initiatives that help homebuyers with funds for down payments, subject to specific eligibility and limitations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment Assistance Programs offer financial aid to first-time homebuyers, enabling them to cover part of their initial down payment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE RELOCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee Relocation refers to the process of moving employees to different locations for job-related purposes and involves specific financial considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 314}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Monthly Payment is a recurring payment made by a borrower to repay the loan amount, typically inclusive of principal and interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monthly Payment refers to the amount a borrower pays each month towards their mortgage or finance arrangement, crucial for calculating debt-to-income ratios in underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIGNATURE LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Signature Loans are personal loans that do not require collateral and are based on the borrower's creditworthiness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 89}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 322}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LINES OF CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lines of Credit are flexible loan options that allow borrowers to access funds up to a certain limit without having to apply for loans individually."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 89}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 322}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OVERDRAFT PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Overdraft Protection is a banking service that allows transactions to proceed even if the account balance is insufficient, effectively acting as short-term credit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 89}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 322}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY PURCHASER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Purchaser refers to the individual or entity that buys a property and assumes responsibility for related costs and fees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRIBUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contributions are financial inputs made by various parties in a real estate transaction to assist the borrower with costs associated with buying a property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 316}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAXIMUM CONTRIBUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum Contributions are defined limits on the amount that can be contributed by interested parties towards closing costs in real estate transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 316}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTED PROCEEDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documented Proceeds refer to verified funds received from financial assistance programs that can influence loan eligibility and assets assessment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS STABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business Stability refers to the financial health and sustainability of a business, particularly relevant in assessments of loan qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACQUISITION FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Acquisition Fees are costs incurred during the purchase or acquisition of assets, including properties in real estate transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 301}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMEPATH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HomePath refers to properties owned by Fannie Mae that can be purchased with special financing options."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa</data>
