<node id="&quot;ESCROW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Escrow is a financial arrangement where a third party holds funds during a transaction until certain conditions are met between the buyer and seller."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow refers to a financial arrangement where a third party holds funds or assets until certain conditions are met, commonly used in real estate transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow refers to a financial arrangement where a third party temporarily holds funds or assets until certain conditions are met, often used in property transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-00440a55cc64896de959c80a8727fbfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32546641e2f2fec0a52f658ed70fc338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21</data>
