<node id="&quot;GIFT FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gift Funds are monetary contributions provided by donors to borrowers to assist with down payments or other home purchasing costs, subject to certain eligibility criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift Funds refer to financial contributions that can be used for down payments or closing costs in real estate transactions, subject to certain eligibility requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift Funds refer to money given to a borrower to help with the purchase of a home, subject to specific guidelines and donor verification during loan application."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift funds refer to monetary contributions given to borrowers by acceptable donors, which can be used for down payments under specific conditions in mortgage transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-164ff18d322608d7342cc1d0619c9f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 82}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 311}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMUM BORROWER CONTRIBUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimum Borrower Contribution is a specific percentage of the total cost that a borrower must provide from their own funds before utilizing other financial assistance or gift funds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minimum Borrower Contribution signifies the least amount of personal funds a borrower must provide when obtaining financing for purchasing a property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 82}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 311}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPAL RESIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Principal Residence refers to the primary home where a borrower resides and is eligible for specific mortgage programs and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence is a term describing a dwelling that a borrower occupies as their primary home, impacting mortgage eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence is defined as the main home where the borrower resides, which is a critical factor in financing and eligibility for gift funds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence is the main home where a borrower resides, which can impact the approval and terms of mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence is the main home where a person resides, often used in financial calculations and mortgage evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence is the main home where an individual resides, which plays a crucial role in mortgage eligibility and loan conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence is the primary home owned by an individual, often influencing loan qualifications and rental income considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence is the primary home where a borrower lives, which may be converted to an investment property for income generation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence is the primary home where an individual resides, which may influence mortgage terms and eligibility in lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence is the primary home where the borrower resides and is subject to specific loan eligibility requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence refers to a primary home where the borrower occupies the property within a specific timeframe after closing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence refers to the main dwelling that a borrower occupies, which can be converted to an investment property under Freddie Mac guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence refers to the primary home in which a borrower lives and is a key factor in eligibility for certain loan products, especially after derogatory events."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence refers to the primary home where the borrower lives, impacting the eligibility for certain mortgage conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Residence refers to the residential property that a borrower occupies as their main home."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal residence refers to the primary home where a borrower lives, which is relevant to underwriting requirements for mortgage loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10ce55972cf12e21fd77796ab69a96ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce8ebe270f2feee194ded8e3d4becdb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c392c46c8ab1fb7407628dd97c6f2c74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb02bde5abfff1b16d83434416df7465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0ff713c7eebcf293485e860ba8cc6a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a01c4d224477788cf5c6bfd6ccc84e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 377}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Relative is any individual related to the borrower by blood, marriage, adoption, or legal guardianship, often eligible to provide gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INELIGIBLE DONORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ineligible Donors are individuals or entities that cannot contribute gift funds due to their affiliations with the real estate transaction, such as builders or agents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GODPARENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Godparent refers to a person who has a special relationship with the borrower's family, sometimes considered eligible as a donor for gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ESTATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Estate is a legal entity that may hold assets and is sometimes involved in financial transactions, including the provision of gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Verification of Deposit (VOD) is a process used to confirm the amount of money in a borrower's bank account, often necessary for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CANCELED CHECK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Canceled Check refers to a check that has been processed and returned to the account holder, serving as proof of funds for lenders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GIFT LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Gift Letter is a document signed by the donor that specifies the details of the gift being provided to the borrower, including the amount and any obligations regarding repayment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift Letter is a document provided by the donor to the borrower, confirming that the funds given are a gift and do not need to be repaid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift Letter is a document that specifies the details of a gift being provided to a borrower for down payment purposes, including donor information and intent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift Letter is a formal document provided by a donor detailing the conditions and intentions behind the gift made to the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 458}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GIFT TOLERANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gift Tolerance indicates the parameters within which gift funds can be utilized, including the allowable percentage of the down payment that can consist of gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPREHENSIVE UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comprehensive Underwriting Guidelines encompass the set of criteria and standards that lenders use to evaluate a borrower's eligibility for a mortgage, including criteria for gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb8af4ec267d0a18313280fdbe45469d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GIFT OF EQUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gift of Equity refers to a financial arrangement in which a portion of the seller's equity in a property is transferred to the buyer as a credit in the transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift of Equity refers to a financial arrangement where a seller allows a buyer to use the equity in a property as part of a down payment, often seen in family transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift of Equity refers to a situation where the seller of a property gifts part of the equity to the buyer, assisting with the purchase without requiring repayment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift of equity refers to a financial arrangement where a property owner helps a buyer by offering part of a property's equity, affecting mortgage evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4de71275bc933c2c228984f601d0e0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 459}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SECONDS PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROGRAM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Seconds Program is a down payment assistance program designed to help low- and moderate-income borrowers access affordable housing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Community Seconds Program is a specific initiative under Freddie Mac's guidelines that provides down payment assistance through various gifts and grants."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 451}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ESTATE OR TRUST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Estates or trusts are legal entities established by individuals to manage their assets and provide for beneficiaries, relevant in the context of gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 212}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DONOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Donor is an individual or entity providing financial assistance, typically in the context of gifts or contributions for housing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Donor is an individual who provides gift funds to the borrower, with specific eligibility requirements related to their residency and financial standing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The donor is an individual or entity providing a financial gift to the borrower, whose relationship to the borrower must be documented."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 458}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ZELLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Zelle is a third-party money transfer application that allows users to transfer money electronically between bank accounts, as mentioned in the context of acceptable transfer methods for gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRUSTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Trustee is an individual or entity that manages the assets held in a trust and acts in accordance with the trust document's provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The trustee is an authorized representative of an estate or trust who is responsible for managing the trust's assets and must sign the gift letter for its validity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9fd7a30043bf2ff61e50fbd6141d212&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 212}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECIPIENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The recipient refers to the individual who is on the receiving end of the gift funds, essentially the borrower in the context of a real estate transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 459}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUNICIPALITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Municipalities are local government entities that may also act as eligible donors in financial transactions related to gifts for down payment assistance programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Municipalities include various levels of local government, such as state, county, and local housing agencies that administer government-sponsored subsidy programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Municipalities refer to local government entities that may provide funding or resources for housing assistance programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 451}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NONPROFIT ORGANIZATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nonprofit Organizations are entities that operate for a purpose other than making a profit, often providing services and support in areas like housing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nonprofit Organizations are entities that operate for charitable purposes and may offer support or grants for housing assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nonprofit organizations are entities that operate for charitable purposes and are considered acceptable donors for gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 458}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT UNIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Credit Unions are not-for-profit financial cooperatives that may offer loans and services to their members, including assistance with home purchases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit unions are member-owned financial cooperatives that provide various financial services and are excluded as acceptable entities in this context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 458}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC AGENCIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Agencies are government bodies that may facilitate housing programs or provide financial assistance to help residents secure homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public agencies are government-related organizations that may also act as acceptable donors in accordance with real estate assistance programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 458}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Document Guidelines refer to the regulations and requirements that outline the necessary documentation for verifying the legitimacy of gift funds and their transfer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 187}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 469}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GIFT/GRANT PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROGRAM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gift/Grant Programs provide financial assistance for down payments, aimed at helping individuals secure housing through gifts or grants."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Builder is a person or company responsible for constructing homes or commercial properties, which may affect financial transactions and agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Builder refers to companies or individuals involved in the construction of residential properties, playing a key role in the real estate market."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e252311920cec13b843fb034a4a69e94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EARNEST MONEY DEPOSIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL TERM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Earnest Money Deposit is a sum of money that demonstrates a buyer's commitment to purchasing a property, often held in escrow."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSFER OF FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transfer of Funds refers to the process of moving money from one account to another, often crucial in real estate transactions for earnest money deposits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEPOSIT HOLDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Deposit Holder refers to the entity or individual responsible for holding the earnest money deposit until the closing of the property transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ESCROW AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Escrow Agent is a neutral third party responsible for managing the transfer of funds and documents in a property transaction until all conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 457}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHURCHES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Churches are religious institutions that may provide support or financial assistance to individuals, particularly in the context of donations for housing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Churches serve as potential Eligible Subsidy Providers, contributing to affordable housing initiatives by offering financial assistance and support."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EARNEST MONEY DEPOSIT HOLDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Earnest Money Deposit Holder is the individual or entity that receives and holds the earnest money deposit during a real estate transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DONOR'S FINANCIAL INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Donor's Financial Institution is the bank or financial entity where the donor's funds are held, which may be involved in verifying the source of gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 458}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER'S ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower's Account refers to the financial account held by the borrower where funds are deposited or transferred in relation to a real estate transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrower's Account refers to the financial record related to the borrower's personal income and liabilities, relevant for evaluating mortgage eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 187}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 469}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ESCROW OR TITLE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Escrow or Title Agent is a professional involved in real estate transactions that ensures proper handling of documents and funds till closing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPY OF DONOR'S CHECK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Copy of Donor's Check is a document that serves as proof of funds gifted to the borrower, crucial for transactions involving gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER’S DEPOSIT SLIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower’s Deposit Slip is a document that shows the transaction details of a deposit made into the borrower's account."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WIRE TRANSFER CONFIRMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wire Transfer Confirmation is a document that verifies that funds were electronically transferred from the donor to the borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wire Transfer Confirmation serves as proof of an electronic transfer of funds to be used in real estate transactions or gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 457}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATION FROM THE DONOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Certification from the Donor is a written statement confirming the donor's relationship with the borrower and their intent to provide financial support."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHARED RESIDENCY DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Shared Residency Documents are evidence that the borrower and donor have lived together, needed to establish the legitimacy of pooled funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDS VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Funds Verification is the process of confirming that the funds in the donor's account are sufficient and legitimate for the gift provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GIFT OF FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL TERM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gift of Funds refers to financial support given to the borrower, which can be used towards the down payment for a home, typically not requiring repayment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Settlement Agent is a third party responsible for managing the closing process in real estate transactions, ensuring proper transfer of funds and documentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 82}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 312}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIMARY RESIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Primary Residence indicates the type of property that qualifies for a mortgage under the guidelines set by the organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence is defined as the dwelling where the borrower lives most of the time and serves as the basis for certain loan requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence is the living space where a person resides most of the time and is often a key factor in determining mortgage eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence refers to the main dwelling where a borrower lives, which is significant in the context of mortgage refinancing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence refers to the main dwelling where an individual lives, necessary for certain mortgage qualification criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence refers to the main dwelling where an individual or family lives, which is often a criterion in mortgage lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence refers to the main home of the borrower, where specific eligibility rules apply for receiving gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909c805f10bec3b9745cd64c1852b1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-164ff18d322608d7342cc1d0619c9f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2eef4940eec1ef97062f77d3efe4074e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 274}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELECTRONIC TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Electronic Transfer refers to the digital method of transferring funds which may include checks or wire transfers used in the context of financial transactions involving gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 82}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 312}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESIDENCY HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Residency History refers to the documented evidence of shared living arrangements between the borrower and donor, establishing eligibility for receiving gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 376}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPORTING DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Supporting Documentation includes various forms of evidence required in the process, such as marriage licenses or educational transcripts to validate claims for gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POOLED FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pooled Funds refer to a combination of gift funds from the donor and the borrower's personal funds used to meet down payment requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 82}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 311}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES PROCEEDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Proceeds represent the financial gains anticipated from the sale of a property, which can influence the borrower’s financial eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sales proceeds are the money obtained from the transaction of selling a business or property, vital for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
