<node id="&quot;HOME FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Home Financing refers to the financial mechanisms and practices employed to facilitate the purchase of residential properties, encompassing loans, mortgages, and other forms of funding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 273}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Underwriter is a financial professional responsible for evaluating a borrower's application and supporting documents to assess risk and determine eligibility for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Underwriter is a financial professional responsible for evaluating loan applications, verifying income, and ensuring that guidelines are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Underwriter is a financial professional who assesses the borrower's application, ensuring all documentation meets the lender's guidelines for loan approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Underwriter is responsible for evaluating mortgage applications and determining the risk associated with significant derogatory credit events."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Underwriter is responsible for evaluating the financial risk of a borrower and determining loan eligibility based on income and business stability."&lt;SEP&gt;"The underwriter is the individual responsible for evaluating a borrower's financial information and the eligibility of their mortgage application."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriter is a financial professional who assesses risk and determines eligibility for loan applications based on various financial documents and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriter is a professional responsible for evaluating and deciding on loan applications based on financial information and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriter is a professional responsible for evaluating mortgage applications and ensuring compliance with guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriter refers to a professional responsible for evaluating and deciding on mortgage applications, ensuring compliance with guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f01d27887cb1edc56efdd9355e2cbba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf6a394b54c040882b94d8dd97b886e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909c805f10bec3b9745cd64c1852b1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6843059eea11d10d23493c39af4afd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14fb0d3aaa293edfdf71f855df5bd9ce</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 283}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income refers to the earnings that a borrower receives, which must meet specific criteria to qualify for a mortgage loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income refers to the financial earnings received by individuals, including RSU payouts, which can influence borrowing capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income refers to the financial gain or profit received from various sources, essential in the context of mortgage qualification and borrower assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income refers to the money received by an individual or organization, typically from work, investments, or business operations, crucial for financial assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income refers to the money that a borrower earns from various sources, which is critically assessed to determine their ability to repay a loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income represents the earnings of the borrower that are considered during loan qualification, subject to verification and documentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income represents the financial earnings received by individuals, from various sources like employment, benefits, or investments, influencing their eligibility for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec242ee203576a6a4b76efbe5458e782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ed1a879d48c49b16f42ce89ae56d954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2eef4940eec1ef97062f77d3efe4074e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 174}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPAL BALANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Principal Balance is the remaining amount of money that a borrower owes on a loan not including interest and fees, relevant in refinancing scenarios."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Balance refers to the amount of money still owed on a loan, excluding interest, which is significant in calculating repayment obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 436}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCED PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financed Properties refer to real estate holdings that have been purchased with the help of loans, affecting the financial assessments and requirements for additional borrowing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financed Properties refer to real estate properties that have been purchased through a mortgage loan or any other form of financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 310}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER’S ACCOUNT BALANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
