<node id="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Credit Report is a detailed report of an individual's credit history used to assess eligibility for financing, including solar panel loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Credit Report is a detailed statement of an individual's credit history prepared by a credit reporting agency, which includes information about accounts, inquiries, and payment history."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Credit Report provides a comprehensive view of a borrower's credit history and score, essential for underwriting decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A credit report is a detailed report of an individual's credit history used by lenders to assess creditworthiness in the mortgage process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Report is a detailed report of an individual's credit history, used by lenders to assess creditworthiness of potential borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Report is a detailed report of an individual's credit history, used by lenders to assess creditworthiness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Report is a detailed report of an individual's credit history, which is essential for assessment by lenders during the underwriting process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 471}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN CASEFILES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Casefiles are the compiled documentation and data associated with a loan application, used to determine eligibility and risk."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMBINATION OF RECENT NON-MEDICAL COLLECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Combination of Recent Non-Medical Collections refers to accumulated unpaid debts that can negatively influence a borrower's credit score."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIONAL CREDIT BUREAUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"National Credit Bureaus are agencies that collect and maintain consumer credit information used for evaluating creditworthiness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCEPTABLE AUS FINDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Acceptable AUS Findings denote results from the Automated Underwriting System that indicate a borrower's creditworthiness is sufficient for loan approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEAVY LATE PAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Heavy Late Pays refer to a pattern of delayed payments on credit accounts that adversely affects credit scores."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHRONIC PATTERN OF CHARGE-OFFS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chronic Pattern of Charge-Offs refers to a repeated occurrence of debts being written off as a loss by creditors, impacting credit evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 471}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAGE 27&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Page 27 discusses specific guidelines and calculations regarding credit scores and eligibility assessments for loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TWO SCORES OBTAINED FOR A BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Two Scores Obtained for a Borrower refers to the scenario where two different credit scores are assessed for loan qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER 1 SCORES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower 1 Scores are the specific credit scores attributed to one individual borrower during the application process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPRESENTATIVE SCORE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Representative Score is the lowest score among the various credit scores from which eligibility decisions for loans are derived."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AVERAGE MEDIAN SCORE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Average Median Score represents the mean of credit scores calculated for borrowers to assess loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER 2 SCORES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower 2 Scores are the specific credit scores attributed to a second individual borrower during the application process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMUM SCORE REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimum Score Requirement outlines the lowest acceptable credit score that borrowers must achieve to qualify for a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 194}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN LEVEL PRICING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Level Pricing pertains to the pricing adjustment applied to certain loans based on the credit risk associated with the borrower's score."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VALID CREDIT SCORE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Valid Credit Score is a score that meets the lender's minimum requirements for loan application approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Valid Credit Score refers to a numerical expression based on the analysis of a borrower's credit files that is used to represent their creditworthiness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9480c322229448ccd0b724ce848cac14</data>
