</node>
<node id="&quot;LPA ACCEPT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LPA Accept is an automated underwriting system employed by lenders to provide decisions on mortgage applications, similar to DU."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 104}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 345}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONFORMING LOAN LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conforming Loan Limits refer to the maximum loan amounts that can be acquired through government-backed financing standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH BALANCE LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High Balance Loans refer to mortgage loans that exceed conforming loan limits and are subject to more stringent eligibility standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOUSING-RELATED NONTRADITIONAL CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Housing-Related Nontraditional Credit includes alternative credit histories related to housing payments, such as rent, utilized for loan eligibility assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment History is a record of a borrower's payment behavior, crucial for assessing creditworthiness and eligibility for loans, even if lacking a traditional credit score."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payment History is a record of the borrower’s payments on debts, critical for evaluating their creditworthiness in the underwriting process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 199}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENTAL HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rental History is assessed to evaluate a borrower's past payment behavior, influencing mortgage qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental History is the record of rental income and expenses over a specific period, which can impact mortgage qualification, especially if partial or no history is available."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental History refers to the documentation of a borrower's previous rental payments, which can be used to establish creditworthiness for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10ce55972cf12e21fd77796ab69a96ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 22}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT SOURCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Credit Sources are the references or types of credit accounts a borrower must provide to demonstrate their creditworthiness, especially in absence of a traditional credit score."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 22}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Credit History comprises the record of an individual's borrowing and repayment activity, affecting their credit score and eligibility for future loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit History is a detailed account of a borrower's borrowing and repayment activities, reflecting their ability to manage debt responsibly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 276}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Eligibility Requirements are the conditions set forth by lending institutions that must be met for borrowers to qualify for loans, particularly after derogatory events."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Requirements are the conditions that must be met to qualify for a loan, often including credit score, income verification, and residency status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Requirements are the criteria that Borrowers must meet to qualify for a mortgage, affecting their financial decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Requirements encompass the criteria that must be met for a mortgage to be approved, including employment history and income verification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Requirements outline the criteria borrowers must meet to qualify for mortgage funding, specifically regarding payment history and resolutions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Requirements refer to the conditions that must be met for borrowers regarding their mortgage status and payment history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Requirements refer to the specific criteria borrowers must meet to be considered for a loan, including citizenship and residency status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-452a34dee684e3a93929cc44930deb38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f01d27887cb1edc56efdd9355e2cbba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ae330f51f478e78f1b91957f17dcdec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 272}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SATISFACTORY PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">("CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Satisfactory Payment History denotes an individual's record of making payments on time, essential for establishing trust with lenders, particularly when traditional credit scores are absent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 22}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Lease is a contract outlining the terms under which one party agrees to rent property owned by another party, containing provisions for rights and obligations of both lessor and lessee."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lease is a contractual agreement that allows one party to use another party's solar panels in exchange for specific terms, affecting loan assessments and financial ratios."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lease is a legal agreement between a lessor and lessee highlighting the terms governing the use and rental of a property, essential for rental relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lease is a legal agreement outlining the terms under which one party agrees to rent property owned by another party, specifically relevant for determining net rental income associated with ADUs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Lease is a legal contract that grants a tenant the right to occupy and use a property for a specified period in exchange for rent."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lease is a legal agreement allowing one party to use property owned by another party, often involving regular payments over a specified period."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lease is a legal document outlining the terms under which one party agrees to rent property owned by another party, critical for supporting income claims related to rental properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 358}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"VOR, or Verification of Rent, is a method used by lenders to confirm a borrower's rental payment history as part of the loan approval process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 358}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITY PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Utility Payment refers to the bills paid for services like electricity, water, or gas, which can be considered as part of a nontraditional credit history."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCOUNT NUMBER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Account Number is a unique identifier assigned to a financial account, used by lenders to track a borrower's financial obligations and history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Account Number is a unique identifier assigned to individual borrower's accounts, essential for tracking payment history and account details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
