</node>
<node id="&quot;NATURE OF OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nature of Obligation refers to the specific type of debt a borrower is responsible for, such as mortgage, rent, or utilities, which lenders assess when evaluating creditworthiness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 417}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OUTSTANDING BALANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Outstanding Balance is the amount of money that is still owed on a loan or account, critical for assessing a borrower's financial responsibility in loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Outstanding Balance refers to the remaining amount of money owed on a loan or mortgage that has not yet been repaid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Outstanding Balance refers to the remaining amount owed on a financial obligation, crucial for calculating debt obligations in loans and credit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 417}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH BALANCE LOAN ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High Balance Loan Eligibility refers to the specific criteria required for loans that exceed the typical conforming loan limits, which often have stricter requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTIVE MILITARY ALERTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Active Military Alerts are notifications on credit reports indicating that an individual is serving in the military, which may affect their financial obligations and responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 350}]</data>
