<node id="&quot;EXTENDED FRAUD ALERTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Extended Fraud Alerts are notices on credit reports that indicate an individual may be a victim of identity theft, prompting lenders to take extra precautions before approving credit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 350}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT INQUIRIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Credit Inquiries are formal requests made by lenders or creditors to access an individual's credit report, which may affect the individual’s credit score based on recent activity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 473}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDITOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Creditor is a person or institution that extends credit or loaned money to borrowers, relying on their financial documentation for approval processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 534}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUDGEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Judgements are legal decisions that may affect a borrower's credit history, indicating financial obligations that must be settled to secure loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 474}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COLLECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Collections are attempts by creditors to recover amounts owed by borrowers, influencing the borrower's creditworthiness and loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Collections refer to overdue accounts that have been sent to a collection agency, impacting the borrower's financial standing when applying for a mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
