  <data key="d2">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOSS MITIGATION PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROGRAM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loss Mitigation Program refers to strategies that help borrowers prevent foreclosure, emphasizing the need for timely payments during trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss Mitigation Program refers to various strategies used by lenders to help borrowers avoid foreclosure, including repayment plans and payment deferrals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 195}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 480}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIGNIFICANT DEROGATORY CREDIT EVENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Significant Derogatory Credit Events encompass severe financial issues like bankruptcy, foreclosure, and short sales that heighten the risk of default on loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 476}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRIAL PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Trial Period refers to a defined timeframe during which a borrower must adhere to specific payment conditions to qualify for loan modifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trial Period refers to a designated timeframe within which borrowers must demonstrate timely payment on modified loan terms to qualify for a long-term resolution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 195}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 478}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT DEFERRAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Deferral is a temporary postponement of mortgage payments, requiring documentation of consecutive timely payments to establish eligibility for refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 195}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 480}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE REFINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Refinancing is the process of obtaining a new mortgage to replace an existing one, often to take advantage of lower interest rates or to change loan terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Refinancing is the process of paying off an existing loan with a new loan that usually has different terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Refinancing is the process of replacing an existing mortgage with a new one, often to achieve better terms or rates, requiring strict adherence to eligibility guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 190}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTED RESOLUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documented Resolution refers to the proof of actions taken to address overdue payments in mortgage settings, which is critical for loan approval processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 272}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;3-MONTH REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"3-Month Requirement is a stipulation within the underwriting guidelines that mandates timely payments for a consecutive three-month period to satisfy certain eligibility criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"3-Month Requirement refers to the stipulated period in which specific conditions, like payment history, must be documented for mortgage refinances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 195}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 478}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIMELY PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Timely Payments refer to payments made on schedule, often crucial for qualifying for loans and other financial products."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 195}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 479}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEROGATORY EVENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Derogatory Events are negative marks on a credit report that can adversely affect a borrower's credit score and loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 471}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAITING PERIODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Waiting Periods are designated durations that borrowers must wait after a derogatory event before they can qualify for new loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Waiting Periods are specified durations that must be completed after certain derogatory events before a borrower can qualify for new loans or mortgages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LUMP SUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lump Sum refers to a single large payment made at one time, rather than through installments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 195}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 478}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODIFICATION PLAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROGRAM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Modification Plan is a program designed to alter the terms of a loan to make it more affordable for the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 195}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 479}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHAPTER 7 OR 11&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chapter 7 or 11 refers to specific types of bankruptcy filings under U.S. bankruptcy law, each with defined waiting periods for recovery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHAPTER 13&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chapter 13 refers to a type of bankruptcy that involves a repayment plan for individuals with a regular income, which also has specific waiting periods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEED-IN-LIEU OF FORECLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Deed-In-Lieu of Foreclosure is a legal process allowing borrowers to transfer ownership of their property back to the lender to avoid foreclosure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deed-In-Lieu of Foreclosure is an arrangement where the borrower voluntarily transfers the property title to the lender to avoid foreclosure, with defined recovery timelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deed-in-Lieu of Foreclosure is a legal process where a borrower voluntarily gives up their property to the lender to avoid foreclosure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deed-in-Lieu of Foreclosure is a legal process where a borrower voluntarily transfers the title of their property to the lender to avoid foreclosure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deed-in-Lieu of Foreclosure is a procedure where a borrower voluntarily conveys property title to the lender to avoid foreclosure proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deed-in-lieu of Foreclosure is a legal agreement where a borrower voluntarily conveys the title of the property to the lender to avoid the foreclosure process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 475}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHARGE-OFF OF MORTGAGE ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Charge-off of a mortgage account refers to the lender's declaration that the mortgage debt is unlikely to be collected, impacting the borrower's credit status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 475}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INACCURATE DEROGATORY CREDIT EVENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Inaccurate Derogatory Credit Events refer to potentially erroneous reports of negative credit incidents, like bankruptcy or foreclosure, that can affect eligibility assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MULTIPLE BANKRUPTCY FILINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Multiple Bankruptcy Filings refer to instances where a borrower has filed for bankruptcy more than once, which impacts recovery timelines based on the most recent discharge or dismissal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARD RECOVERY TIME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Standard Recovery Time is the predetermined period that must elapse following certain derogatory credit events before a borrower can be considered for new loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additional Requirements are stipulations that accompany the eligibility criteria for loans, affecting how various events are handled in underwriting processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 272}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAXIMUM LTV, CLTV, OR HCLTV RATIOS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum LTV, CLTV, or HCLTV ratios are limits on the loan-to-value ratios that dictate how much can be borrowed against a property relative to its value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 272}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RATE-AND-TERM REFINANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rate-and-Term Refinances are processes that allow borrowers to refinance their existing mortgage under new terms, which are typically permitted for all occupancy types."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 377}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPANCY TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupancy Types refer to the classification of properties based on how they are used by the borrower, such as primary residences, second homes, or investment properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 377}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IRS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"IRS (Internal Revenue Service) is the U.S. government agency responsible for tax collection and tax law enforcement, including managing income tax installment agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"IRS (Internal Revenue Service) is the U.S. government agency responsible for tax collection and tax law enforcement, which provides regulations regarding income and distributions."&lt;SEP&gt;"IRS, or the Internal Revenue Service, is a U.S. government agency responsible for tax collection and tax law enforcement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IRS (Internal Revenue Service) is a government agency responsible for collecting taxes and enforcing tax laws in the United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IRS (Internal Revenue Service) is the U.S. federal agency responsible for tax collection and tax law enforcement, significantly involved in taxpayer identification and tax return processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IRS (Internal Revenue Service) is the U.S. government agency responsible for tax collection and enforcement of tax laws, relevant for verifying income."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IRS, or Internal Revenue Service, is the U.S. government agency responsible for tax collection and enforcement; tax returns must be filed for mortgage qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The IRS, or Internal Revenue Service, is the revenue service of the United States federal government, responsible for tax collection and tax law enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a173c08400538977a1dc5397bceda0a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb3009468a2e7eaa9aab8998eae8ca6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 255}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELINQUENT CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delinquent Credit refers to accounts that are past due or in default, which significantly impact a borrower’s creditworthiness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 474}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTENUATING CIRCUMSTANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Extenuating Circumstances are unique, nonrecurring events beyond a borrower’s control that lead to financial difficulties, potentially affecting credit assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 75}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEDERAL TAX INSTALLMENT PLANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Federal Tax Installment Plans are arrangements that allow taxpayers to pay off delinquent federal income taxes in installments rather than a lump sum."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 266}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan File is a collection of documents and applications submitted by a borrower to a lender for mortgage approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan File is a collection of documents and information related to a mortgage application and approval process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan File is a collection of documents pertaining to a loan application, which includes financial records and credit history of the borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan File is the collection of documents and information compiled for a loan application, containing vital data needed for underwriting and approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEBT-TO-INCOME RATIO (DTI)">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Debt-to-Income Ratio (DTI) is a financial measure used by lenders to evaluate a borrower's ability to manage monthly payments and repay debts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHARGE-OFF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Charge-off refers to the accounting action taken by lenders when they deem a debt uncollectible and write it off, though the debtor is still responsible for the debt."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVORCE DECREE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Divorce Decree is a legal document issued by a court that finalizes a divorce, outlining obligations and rights, which may influence a borrower's financial situation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Divorce Decree is a legal document outlining the terms of a divorce, including payments for alimony or child support to be considered stable income."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 73}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL BILLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Medical Bills are charges for healthcare services provided to individuals, which may impact a person's financial standing and creditworthiness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JOB LAYOFF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Job Layoff refers to an involuntary termination of employment, which may lead to financial instability for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 75}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEVERANCE PAPERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Severance Papers are documents issued to employees when they are laid off, detailing their rights and the compensation they will receive after leaving the job."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 75}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY LISTING AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Listing Agreements are contracts between a seller and a real estate agent outlining the terms for selling a property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 476}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEASE AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lease Agreements are contracts between a landlord and a tenant specifying the terms under which a property is rented."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 75}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tax Returns are annual financial documents filed with the IRS that report an individual or business's income, expenses, and other pertinent financial information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns are documents filed with the IRS that report income, expenses, and other tax obligations, necessary for assessing a self-employed individual's financial stability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns are financial documents submitted by individuals to report income and are required for assessing borrowers' income stability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns are financial documents submitted to tax authorities, providing insight into a borrower's income and financial situation for loan qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns are forms filed with the IRS that document an individual's income and tax obligations for a specific year."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns are forms submitted to tax authorities detailing income and deductions, used to assess financial standing and rental history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns are official documents filed with the IRS detailing a borrower's income and tax obligations, required for loan application processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns are official documents filed with the government that detail a person's income and tax information, crucial for mortgage qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns are official documents submitted to the IRS that detail an individual's income, expenses, and tax liability, essential for financial assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns are official forms submitted to tax authorities detailing income, expenses, and taxes paid, which are often required by lenders for loan evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns refer to the forms filed with the IRS reporting income, deductions, and credits that determine tax liability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax returns are financial documents submitted to the IRS, used to establish a history of income for verification purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax returns are legal documents filed with tax authorities, crucial for verifying a borrower's income over the past years."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a173c08400538977a1dc5397bceda0a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f91be92d53c1aed3b7126461f33e415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ae330f51f478e78f1b91957f17dcdec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1955da1ebc911d30ff778d5b9e719028&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-332ea40a8706fdd85456078cf47232fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ed1a879d48c49b16f42ce89ae56d954</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 266}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LETTER FROM BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Letter from Borrower is a written document provided by a borrower explaining their financial situation, often used to support claims of financial distress."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 266}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DU FINDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DU Findings come from Desktop Underwriter, which assesses borrowers' creditworthiness and eligibility for mortgage loans, determining their risk within the lending framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU Findings refers to the results generated by Desktop Underwriter, an automated underwriting system used by lenders to assess a borrower's mortgage application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ALIMONY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Alimony is a financial support obligation that must be verified to be considered acceptable stable income during mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alimony refers to the financial support that one spouse is required to pay to another after separation or divorce, which must be verified through legal documents for mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alimony refers to the financial support that one spouse may be required to pay to another after a divorce, treated as a liability in loan underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 73}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHILD SUPPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Child Support is a court-ordered payment from one parent to another, aimed at supporting the upbringing of a child after separation or divorce."&lt;SEP&gt;"Child Support is a legal obligation for a non-custodial parent to provide financial support for their children, requiring verification for stability in financial assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Child Support is a legal obligation to provide financial support for a child after parental separation, which can impact a borrower's financial assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Child support is a financial obligation that must be documented to be accepted as stable income for mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 73}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRIDGE LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A bridge loan is a short-term loan used to bridge the gap between the purchase of a new property and the sale of an existing one, secured by the present home."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY DEBT OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Monthly Debt Obligations are recurring payments that borrowers must make as part of their financial commitments, including loans and other responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monthly Debt Obligations pertain to the recurring debts a borrower must account for when assessing their financial capacity for a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 63}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORIZED USER ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Authorized User Accounts refer to credit accounts granted to another person (authorized user), which can affect the credit assessment of the primary borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 63}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business Debt refers to debts incurred by a borrower’s business, which can sometimes be excluded from their personal financial assessments if certain conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COUNTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"County refers to the specific administrative region in which the subject property is situated, affecting the legal and financial context of the mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT REMINDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment reminder is a notification from the IRS regarding upcoming or missed payments, important for validating a borrower's compliance with payment plans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHARGE-OFFS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Charge-offs refer to debts that a creditor has deemed unlikely to be collected, which can affect a borrower's credit profile and loan qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2 TO 4-UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"2 to 4-unit properties are residential properties with multiple living units, impacting the specific lending criteria applicable during underwriting."&lt;SEP&gt;"2 to 4-unit properties refer to residential buildings that contain multiple housing units, which may have specific requirements for appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 329}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECURRING OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Recurring obligations encompass the ongoing financial responsibilities of a borrower, which must be reviewed during the debt-to-income ratio computation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 63}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL ESTATE TAX PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Real Estate Tax Payment refers to the monthly obligation that must be calculated based on the value of improvements and land for properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 213}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Courts are judicial institutions where matters related to assignments of debts and legal obligations may be addressed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL_TERM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Payment includes all obligations the borrower must pay, particularly regarding property taxes and other financial responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Payment includes the full payments made towards a mortgage loan, which are assessed when calculating a borrower's total monthly obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
