</node>
<node id="&quot;GARNISHMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Garnishments refer to legal deductions from an individual's salary to satisfy a debt, which impact the borrowing capacity as outlined in the guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 199}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-MORTGAGE DEBTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-Mortgage Debts are financial obligations other than mortgages that may affect the qualification of a borrower, subject to specific documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFERRED INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Deferred Installment Debt refers to scheduled payments that are temporarily postponed, impacting a borrower's total monthly obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CURRENT PRIMARY RESIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Current Primary Residence is the home of the Borrower where they reside and is subject to specific underwriting considerations during a sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 507}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINGENT LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contingent Liability is a potential financial obligation that could arise under certain conditions, impacting how debt qualifications are assessed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contingent Liability refers to the potential obligation a borrower may have under a mortgage when their interest in a property is bought out but the mortgage liability is not canceled."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61ba5485d92daa30adf4ee02bfab7d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 199}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT-ORDERED ASSIGNMENT OF DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court-Ordered Assignment of Debt refers to the legal process where a borrower's outstanding debt is assigned to another party by court order, affecting their liabilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 199}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OUTSTANDING DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Outstanding Debt refers to the total amount of money that a borrower owes, which can impact their eligibility for new loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXECUTED BUYOUT AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Executed Buyout Agreement refers to a finalized agreement where an employer or relocation company agrees to take responsibility for a borrower's mortgage, as part of a relocation plan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 507}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACQUISITION OF REAL ESTATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Acquisition of Real Estate refers to the process of purchasing property, which includes considerations of existing mortgages and debts to qualify for financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 507}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUFFICIENT RESERVES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sufficient Reserves refer to the financial resources that a borrower must have to cover monthly payments while waiting for a home sale to close."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 55}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LPA RESPONSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LPA Response refers to the findings from the Loan Product Advisor, a tool used in the mortgage industry to assess borrower qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 55}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY PAYMENT AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Monthly Payment Amount is the sum that a borrower must pay each month towards their loan obligations, inclusive of principal and interest."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER'S PAYMENT LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower's Payment Letter is a document that details the payment obligations for deferred debts, helping in the evaluation of total monthly obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORBEARANCE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Forbearance Agreement is a legal document that temporarily reduces or suspends a borrower's debt payments, taking into account their financial situation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Installment Debt refers to loans that require monthly payments over a specified period and must be included in debt calculations when relevant."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEASE PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lease Payments are recurring debts associated with leasing agreements that must be accounted for in monthly financial obligations regardless of lease term."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lease Payments are the scheduled monetary obligations an individual or organization must fulfill under a lease agreement for solar panels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 32}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE ASSUMPTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Assumptions involve the transfer of mortgage liability to a new owner when a property is sold, subject to specific documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 414}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;401K&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"401K is a type of retirement savings account that allows individuals to save for retirement with tax advantages, often used as collateral for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IRA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An IRA (Individual Retirement Account) is a savings account that is designed to help individuals save for retirement with tax advantages."&lt;SEP&gt;"An IRA (Individual Retirement Account) is a tax-advantaged account that individuals use to save for retirement, allowing them to invest in various assets."&lt;SEP&gt;"An IRA, or Individual Retirement Account, is a savings account with tax advantages that individuals can use to save for retirement, which may include investments such as stocks and mutual funds."&lt;SEP&gt;"IRA (Individual Retirement Account) is a financial product that provides individuals with tax advantages for retirement savings."&lt;SEP&gt;"IRA, or Individual Retirement Account, is a financial product that allows individuals to save for retirement with tax advantages, composed of various investments like stocks and mutual funds."&lt;SEP&gt;"IRA, or Individual Retirement Account, is a savings account that offers tax advantages for retirement savings and may serve as collateral for secured loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bc03d45e68c4df0463506aff2ba2a679&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67964fc288da88f7bb3defef1f29177&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c392c46c8ab1fb7407628dd97c6f2c74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 90}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CD stands for Certificate of Deposit, a financial product that offers a fixed interest rate on a deposit for a specified term, often used as collateral."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Debt represents the amount owed on loans secured by property, critical in real estate transactions and financial assessments."</data>
