<node id="&quot;TAX RETURN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Tax Return is a form filed with the IRS reporting income, expenses, and other pertinent financial information used to determine tax liability."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Tax Return is a formal declaration of income filed with tax authorities, which may be required for verifying a borrower's financial status in mortgage processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Tax Return is a formal report filed with a tax authority detailing income, expenses, and other relevant tax information, used for verifying income."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Tax Return is a formal report where an individual or business outlines income, expenses, and other tax information, essential for verifying income in loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tax return is a form filed with the IRS reporting income, expenses, and other relevant tax information used to calculate tax obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Return is a financial document that borrowers must provide to prove income when qualifying for a mortgage loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Return refers to the annual report filed by individuals to the IRS detailing income, expenses, and other tax information, relevant in verifying income such as royalties."</data>
