<node id="&quot;MARKETABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Marketability describes how easily a property can be sold in the market, influenced by various factors such as condition, location, and the presence of accessory dwelling units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marketability refers to how easily a property can be sold in the market, affected by resale restrictions and property condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marketability refers to how easily a property can be sold in the market, influenced by various factors including location, condition, and market conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marketability refers to the appeal and value of a property in the real estate market, influenced by various factors including environmental conditions and legal requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marketability refers to the desirability and feasibility of selling a property in the current real estate environment, impacting its overall value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marketability refers to the desirability or selling potential of a property based on comparable sales and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marketability refers to the ease with which a property can be sold and is an important consideration in the appraisal of manufactured homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marketability refers to the ease with which a property can be sold in the market, impacted by its condition and appraised value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marketability refers to the ease with which a property can be sold in the market, influenced by the presence of solar panels and the conditions outlined in the underwriting guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marketability refers to the ease with which a property can be sold, especially in relation to its features like solar panels, which can influence perceived value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-137c762b3ac588b243786790757dd239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12708616563afb36a31ad3cf8523241b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 394}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMEREADY PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The HomeReady Program is a mortgage initiative designed to assist first-time homebuyers, particularly those with low to moderate incomes, providing them financial pathways to homeownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HUD (Department of Housing and Urban Development) is a U.S. government agency that oversees homeownership education, counseling, and other housing-related programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"HUD, or the Department of Housing and Urban Development, is a U.S. government agency that establishes and enforces standards for manufactured homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"HUD, or the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, is a government agency that oversees federal programs related to housing and urban development, including the safety standards for manufactured homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"HUD, or the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, provides guidelines and standards for housing and financial counseling services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 484}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAMEWORK HOMEOWNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Framework Homeownership is an online education program required for borrowers to complete prior to loan closing, focusing on homeownership education and financial literacy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 482}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMEOWNERSHIP EDUCATION AND COUNSELING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Homeownership Education and Counseling encompasses training programs and assistance aimed at guiding potential buyers through the home-buying process and managing financial aspects related to homeownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 482}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOUSING COUNSELING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Housing Counseling refers to personalized financial assistance addressing individual housing issues and obstacles to homeownership, which is essential for successful home ownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUDGET AND WRITTEN ACTION PLAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Budget and Written Action Plan is a structured approach for borrowers to manage their financial situation and prepare for homeownership, which must be created during housing counseling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 483}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION OF HOUSING COUNSELING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Certificate of Completion of Housing Counseling is a formal document verifying that a borrower has successfully completed housing counseling, essential for meeting loan requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 482}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN-LEVEL PRICE ADJUSTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan-Level Price Adjustment refers to adjustments in mortgage pricing associated with certain borrower qualifications, including completion of housing counseling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 482}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACQUISITION OF PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Acquisition of Property refers to the process outlined in the text, specifically involving the purchase money transaction for financing the acquisition of real estate."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 482}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EDUCATION WITH AN ESTABLISHED CURRICULUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Education with an Established Curriculum refers to structured learning programs designed to impart essential knowledge about homeownership, aimed at helping borrowers succeed in the home-buying process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 207}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROUP OR CLASSROOM SETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Group or Classroom Setting indicates the format in which homeownership education can be delivered, highlighting the importance of interactive learning experiences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 207}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ONE-ON-ONE ASSISTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"One-on-One Assistance provides personalized, tailored support to individuals addressing unique financial and housing challenges in achieving homeownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREDATORY LENDING PRACTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Predatory Lending Practices refer to deceptive financial practices that disadvantage borrowers, emphasizing the need for awareness and education in the home-buying process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAIR LENDING OR FAIR HOUSING REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fair Lending or Fair Housing Requirements are legal standards ensuring equitable access to housing and mortgage services, protecting consumers from discrimination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMEOWNERSHIP EDUCATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Homeownership Education Requirements are stipulations set forth by Freddie Mac that at least one borrower must complete education prior to the loan note date."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeownership Education Requirements outline the criteria that must be met by borrowers to ensure they are adequately informed about the responsibilities of homeownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 483}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COURSE COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Certificate of Course Completion is a document issued to participants who successfully complete required homeownership or landlord education courses."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Certificate of Course Completion is a necessary document confirming that a borrower has finished required education or counseling courses prior to closing on a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 494}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIONAL INDUSTRY STANDARDS FOR HOMEOWNERSHIP EDUCATION AND COUNSELING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This organization sets the standards for homeownership education and counseling programs in the U.S., ensuring quality and compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 484}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMEPOSSIBLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HomePossible is a mortgage product offered by Freddie Mac that requires educational courses for borrowers, aimed at supporting multi-unit purchases and first-time homebuyers."&lt;SEP&gt;"HomePossible is a mortgage product that requires borrowers to meet certain income limits for eligibility, affecting property purchasing and refinancing options."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 95}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LANDLORD EDUCATION PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Landlord Education Program is a required training for borrowers to prepare for managing rental properties, ensuring they are informed and compliant with management practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Landlord Education Program is a course that qualifying borrowers must participate in to manage rental properties effectively, ensuring they understand landlord responsibilities and rental management."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Landlord Education Program is a required educational course for borrowers involving rental property management, ensuring they are equipped with knowledge on being responsible landlords."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b454650a6e8dde5a93325db30813c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 123}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUITY OF OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continuity of Obligation is a requirement that ensures at least one borrower remains involved in the refinancing process, preserving legal obligations from the original mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Continuity of Obligation refers to the requirement that certain conditions must be met in refinancing transactions, ensuring responsible lending and borrowing practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 95}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE INSURANCE COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are companies that provide mortgage insurance for lenders, including Arch, Enact (formerly Genworth), MGIC, and Radian, ensuring that loans are protected against default."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"NIS stands for National Industry Standards, which set guidelines for homeownership education and counseling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 483}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDITSMART HOMEBUYER U&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CreditSmart Homebuyer U is an educational curriculum developed by Freddie Mac aimed at equipping potential homebuyers with knowledge for making informed buying decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 484}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Certificate of Completion is necessary documentation for the completion of HUD-approved education courses, ensuring compliance with lending standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7af9f372a5143b38d8551b1bc9a9f8f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 483}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFINOW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"RefiNow is a refinancing program offered by Fannie Mae aimed at helping borrowers refinance their existing mortgages under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFI POSSIBLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refi Possible is a refinancing initiative by Freddie Mac designed to assist borrowers in refinancing under certain guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELINQUENT REAL ESTATE TAXES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delinquent Real Estate Taxes are unpaid property taxes that impact the eligibility and conditions for refinancing transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 301}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Payment History denotes the record of payments made by borrowers, which is essential for assessing their eligibility for refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 95}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EQUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Equity is the difference between the market value of a property and the amount owed on the mortgage, crucial for determining loan eligibility and amount."&lt;SEP&gt;"Equity is the difference between the market value of a property and the amount owed on the mortgage, influencing refinancing opportunities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Equity is the difference between the value of the property and the amount owed on any liens or mortgages against that property, pertinent in cash-out refinances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Equity is the value of the borrower's interest in a property after subtracting liabilities, significant in determining refinancing options and mortgage strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Equity refers to the value of an ownership interest in property, often measured by the difference between the property’s market value and the balance of any debts secured against that property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OUTSTANDING LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Outstanding Lien refers to a legal claim against a property that has not been satisfied, affecting refinancing possibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEASONING PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seasoning Period refers to the minimum duration that must pass before refinancing a mortgage, typically aimed at ensuring financial stability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATE MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A subordinate mortgage is a loan secured by a property that ranks below the primary mortgage in terms of repayment priority during a foreclosure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Mortgage is a type of loan that is secondary to a primary mortgage, potentially impacting refinancing strategy and eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Mortgage refers to a type of loan that is secured (or subordinate) to another loan on the same property, affecting the hierarchy of claims to payment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 461}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-OUT TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A cash-out transaction is a refinancing method where a borrower takes out a larger loan than the existing mortgage, receiving the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Transaction occurs when a borrower refinances and takes additional cash from their property's equity, often affecting their loan terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISSOLUTION OF A DOMESTIC PARTNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dissolution of a Domestic Partnership refers to the legal termination of a partnership, which can involve inherited property considerations in refinancing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The dissolution of a domestic partnership is the legal termination of a partnership agreement, similar to a divorce, often requiring settlement agreements on property and assets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOME EQUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Home Equity signifies the portion of the property's value that the owner actually owns outright, playing a critical role in refinancing options."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIMARY RESIDENCE DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Primary Residence Documentation includes records that confirm a borrower's primary residence status, necessary for qualifying for certain refinancing products."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Assessed Clean Energy (PACE) refers to programs that finance energy-related improvements for residential properties through localities, usually repaid via property tax bills."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 248}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-OUT REFINANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cash-out refinances are transactions that enable borrowers to access equity in their property by obtaining a new mortgage, distinct from traditional refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refinance refers to the process in which existing debt is retired and replaced with new debt under different terms, and it requires verification of income and rental documentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refinance refers to the process of replacing an existing loan with a new loan under different terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refinancing is the process of obtaining a new mortgage to replace an existing one, often to benefit from lower interest rates or to access home equity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 120}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 365}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"First Mortgage refers to the primary loan that a borrower takes out, which is secured against the property being purchased and influences borrower costs and lending risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The first mortgage is the primary loan taken out to purchase a property, which has the first claim against the property in case of default or foreclosure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909</data>
