</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVORCE SETTLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A divorce settlement is an agreement reached between parties in a divorce case concerning the division of assets, which can include property interest buyouts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A property transfer refers to the legal process of changing ownership of a property from one party to another, often involving documentation and agreements among owners."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENERGY RETROFIT LENDING PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Energy retrofit lending programs are financial programs designed to fund improvements in residential properties aimed at increasing energy efficiency."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 248}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL ESTATE TAX BILL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A real estate tax bill is a statement issued to property owners indicating the amount of tax owed on their property, which may include PACE loan repayments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 248}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTATION TO SUPPORT THE PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documentation to support the property involves the necessary paperwork evidencing ownership, condition, and valuation of a property, crucial in loan transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-faa30e2538a6e107a9cdb96ee1067084</data>
