</node>
<node id="&quot;LIMITED LIABILITY CORPORATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Limited Liability Corporation (LLC) is a business structure that offers protection for its owners against personal liability for debts, and ownership can impact mortgage refinancing processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 436}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIMITED PARTNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Limited Partnership (LP) is a business entity that has at least one general partner and one limited partner, relevant in the context of mortgage and refinance ownership requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 436}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOME EQUITY LINE OF CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Home Equity Line of Credit (HELOC) is a revolving loan in which the borrower can draw against the equity of their home, affecting refinancing guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 436}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PACE LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A PACE Loan is a financing mechanism used to fund energy-efficient residential improvements, like solar panels, with a focus on property tax assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A PACE Loan is a type of financing that allows property owners to pay for energy efficiency upgrades, paid back through property taxes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A PACE loan is a financing option that enables property owners to fund energy efficiency and renewable energy improvements, affecting mortgage lending practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIAL FEATURE CODES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Special Feature Codes (SFC) are identifiers used in loan processing systems to signal specific characteristics or requirements pertaining to mortgage transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Special Feature Codes are identifiers used to signify specific attributes or conditions related to mortgage products during underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STUDENT LOAN CASH-OUT REFINANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Student loan cash-out refinances allow borrowers to use refinancing transactions to pay off student loan debt, providing a possible waiver under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL CLEAR TO CLOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Final Clear to Close is a status indicating that all conditions have been met to proceed with mortgage closing, crucial for loan processing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 302}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELEGATED CORRESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delegated Correspondent refers to entities that have been granted authority to approve mortgages on behalf of another lender, impacting mortgage processing timelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 302}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A mortgage file is a collection of documents pertaining to a mortgage loan, which lenders use to make assessments regarding the loan's terms and borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage file refers to a collection of documents related to a mortgage, including underwriting guidelines, loan agreements, and financial statements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Mortgage File is a collection of documents and correspondence that includes all necessary information for verifying a borrower's employment and loan details."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Mortgage File is a compilation of documents related to a mortgage loan, including evidence of income, rental agreements, and educational program completion for landlords."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Mortgage file is a collection of documents related to a mortgage application and approval process, used to assess the borrower's eligibility, including rental income from ADUs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec242ee203576a6a4b76efbe5458e782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 358}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY ACQUISITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property acquisition refers to the process of obtaining property ownership through purchase or other means, with specific timelines related to refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNERSHIP REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ownership Requirement refers to the conditions that must be met regarding the length of property ownership before refinancing can occur, specifically in mortgage guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIX-MONTH OWNERSHIP REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Six-Month Ownership Requirement is a stipulation that a borrower must own a property for a minimum of six months before refinancing, with exceptions applicable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUNIOR LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A junior lien is a second mortgage or subordinate lien that is secured against property after the first mortgage, influencing refinancing options."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BLANKET MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A blanket mortgage covers multiple properties under one lien, impacting refinancing processes and transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-OUT REFINANCE LLPA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cash-out Refinance LLPA refers to the Loan Level Pricing Adjustment applicable to cash-out refinance loans, which affects the pricing and eligibility of such loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 436}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-OUT REFINANCE LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A cash-out refinance loan is a type of mortgage that allows the borrower to convert the equity in their property into cash, typically by refinancing for more than the amount owed on the existing mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 436}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL CLOSING STATUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Final Closing Status refers to the last stage in the mortgage process where all requirements are satisfied and the transaction is ready for closure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 301}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPAIR DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Repair Documentation provides evidence of repairs made to a property, which may be required for loan processing and approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 302}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY LISTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Listing refers to the act of putting a property for sale in the market, which may affect the refinancing process if the property has been recently listed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 457}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Market Documentation includes records and data related to the current market conditions that may influence property valuation and loan assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 514}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSFER OF TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transfer of Title is the process of changing the legal ownership of a property, which is essential in mortgage transactions, especially when refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN APPROVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Approval is the formal consent given by a lender that allows a borrower to receive a mortgage, subject to meeting specific criteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 32}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LTV RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LTV Ratio (Loan-to-Value Ratio) measures the ratio of a loan amount to the appraised value of the property, used in underwriting mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV Ratio is a financial calculation that assesses the ratio of a loan to the appraised value of the property, indicating risk levels for lenders."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV Ratio, or Loan-To-Value Ratio, measures the loan amount against the appraised value of a property, crucial for assessing risk in lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV Ratio, or Loan-to-Value Ratio, is a financial term used by lenders to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, often used in mortgage applications to assess risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV Ratio, or Loan-to-Value Ratio, is a financial term used by lenders to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV Ratio, or Loan-to-Value Ratio, is a financial term used to express the ratio of a loan amount to the appraised value or purchase price of the property, used as a risk assessment measure."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV Ratio, or Loan-to-Value Ratio, is a mathematical calculation used to determine the risk posed by a mortgage loan based on the property value and the loan amount."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV Ratio, or Loan-to-Value ratio, is a financial term used to assess the risk of a loan based on the property's value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2e912b60195be8ca87a44127ef55d282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4de71275bc933c2c228984f601d0e0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 463}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLTV RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CLTV Ratio (Combined Loan-to-Value Ratio) refers to the total ratio of all loans secured against a property to its appraised value."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV Ratio calculates the combined loan-to-value ratio, factoring in both the primary mortgage and any second mortgages to assess total debt against property value."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV Ratio, or Combined Loan-To-Value Ratio, takes into account all loans secured by a property, providing a broader view of home financing and risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV Ratio, or Combined Loan-to-Value Ratio, is a financial metric used to assess risk by representing the ratio of all loans secured by the property compared to its value."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV Ratio, or Combined Loan-to-Value Ratio, refers to the ratio of all loans secured by a property compared to its appraised value, important for refinancing and loan evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV Ratio, or Combined Loan-to-Value ratio, is a financial metric that combines the first mortgage and any other liens to evaluate the total risk associated with property financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Combined Loan-to-Value (CLTV) ratio is a metric used to calculate the total proportion of residential property value that is mortgaged, including all subordinate funding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4de71275bc933c2c228984f601d0e0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 463}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HCLTV RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HCLTV Ratio, or Home Equity Combined Loan-to-Value Ratio, includes all lines of credit against the property's market value, vital in refinancing decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"HCLTV Ratio, or Home Equity Combined Loan-to-Value Ratio, is a calculation that includes all outstanding loans in relation to the property’s value."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Home Equity Combined Loan-to-Value (HCLTV) ratio is specifically used for home equity loans, comparing the total of first lien mortgages and all available lines of credit against the value of the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 419}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWING LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrowing Limits refer to the maximum amount a borrower is allowed to borrow based on various factors, including creditworthiness and property value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITING REVIEW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Underwriting Review is the assessment performed by the underwriter to determine loan eligibility and compliance with guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Review is the process by which lenders evaluate the risk of insuring a loan, determining whether to approve or deny a mortgage application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6843059eea11d10d23493c39af4afd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 516}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN LEVEL PRICING ADJUSTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Level Pricing Adjustment (LLPA) involves adjustments to mortgage rates based on the assessed risk of the borrower and property, influencing the final cost of borrowing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELAYED FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delayed Financing refers to the process that allows borrowers who purchased a property within the last six months to refinance under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 437}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENERGY IMPROVEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORM_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Energy Improvements refer to modifications or upgrades made to a property to increase its energy efficiency, often financed through special loans or programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WELCOME MENU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORM_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Welcome Menu refers to a user interface or a list of options available to a user when they initiate a program or system."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORM_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Division refers to the act of separating something into parts, often used here in the context of financial calculations or ratios in the underwriting process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">("NORM_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment refers to the transfer of money or value from one entity to another as compensation for services rendered or goods provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest Rate refers to the amount charged, expressed as a percentage of the principal, by a lender to a borrower for the use of assets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Rate refers to the cost of borrowing in the form of a percentage of the loan amount, affecting mortgage payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0610be8f2c48d2ab9263a9d9aea08a29</data>
