  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Partnership is a business entity where two or more individuals manage and operate a business while sharing its profits and liabilities, particularly in the context of reporting rental income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Partnership indicates a business structure where two or more individuals share ownership, which may also act as borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Partnership is a business structure where two or more individuals manage and operate a business on shared terms, significant for self-employment income analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Partnership is a business structure where two or more individuals manage and operate a business together, sharing its profits and liabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Partnership refers to a business structure where two or more individuals share ownership and the profits or losses of the business, often requiring specific documentation for income assessment."</data>
