<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATE FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subordinate Financing refers to a secondary loan that is secured by a property in addition to the primary mortgage, which must be disclosed and considered during loan evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to additional financing that is placed behind the primary mortgage in terms of claim on the property in case of default."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to secondary loans taken in addition to a primary mortgage, with terms affecting the overall loan structure and its acceptance in underwriting processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing signifies any secondary loan provided on a property, which affects the terms and limitations of primary financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate financing is a form of secondary financing that ranks below primary mortgages in terms of claim priority against the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e252311920cec13b843fb034a4a69e94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
