<node id="&quot;HIGH-COST AREA LOAN LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High-Cost Area Loan Limits are specific borrowing limits set for areas where property prices are significantly above the national average, necessitating special consideration in financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-Cost Area Loan Limits are the maximum allowable loan amounts established for areas that experience elevated housing costs relative to the national average."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e252311920cec13b843fb034a4a69e94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 338}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISER'S CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Appraiser's Certificate of Completion is a document certifying that a property has been constructed as per agreed specifications and is necessary for mortgage approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e252311920cec13b843fb034a4a69e94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 492}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF OCCUPANCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Certificate of Occupancy is an official document issued by a local government certifying that a building is compliant with regulations and suitable for occupancy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e252311920cec13b843fb034a4a69e94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 204}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 492}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST MORTGAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"First Mortgages are the primary loans secured by a property, typically holding priority over any other liens or debts associated with that property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e252311920cec13b843fb034a4a69e94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PURCHASE TRANSACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Purchase Transactions refer to the process of acquiring property through a sale, including the terms and conditions for financing the purchase."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e252311920cec13b843fb034a4a69e94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DETACHED CONDOMINIUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Detached Condominium is a type of housing where the unit owner owns both the condo unit and the land it's built on, differing from traditional condominium structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Detached Condominium is a type of property that is separate from other units, which can influence its eligibility for certain mortgage products under specific guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e252311920cec13b843fb034a4a69e94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTIGUOUS STATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contiguous States refer to the 48 adjoining U.S. states and the District of Columbia, excluding Alaska and Hawaii, influencing loan limits in the region."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 30}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFINANCE TRANSACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refinance Transactions involve replacing an existing loan with a new one, often for better rates or terms, and are addressed under specific underwriting guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refinance Transactions involve the replacement of an existing mortgage with a new one, which is significant for underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SECOND PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Second Program refers to a specific type of financing aimed at making housing more affordable, detailed in product guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 420}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GIFT/GRANT PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gift/Grant Program is a financial assistance initiative to aid homebuyers, linked to community support for property acquisition."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 420}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER SUBORDINATE FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer Subordinate Financing is a financial arrangement where employers provide loans to employees, often with flexible repayment terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employer Subordinate Financing refers to loans provided by employers to employees, which may have special conditions regarding repayment and eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 168}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEGATIVE AMORTIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Negative Amortization is a financial situation where the loan balance increases over time due to insufficient payments, often relevant in discussions of subordinate financing types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negative Amortization refers to a situation in which the mortgage payments do not cover the interest due, causing the loan balance to increase."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negative Amortization refers to a situation where the loan balance increases due to non-adequate payments, relevant to loan management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 168}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FULLY AMORTIZING LEVEL PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fully Amortizing Level Payments refers to a structured repayment schedule where the borrower pays a fixed amount each period towards the loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 167}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFERRED PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Deferred Payments refer to arrangements wherein the borrower is allowed to postpone payments for a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 168}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRAP-AROUND TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wrap-around Terms describe a financing structure that consolidates first and subordinate mortgage debts into a single agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wrap-around Terms refer to financing structures where a secondary mortgage wraps around an existing primary mortgage, combining different levels of indebtedness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 165}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE/DEED OF TRUST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage/Deed of Trust is a legal document that secures the loan with the property pledged as collateral, essential in the foreclosure process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 329}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VARIABLE PAYMENT MORTGAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Variable Payment Mortgages are loan products that have adjustable interest rates, leading to fluctuating payment amounts based on market changes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 167}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Market Rate refers to the average interest rate prevailing in the financial market, against which other rates, such as those for subordinate financing, are compared."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 338}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HELOCS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HELOCs, or Home Equity Lines of Credit, are revolving credit lines secured by a home's equity, allowing homeowners to borrow against their property's value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 167}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST DUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest Due signifies the amount of interest payable at a given time within a financing agreement, influencing payment schedules and amortization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 167}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FULLY AMORTIZING DEFERRED PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fully Amortizing Deferred Payments represent a financing method where payments are postponed initially but eventually require full amortization over the loan term."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 168}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORGIVENESS OF DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Forgiveness of Debt refers to the cancellation of a borrower's obligation to repay part or all of their debt, often structured over time in employer financing agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 168}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VARIABLE INTEREST RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Variable Interest Rate is an interest rate that fluctuates based on changes in a benchmark rate, affecting loan payments and overall borrowing costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 167}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES CONCESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Concession is a financial arrangement where a seller provides a concession in the sales price, often influencing the terms of a subordinate financing agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb6bc64edebfe344dd27f1923850080</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TLTV RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Total Loan-to-Value (TLTV) ratio is a financial metric used to assess the risk of lending against a property, calculated by combining the unpaid principal of the first mortgage and subordinate mortgages divided by the property value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 419}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SECOND LIENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Second liens are financial products offered to help borrowers finance homes, which cannot be subordinated on cash-out transactions according to the guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EQUITY SHARING LIENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Equity Sharing liens are financial structures where an investor shares in a property's equity, which must adhere to specific eligibility requirements outlined in the guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RATE-AND-TERM REFINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rate-and-Term Refinance is a financial event that involves refinancing a loan with the goal of adjusting the interest rate or changing the loan term."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rate-and-Term Refinance is a mortgage product that aims to lower the interest rate or change the term of the mortgage without taking cash out."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rate-and-Term Refinance is a type of refinancing transaction aimed at adjusting the interest rate or terms of an existing mortgage without extracting cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rate-and-Term Refinance is an event where a borrower refinances an existing mortgage for a lower rate or better terms, often involving various eligibility criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rate-and-Term Refinance refers to a financial transaction that allows borrowers to refinance their manufactured home loan under certain guidelines including paying off existing mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rate-and-term refinance is a type of refinancing that adjusts the loan terms or interest rate without cashing out homeowner equity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rate-and-term refinance is a type of transaction where an existing mortgage is replaced with a new one under different terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-645973893eaf0e8d2eb4a7822c3fe6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 131}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTIONAL LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conventional Loans are a type of mortgage loan not backed by the government, usually adhering to specific underwriting guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Loans are standard mortgage loans that are not insured or guaranteed by the federal government, subject to the guidelines discussed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional loans are mortgage loans that are not insured or guaranteed by the government and must adhere to certain underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 407}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATE LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subordinate Loans are secondary loans to a primary mortgage that carry higher risk and different underwriting requirements according to the guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATURITY DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Maturity Date in financing refers to the date on which the final payment of a loan is due, marking the end of the loan agreement period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BALLOON PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Balloon Payment is a large payment due at the end of a loan term, which can be a crucial consideration in subordinate financing arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITING CONSIDERATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Underwriting Considerations are the criteria and standards used by lenders to evaluate the risk and eligibility of loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 210}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATE FINANCING WITH WRAP-AROUND TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subordinate Financing with Wrap-around Terms refers to a financing arrangement where subordinate loans combine the indebtedness of both primary and subordinate mortgages, impacting the total risk assessment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financing generally refers to the management of money and credit to fund various projects, including mortgages, with specific guidelines for subordinate financing implications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER SUBORDINATE FINANCING WITH DEFERRED PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer Subordinate Financing with Deferred Payments is a type of loan provided by employers that allows repayment to be delayed under certain circumstances, affecting its evaluation in underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER’S DTI RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Borrower's Debt-to-Income (DTI) Ratio is a measurement of an individual's monthly debt payments in relation to their gross monthly income, critical for assessing financial stability in loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Value refers to the worth of a property based on various factors, including market conditions, location, and physical characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Value represents the worth of a property, which is used in calculations for various loan-to-value ratios that determine lending eligibility and terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property value is the estimated worth of real estate, influenced by various factors including market conditions, location, and property features."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 394}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-PURCHASE MONEY SECOND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Non-purchase Money Second refers to a type of subordinate financing that is acquired without the purchase of the property, subject to different underwriting standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CALCULATIONS OF CREDIT LINE LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Calculations of Credit Line Limits involve determining the total available credit for financing, which influences the loan amounts and conditions under underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATURITY OR BALLOON PAYMENT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Maturity or Balloon Payment Date indicates when a loan must be fully settled or a large payment made, crucial for managing refinancing and payment structuring."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer Financing refers to financial arrangements or loans provided by an employer to employees, which often have unique terms compared to traditional loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTIONAL LOANS WITH SUBORDINATE FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conventional Loans with Subordinate Financing are standard mortgages that allow for additional subordinate loans secured against the same property, following regulatory guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b73f39faaa03ed0e70ba760ab8eca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 329}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIVATE MORTGAGE INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Private Mortgage Insurance is insurance that protects lenders against borrower default, required for loans exceeding 80% loan-to-value (LTV)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 340}]</data>
