</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY TYPE LOAN PURPOSE POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Type Loan Purpose Policy establishes criteria based on the type of property and purpose of the loan to determine mortgage insurance requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SFR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"SFR, or Single-Family Residence, refers to a property type commonly used in mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2 TO 4-UNIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"2 to 4-Unit refers to properties that house two to four separate living units, affecting how mortgage insurance is assessed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Condo, or condominium, refers to a residential property divided into several units while retaining shared ownership of the common areas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PUD stands for Planned Unit Development, a designation for a type of property where the land is designed for a variety of dense uses."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUD, or Planned Unit Development, is a type of community that allows for a variety of housing types and is subject to specific eligibility criteria under mortgage guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUD, or Planned Unit Development, is a type of development that integrates residential and commercial units, allowing for a diverse living environment with shared amenities."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUD, or Planned Unit Development, refers to a type of building development that integrates different types of housing and commercial uses."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUD, or Planned Unit Development, refers to a type of community designed to be more integrated with shared spaces and possibly mixed-use developments, affecting eligibility for manufactured homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Development (PUD) is a type of building development designed to allow for a variety of housing types and mixed-use spaces."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE INSURANCE COVERAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Insurance Coverage protects lenders against borrower default, typically required when the down payment is below a certain threshold."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENDORSEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Endorsement refers to an addition to the mortgage insurance policy that specifies coverage details or requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INITIAL MORTGAGE PREMIUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">("PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Initial Mortgage Premium is the upfront fee required at the start of a mortgage agreement, impacting overall loan costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-464152a069c6a4d42a031274bf69430a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CO-OP REFINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Co-op Refinance refers to a specific event in which a cooperative property is being refinanced, with specific guidelines regarding mortgage insurance requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 341}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT STABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Stability emphasizes the importance of a borrower's stable and predictable income for qualifying for mortgage loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 77}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 300}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ITIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ITIN or Individual Taxpayer Identification Number is relevant for applicants who do not have a Social Security number but still need to apply for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 341}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STABLE INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stable Income refers to a consistent and reliable source of income, essential for mortgage approval, particularly regarding payments like alimony and child support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stable Income refers to consistent and predictable earnings from employment or other sources, crucial for loan approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stable Income refers to consistent earnings from employment or other sources that can be reliably expected to continue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stable income denotes reliable and consistent earnings over time, viewed favorably in the loan qualification process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f91be92d53c1aed3b7126461f33e415</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 77}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 299}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TWO-YEAR EMPLOYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Two-Year Employment History is a requirement for mortgage applications to demonstrate consistent income over a period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 77}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 298}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY TYPE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Type categorizes real estate properties based on their characteristics, influencing eligibility for loans and insurance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type refers to the classification of the real estate involved in the mortgage transaction, such as single-family homes or multi-family units."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed0db69e97fa62c70a7cb29c5e75fe07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 520}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CUSTOM MORTGAGE INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Custom Mortgage Insurance is a tailored insurance product for specific loans that may not meet standard criteria, providing unique coverage options."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 341}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHORT REFINANCE/PAYOFF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Short Refinance/Payoff refers to a refinancing event where the loan amount is reduced to reflect the current market value of the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 341}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STABLE EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stable Employment indicates a reliable job status that assures lenders of the borrower's ability to maintain mortgage payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 272}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VERBAL VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Verbal Verification is a process used in loan underwriting to confirm a borrower's employment status through direct communication with their employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 77}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 300}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAXIMUM LTV/CLTV/HCLTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum LTV/CLTV/HCLTV defines the highest permissible loan-to-value ratio for loans involving co-borrowers, crucial for assessing risk."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 77}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 298}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT GAP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Gap refers to the periods when an individual is not employed, which are reviewed to determine income stability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 205}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 500}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHANGING CAREERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Changing Careers is the act of transitioning from one occupation to another, which may affect a borrower's employment stability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 503}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FULL TIME EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Full Time Employment indicates a shift in a person's work status from part-time to full-time with the same employer, which is documented for loan qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART TIME EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part Time Employment refers to a work status where an individual works less than the standard full hours, which can impact income stability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 76}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VARIABLE INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Variable Income includes earnings that can fluctuate, such as commissions and bonuses, affecting loan qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Variable income refers to earnings that may fluctuate, such as overtime or bonuses, and are subject to different qualifying conditions in lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f91be92d53c1aed3b7126461f33e415</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 76}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELF-EMPLOYED INDIVIDUALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Self-Employed Individuals are those who work for themselves and whose income must be substantiated through tax returns for loan qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 76}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 297}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEASONAL EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seasonal Employment indicates jobs that are only available at certain times of the year, which can lead to frequent job changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seasonal employment refers to jobs that are available during certain seasons or times of the year, necessitating specific considerations for income assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seasonal employment refers to work that is only available during specific times of the year, affecting eligibility for financial support."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 54}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JOB CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Job Changes refer to the instances of an individual switching positions or companies, which may impact their employment history review."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 205}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 500}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income Calculation involves determining a borrower's earnings through various metrics to assess loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income Calculation refers to the method of determining the total income available to support loan repayment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income Calculation refers to the method used to assess a borrower's income based on verified income sources and expenses, critical for underwriting decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ed1a879d48c49b16f42ce89ae56d954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 76}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 297}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WVOE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"WVOE (Verification of Employment) is a form used to document an employee's transition from part-time to full-time status for loan qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"WVOE, or Written Verification of Employment, is a documentation method used to confirm a borrower's employment status and income, crucial for mortgage applications."</data>
