<node id="&quot;MARKET VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Market Value is an estimate of the price a property would sell for in the current market, influenced by various factors including condition, location, and the presence of units like ADUs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Value is the appraised value of a property which serves as the basis for determining loan-to-value (LTV) ratios in mortgage transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Value is the estimated price a property would sell for on the open market, based on various valuation methods and comparable sales."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Value is the estimated price that a property would sell for under normal conditions, affecting mortgage assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Value refers to the estimated price at which a property would sell in a competitive market, influenced by various external factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Value refers to the price at which a property would sell under normal market conditions, which appraisals aim to determine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Value refers to the worth of assets as determined by the current market, essential for verifying financial qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Value represents the estimated amount for which a property should exchange on the date of appraisal, considering various factors such as comparable sales and local conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Value represents the estimated worth of a property based on current market conditions and comparable sales, which can be affected by the presence of solar panels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-452a34dee684e3a93929cc44930deb38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 402}]</data>
</node>
