  <data key="d1">"Asset eligibility requirements are criteria that must be met for financial assets to be considered valid for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 46}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAXES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Taxes refer to financial obligations imposed by governments on income or transactions that must be filed and paid, impacting a borrower's financial status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VERIFICATION OF DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Verification of debt involves confirming outstanding balances and obligations of a borrower as part of the mortgage application process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 137}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAY STUBS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pay stubs are documents provided by employers to employees that list earnings, taxes, and deductions, used to verify income for mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 49}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STOCK PRICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stock prices refer to the current trading value of shares, used to assess the value of securities when verifying assets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL PUBLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial publications are authoritative sources that provide current financial data and information that may be used in asset verification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEDERAL INCOME TAX RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Federal Income Tax Returns are annual financial statements submitted to the IRS, providing insight into a borrower's income and financial status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Federal income tax returns are documents filed with the IRS that outline an individual's or business's income and expenses, crucial for income verification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8864c52069485823a39babaa2b2005e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 255}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LETTER FROM ORGANIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A letter from an organization is a formal document confirming income sources such as foster care, which is necessary for verification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 49}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VERIFICATION OF ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Verification of assets involves confirming a borrower's ownership and value of financial resources, which is part of the mortgage qualification process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 290}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE CREDIT CERTIFICATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Credit Certificates (MCCs) are issued by states or political subdivisions to provide first-time homebuyers with a federal tax credit on mortgage interest payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 276}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 8 VOUCHER PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 8 Voucher Payments are part of the Housing Choice Voucher programs, which aid eligible individuals without requiring prior receipt or expectation of ongoing payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 52}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC ASSISTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Assistance refers to welfare income that can be considered stable for mortgage application purposes, contingent on expected duration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 52}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFESSIONAL GAMBLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Professional Gambler refers to an individual who earns income through gambling activities and must document income stability for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THREE-YEAR CONTINUANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Three-Year Continuance refers to the expectation that certain income will continue for at least three years to be considered valid in mortgage underwriting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Three-Year Continuance refers to the requirement for certain benefits to be verified for likely continuation for at least three years in the context of income verification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Three-year Continuance refers to the requirement for confirming that certain benefits will continue for at least three years, especially in relation to the borrower's age."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c5f3698bd3a35ae6c5127d81864d41d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 537}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAX CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tax Credit is a government incentive allowing taxpayers to reduce their tax bills proportionate to specified expenses, such as mortgage interest payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 276}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest Income is the income earned from assets which can be factored into a borrower's financial assessment for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 266}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVIDEND INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dividend Income is the income generated from owning shares in companies, relevant in assessing a borrower's financial standing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 266}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET-RATE MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Market-Rate Mortgage is a loan for purchasing a home that reflects the current interest rates available in the marketplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Document Evidence refers to the required written proof needed to support a borrower's claims about their financial status in mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER'S BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Borrower's Business refers to the income-generating entity owned by the borrower, which may factor into their financial evaluation for loan qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELF-EMPLOYED INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Self-Employed Income is earnings obtained from running one's own business, which requires specific documentation for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE REVENUE BONDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Revenue Bonds are municipal bonds used to finance housing projects, often providing favorable mortgage terms to borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 276}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PENSION INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pension Income represents regular payments made to retirees from their previous employer, which need to be documented for stability and longevity considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETIREMENT INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Retirement Income is income received after retiring from work, which can be used as a source of income for loan qualification without considering self-employment losses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Retirement Income is the payments received by individuals after they have retired, which must be verified as stable for financial evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79943296a1fa68394820a29e269db689</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IRS W-2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"IRS W-2 forms are official documents used for tax reporting that indicate an employee's yearly wages and the taxes withheld from their paycheck."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IRS 1099&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"IRS 1099 forms are tax documents used to report various types of income other than wages, salaries, and tips."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;401(K) RETIREMENT ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A 401(k) is a tax-advantaged retirement savings account offered by many employers that allows employees to save a portion of their paycheck before taxes are taken out."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KEOGH RETIREMENT ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Keogh plan is a tax-deferred pension account that allows self-employed individuals to contribute to their own retirement savings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EFFECTIVE DATE OF INCOME COMMENCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Effective Date of Income Commencement refers to the specified date when income payments begin, required for financial documentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT FREQUENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Frequency indicates how often payments are made, such as monthly, annually, etc., which is important in assessing income stability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payment Frequency refers to how often income payments are received, which influences the assessment of income stability in mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 424}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Amount refers to the specific quantity of money paid during a transaction or at regular intervals, significant for budgeting and financial evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL OR BANK ACCOUNT STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial or Bank Account Statements are documents issued by financial institutions that summarize financial activities and balances over a specific period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 424}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE PAYMENT DUE DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Payment Due Date is the date by which a borrower must make their mortgage payment to avoid penalties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 424}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISTRIBUTION AMOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Distribution Amounts refer to the specific quantities of money withdrawn from retirement accounts, affecting income stability assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 424}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HISTORY OF RECEIPT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"History of Receipt denotes the record of consistent income received over time, which helps establish the reliability of income for applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 424}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETIREMENT INCOME GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Retirement Income Guidelines are procedures and requirements set forth to evaluate retirement income stability and eligibility for financial assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOVERNMENT ANNUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Government Annuity refers to a series of payments made by the government to individuals as part of their pension or retirement plan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BENEFICIARY VERIFICATION LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Beneficiary Verification Letter is a document confirming an individual's entitlement to benefits such as retirement or pension payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 421}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Documentation encompasses all records and evidence required to substantiate income claims for loans and financial applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXCISE TAX PENALTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Excise Tax Penalty is a financial penalty imposed for not complying with specific tax rules such as those related to withdrawals from retirement accounts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUFFICIENT ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sufficient Assets refer to the required financial resources that a borrower must demonstrate to support their qualifying income."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 531}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CURRENT RECEIPT OF INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Current Receipt of Income indicates that the income is actively being received and documented at the time of application for financial assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Current Receipt of Income is a documentation requirement confirming the ongoing receipt of income for purposes of mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3719c6acb29bd52b7e1e409b90cedc6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE UNDERWRITER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Mortgage Underwriter is a financial professional who evaluates loan applications, determining the creditworthiness and risk of potential borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 421}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTED HISTORY OF RECEIPT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documented History of Receipt refers to the established track record of continuous income that can be evidenced through documentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME SOURCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income Source indicates where income originates from, such as employment, investments, or government benefits, playing a crucial role in financial evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income Source refers to the origin from which an individual receives financial earnings, crucial for documenting qualifying income for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 531}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETIREMENT ACCOUNT STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Retirement Account Statement is a report issued by a financial institution summarizing the activity and balance of an individual's retirement account over a specific period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WITHDRAWAL PENALTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Withdrawal Penalty refers to a fee incurred when funds are taken out of an account before a specified age or outside of agreed-upon conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATURAL PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Natural Person refers to an individual human being as opposed to a legal entity such as a corporation or organization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 421}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTED TERMS OF INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documented Terms of Income refer to the agreed-upon stipulations regarding the receipt of income, including amounts, frequency, and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETIREMENT DISTRIBUTION OPTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Retirement Distribution Options refer to the various ways retirees can receive their benefits, such as lump sum or periodic payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROYALTY PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Royalty Payments indicate income received by borrowers that can be considered for mortgage qualification, requiring documentation of amounts and frequency."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SECURITY INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Social Security Income is the money received from the Social Security program, which can be used as qualifying income for mortgages under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social Security Income refers to a government program providing financial support to individuals based on their work record, particularly for the retired, disabled, or survivors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 539}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXECUTED SSA-3288&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Executed SSA-3288 is a form used to authorize the release of information from the Social Security Administration, necessary for verifying Social Security benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 539}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SSA AWARD LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"SSA Award Letter is a document from the Social Security Administration confirming eligibility and amount of benefits received, used in income verification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 539}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RMD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"RMD (Required Minimum Distribution) refers to the IRS requirements for minimum withdrawals from retirement accounts, relevant for income verification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISTRIBUTION PATTERNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Distribution Patterns refer to the regularity and frequency of income distributions considered in the underwriting guidelines, impacting the evaluation of stability for qualifying income."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 422}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIXED AMOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fixed Amounts are specific, consistent income distributions that occur at regular intervals, which may require a shorter history for stability evaluations in underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 422}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLUCTUATING AMOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fluctuating Amounts indicate income distributions that vary in amount and frequency, often necessitating more extensive documentation to establish stability for qualifying income."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 422}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETIREMENT PLAN RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Retirement Plan Rules refer to the regulations governing retirement accounts that can affect the income received from such plans during the mortgage application process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER RETIREMENT PLAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer Retirement Plan is a benefit plan established by an employer with rules affecting the income distribution and qualification for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANALYSIS METHODOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Analysis Methodology describes the approach used by underwriters to evaluate and determine stable monthly qualifying income based on various income sources."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 421}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMUM PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimum Payment History is the shortest timeframe the underwriter may consider acceptable to justify a stable income amount for qualifying."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95358b428c5f107947a116a0643878c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 423}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SECURITY INCOME DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Social Security Income Documentation Requirements refers to the guidelines for documenting receipt of Social Security payments, including what types of evidence are needed based on the benefits drawn from either the borrower's own account or another person's account."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c5f3698bd3a35ae6c5127d81864d41d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 538}]</data>
