<node id="&quot;S CORPORATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An S Corporation is a tax designation granted by the IRS allowing earnings to pass through to shareholders without being taxed at the corporate level, affecting how rental income is reported."&lt;SEP&gt;"S Corporation is a special type of corporation that meets specific Internal Revenue Code requirements, allowing income to pass through to shareholders to avoid double taxation."&lt;SEP&gt;"S Corporation is a type of corporation that meets specific Internal Revenue Code requirements and can affect self-employment income and tax documentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-332ea40a8706fdd85456078cf47232fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
