</node>
<node id="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rental Income is money earned from renting out properties, which must be documented through Schedule E when evaluating a borrower's financial status for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income is the earnings received from renting out property, which is a critical factor in evaluating a borrower's loan application."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to earnings received by landlords from renting out properties, subject to various documentation and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to the earnings derived from renting out properties, which can impact loan qualification processes in real estate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to the earnings generated from leasing out property, which is key for borrowers to demonstrate financial viability in loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to the earnings generated from renting out property, which is analyzed in mortgage underwriting processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to the earnings generated from renting properties, which are evaluated during the underwriting process to determine a borrower's financial qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to the earnings that a property owner receives from tenants renting their property, which can affect qualifying decisions in loans and mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to the money collected from renting out real estate properties, which is evaluated under specific guidelines for mortgage qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to the money received by the property owner from renting out a residential or commercial property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income represents the earnings generated from renting out property, which can affect mortgage qualifications and borrower analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental income refers to money received from leasing out properties, such as real estate or other assets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-10ce55972cf12e21fd77796ab69a96ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea98d6086733276bdd5c19993c4deb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b454650a6e8dde5a93325db30813c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8864c52069485823a39babaa2b2005e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb02bde5abfff1b16d83434416df7465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79943296a1fa68394820a29e269db689&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a01c4d224477788cf5c6bfd6ccc84e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 118}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 360}]</data>
