<node id="&quot;NET RENTAL INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Net Rental Income is the income generated from renting a property after accounting for expenses, essential for financial assessments within mortgage guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Net Rental Income is the income remaining after deducting expenses related to vacancies and maintenance from Gross Rental Income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Net Rental Income is the total income from renting out properties after deducting expenses such as maintenance and vacancy losses, impacting borrowers' financial assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb02bde5abfff1b16d83434416df7465</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 119}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CURRENT LEASE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Current Lease Agreement is a contract outlining the terms under which a property is rented, crucial for verifying rental income history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Current Lease Agreement is a contract outlining the terms under which a property is rented, including rental amount and duration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Current Lease Agreement refers to the document that outlines the terms of rent between the landlord and tenant, required for evaluating rental income."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532</data>
