<node id="&quot;FEDERAL INCOME TAX RETURN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Federal Income Tax Return is a filing used by individuals to report income and other financial information to the government, relevant for income verification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Federal Income Tax Return is a government form used by businesses and individuals to report income, expenses, and other tax-related information to the IRS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Federal Income Tax Return is a legal document required for verifying a borrower's income and tax obligations, including rental income and expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Federal Income Tax Return is the annual report filed with the government that details an individual's income, including various schedules used for reporting rental income."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Federal Income Tax Return is a government form filed annually by individuals and businesses to report their income, expenses, and other tax information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b454650a6e8dde5a93325db30813c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb02bde5abfff1b16d83434416df7465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
