  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fair Rental Days are used to determine the number of days a property is rented out during the year, impacting rental income reporting on tax schedules like Schedule E."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fair Rental Days is the number of days a rental property was actively rented out, used to assess financial data and compliance with loan terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fair Rental Days refers to the number of days a property has been rented out during the year, which influences rental income calculations and eligibility."</data>
