<node id="&quot;ACCESSORY DWELLING UNIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU) refers to a secondary housing unit on a property that can generate rental income, subject to specific zoning and land use requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Accessory Dwelling Units are secondary living spaces that must adhere to specific guidelines, including size and design standards, to be considered acceptable."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU) refers to a secondary housing unit on a single-family residential lot, which must meet specific appraisal and zoning requirements as outlined by Freddie Mac."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Accessory Dwelling Unit is a secondary housing unit on a property that may not be included in the financing for a manufactured home."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b454650a6e8dde5a93325db30813c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 372}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNER-OCCUPIED PRIMARY RESIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Owner-Occupied Primary Residence refers to the main home where an individual resides, which can impact loan eligibility and rental income considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b454650a6e8dde5a93325db30813c30</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 123}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCESSORY DWELLING UNIT (ADU)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Accessory Dwelling Units (ADUs) are secondary housing units located on the same property as a primary residence, often used for rental income."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU) is a secondary housing unit on a property that provides rental income opportunities and is subject to specific appraisal requirements and zoning regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU) is a secondary housing unit on a single-family lot that can be rented out, subject to legal and zoning requirements, and is significant in the context of rental income guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU) is a secondary housing unit on a single-family residential lot, which can be rented out to generate income, and is subject to specific appraisal and rental income documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a01c4d224477788cf5c6bfd6ccc84e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea98d6086733276bdd5c19993c4deb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 396}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADU RENTAL ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ADU Rental Analysis is a method used to evaluate the potential rental income from an Accessory Dwelling Unit, supporting income claims against current rental agreements and tax returns."&lt;SEP&gt;"ADU Rental Analysis is the evaluation process used to determine the rental income potential of an Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU), which is necessary when a lease is unavailable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ZONING AND LAND USE REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Zoning and Land Use Requirements refer to legal specifications that dictate how land can be used, which affect the approval of ADUs and rental properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zoning and Land Use Requirements refer to local laws that dictate how properties can be used, which impact whether an ADU is considered legal or permissible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zoning and Land Use Requirements refer to the regulatory framework that governs how property can be used, which must be complied with for ADU rental income to be considered eligible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zoning and land use requirements are legal regulations that dictate how a property can be used, impacting eligibility for financing and development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a01c4d224477788cf5c6bfd6ccc84e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 396}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENTAL MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rental Management refers to the practices and processes involved in maintaining, managing, and overseeing rental properties to ensure profitability and compliance with regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 123}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INVESTMENT PROPERTY MANAGEMENT EXPERIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EXPERIENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Investment Property Management Experience refers to the knowledge and skills a borrower must have in managing rental properties, which can exempt them from certain educational requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 123}]</data>
