<node id="&quot;COMPARABLE RENTALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comparable Rentals are similar rental properties used as benchmarks to determine market rents for other units."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7a01c4d224477788cf5c6bfd6ccc84e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 127}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ADU, or Accessory Dwelling Unit, is a secondary housing unit that can be rented out and requires specific appraisal and zoning information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7a01c4d224477788cf5c6bfd6ccc84e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 377}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VACANCIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Vacancies indicate periods when a rental property is unoccupied, affecting the calculation of net rental income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vacancies refer to unoccupied rental properties, which can affect rental income and overall profitability of property investments."</data>
