<node id="&quot;ORDINARY BUSINESS INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ordinary Business Income refers to the regular income a business earns from its operations, excluding gains from investments or one-time events."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 122}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEPRECIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Depreciation is a method of allocating the cost of a tangible asset over its useful life, affecting income calculations in financial assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depreciation is an accounting method of allocating the cost of a tangible asset over its useful life, impacting business cash flow calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873</data>
