</node>
<node id="&quot;AMORTIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amortization is the process of gradually paying off a debt over time through regular payments, which affects financial assessments in underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 122}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLUID ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fluid Assets refer to assets that can quickly be converted into cash without significant loss in value, important for business liquidity evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 122}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OBLIGATIONS ON MORTGAGES OR NOTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Obligations on Mortgages or Notes refer to the responsibilities to pay back borrowed funds secured by collateral, typically property or assets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 122}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUICK RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Quick Ratio is a financial metric used to assess a business's ability to meet its short-term obligations, excluding inventory from current assets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quick Ratio is a financial metric used to evaluate a company's ability to meet its short-term liabilities with its most liquid assets, excluding inventory."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quick Ratio is a financial metric used to evaluate a company's short-term liquidity by measuring the proportion of current assets available to meet current liabilities, excluding inventory."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76dfd0d1478f77acd572a51bf4e3956a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 126}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKING CAPITAL RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Working Capital Ratio is a financial measure that assesses a company's operational liquidity by comparing current assets to current liabilities, applicable for businesses not relying on inventory."&lt;SEP&gt;"Working Capital Ratio is a financial metric that measures a company's efficiency and short-term financial health, calculated as current assets divided by current liabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Working Capital Ratio measures a company's ability to pay off its current liabilities with its current assets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76dfd0d1478f77acd572a51bf4e3956a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 126}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CURRENT RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Current Ratio is a liquidity ratio that measures a company's ability to pay short-term obligations with its current assets, calculated as current assets divided by current liabilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 126}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSONAL RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
