</node>
<node id="&quot;MAY 31&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"May 31 marks a deadline for submitting federal tax forms and supporting documentation, as outlined in the relevant IRS guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddb3009468a2e7eaa9aab8998eae8ca6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 38}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 260}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAXPAYER IDENTIFICATION THEFT VICTIMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Taxpayer Identification Theft Victims are individuals who have had their personal tax information compromised, leading to significant challenges in validating their tax returns."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddb3009468a2e7eaa9aab8998eae8ca6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 37}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IRS GET TRANSCRIPT APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The IRS Get Transcript Application is a digital service provided by the IRS that allows taxpayers to request and receive their tax transcript electronically."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddb3009468a2e7eaa9aab8998eae8ca6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 35}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 249}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CUSTOMER SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The IRS Customer Service provides assistance and support to taxpayers regarding their inquiries and issues associated with tax filings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 257}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCESSORY DWELLING UNITS (ADU)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Accessory Dwelling Units are additional living spaces that provide facilities for living, sleeping, cooking, and bathrooms, allowable in certain property scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;W2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"W2 forms are tax documents provided by employers indicating an employee's annual earnings and the taxes withheld from their paychecks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1099&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1099 forms are used to report various types of income other than wages, salaries, and tips to the IRS."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY AND APPRAISAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property and Appraisal refers to the evaluation of properties to determine their market value and ensure they meet mortgage financing requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YEAR END PAYSTUB&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Year End Paystub provides a summary of an employee's earnings and deductions for the entire year, typically used to verify income."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAX ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tax Accounts refer to financial records related to the taxes owed or paid by individuals or businesses, which are managed by the IRS."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 35}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 249}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REJECT CODE 10&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reject Code 10 indicates a situation in which the IRS cannot provide tax transcripts due to potential identity theft on a taxpayer's account."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 255}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME VERIFICATION EXPRESS SERVICE (IVES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income Verification Express Service (IVES) is a program used by the IRS to provide tax return information to authorized lenders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAXPAYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Taxpayer refers to an individual or entity who is obligated to pay taxes to a governmental authority."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDITIONAL LIVING SPACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additional Living Space describes any area within a property that is designed for residential purposes beyond the primary dwelling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAILED NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mailed Notice refers to a notification sent by the IRS to inform taxpayers about the status of their tax requests or issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 255}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKETABILITY OF PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Marketability of Property refers to how easily a property can be sold in the real estate market, often influenced by its features and external conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPARABLE PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comparable Property is a similar property in the same area used to assess the value of a subject property during appraisal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comparable Property is a similar real estate asset used in appraisals to determine the value of the subject property through comparison."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ZONING REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Zoning Requirements are regulations that dictate how properties can be used in specific areas, affecting the classification and legality of accessory dwelling units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zoning Requirements dictate how land can be used, influencing property development and permitted activities based on local regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 372}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUD REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HUD Regulations refer to guidelines established by the Department of Housing and Urban Development, governing various housing standards, including those related to manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 372}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KITCHEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The kitchen is a fundamental component of living spaces, mandated to include specific features such as cabinets, a countertop, sink with running water, and a stove."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 372}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Utilities refer to essential services such as water and electricity that must be separately metered for properties with accessory dwelling units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Utilities refer to essential services such as water, electricity, and gas, which are often included in the operating expenses associated with leasehold agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 115}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIMARY DWELLING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The primary dwelling is the main residential structure on a property, which accessory dwelling units must be subordinate to in size and value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 372}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOUNDATION SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The foundation system is the structural base that supports a manufactured home, requiring specific standards for safety and stability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 372}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEDERAL MANUFACTURED HOME CONSTRUCTION AND SAFETY STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These standards, established on June 16, 1976, outline the safety and construction requirements for manufactured homes in the U.S."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 371}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MULTI-UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Multi-Unit Properties are buildings designed to house multiple separate dwelling units, which have specific eligibility criteria in mortgage lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multi-unit properties are real estate structures that contain more than one separate living unit, which can influence appraisal and zoning considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 380}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEIGHBORHOOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Neighborhood refers to the geographic area surrounding a subject property, affecting its marketability and valuation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neighborhood refers to the local area where properties are located, impacting real estate market conditions and trends in property values."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neighborhood refers to the surrounding area of a property that can affect its market value and appeal, influenced by factors like crime rates and desirability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neighborhood refers to the surrounding area of a property, which can affect the marketability and compliance of accessory dwelling units."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Neighborhood is the area surrounding the subject property, which has specific characteristics relevant to property valuation and market comparisons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98fca990e6b71624308defbc9fca0285&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 390}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUD CERTIFICATION LABEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The HUD Certification Label is a marker affixed to manufactured homes confirming compliance with federal standards, crucial for appraisals and eligibility in loan processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The HUD Certification Label is a metal plate affixed to manufactured homes that verifies compliance with safety standards, essential for loan qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 386}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL REQUIREMENTS FOR MANUFACTURED HOME ACCESSORY UNITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Appraisal Requirements for Manufactured Home Accessory Units detail the necessary steps and standards that must be adhered to when appraising such properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 371}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATE OF MANUFACTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Date of Manufacture refers to the specific date a manufactured home was constructed, which is critical for compliance and valuation assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 399}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDITION WITHOUT PERMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additions Without Permits refer to any modifications made to a property that lack the required official documentation, affecting evaluation and compliance during appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 396}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANUFACTURED HOME STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Manufactured Home Standards are regulations that ensure safety, durability, and quality of manufactured homes, affecting appraisal evaluations and loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 396}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ONE-UNIT PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"One-Unit Property refers to a type of residential property consisting of a single housing unit, which is subject to specific appraisal guidelines in relation to accessory dwelling units."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Utility refers to the usefulness and functionality of a property, especially concerning how well it serves its intended purpose in relation to market value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 394}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA PLATE/COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Data Plate/Compliance Certificate is documentation affixed to manufactured homes certifying compliance with construction and safety standards, essential for appraisal and lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 386}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL DESCRIPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Description is a formal description of a property that defines its boundaries and identifies its location in legal documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal Description is a formal description of a property's boundaries and characteristics as specified in legal documents, important for verifying property details against title commitments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal Description is a formal way of describing real property that includes specific details necessary for its identification in transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 512}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUD PLATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The HUD Plate is a label on manufactured homes that indicates it has been built to federal standards, necessary for compliance verification during appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f562ac717c24b9fccfb1aab0164fb157</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 399}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USPAP GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"USPAP guidelines refer to the standards for professional appraisal practice, ensuring quality and integrity in appraisal reports."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOANTRAC APPRAISAL MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loantrac Appraisal Management is referenced as the entity through which appraisals must be ordered for compliance with Flagstar Bank's requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 408}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNIQUE PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unique Properties refer to real estate that has distinctive characteristics requiring comparables with similar uniqueness for proper valuation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 152}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL WAIVER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Appraisal Waiver is an approval from a lender allowing a buyer to skip the traditional appraisal process under certain conditions to expedite closing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal Waiver is a feature that allows certain loans to close without a full appraisal process, reducing time and costs for the borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal Waiver is a process that allows certain loan transactions to occur without a traditional appraisal, streamlining the mortgage approval process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal Waiver refers to a circumstance where eligibility for a mortgage can be established without a traditional property appraisal, as part of processes from organizations like Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal Waiver refers to specific circumstances under which a property may not need a formal appraisal, allowing for expedited loan processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal Waiver refers to the process allowing certain transactions to proceed without a traditional appraisal under specified conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4de71275bc933c2c228984f601d0e0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-645973893eaf0e8d2eb4a7822c3fe6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb9a9047b04f55e775ab1675823f162</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 348}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL PORTABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraisal Portability is the process that allows appraisal reports to be used across different lenders, ensuring flexibility in property evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIOR AND EXTERIOR INSPECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interior and Exterior Inspection describes the requirement for appraisals to include physical evaluations of properties for accuracy and compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 182}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Standards refer to regulations that govern the minimum requirements for electric power access and other local protocols regarding solar energy systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Standards refer to the expectations and regulations in a locality regarding the utilities and safety of properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Standards refer to the guidelines and regulations that dictate acceptable sources of electric power and energy production in a given area, relevant for properties with solar panels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 182}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPARABLES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comparables are properties comparable to the subject property used in determining its appraised value based on market data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comparables are properties similar to the subject property that are used to determine its market value by comparison based on sales data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comparables are properties that are similar in nature to a subject property used for valuation purposes in appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-137c762b3ac588b243786790757dd239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 152}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNIT NUMBER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unit Number refers to the specific identification of units within multi-unit properties, important in legal documentation and appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 512}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDENDUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Addendum refers to supplemental documentation required to clarify legal addresses in property appraisals and transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 512}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISER INDEPENDENCE COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraiser Independence Compliance ensures that appraisal processes are conducted without undue influence from interested parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d1c3e36c841bdc1a7ede120ae160e58</data>
