  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME APPROACH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Income Approach is a valuation method that assesses property value based on the income it generates, particularly relevant for rental properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 148}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPARABLE SALES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comparable Sales are sales of similar properties in the vicinity used to determine the value of the subject property during appraisal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comparable Sales are used in real estate appraisal to determine the value of a property by comparing it to similar properties that have recently sold."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comparable Sales refer to properties that are similar to the subject property and are used as benchmarks in the appraisal process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comparable Sales refer to sales of similar properties that are used by appraisers to determine the market value of the subject property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 391}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VALUATION RECONCILIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Valuation Reconciliation refers to the process of integrating various appraisal approaches to arrive at a final value for a property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 148}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2-4 UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"2-4 Unit Properties are residential properties that contain two to four individual living units, often used for rental income."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPANCY APPRAISAL FORM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Occupancy Appraisal Form is a required form that documents the occupancy status of a property during the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET APPROACH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Market Approach is a valuation method that considers the prices of comparable properties to estimate the value of the subject property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 148}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENTAL MARKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rental Market refers to the supply and demand conditions for rental properties in a given area, influencing property values."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 148}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DECLINING MARKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Declining Market describes an area where property values are decreasing, impacting the appraisal process and comparable sales selection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Declining Market refers to an economic condition where property values are decreasing, impacting the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24638398312c4aec93c00e795739cbf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 391}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPARATIVE MARKET DATA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comparative Market Data refers to the sales data used by appraisers to evaluate the market value of properties in relation to similar properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 398}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Records are official documents or pieces of information that are maintained by government agencies and are generally accessible to the public."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBDIVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subdivision refers to a tract of land that has been divided into smaller parcels for the purpose of development and sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 152}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET ACCEPTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Market Acceptance refers to the acknowledgment and validation by the market of a certain property ownership type, indicating its desirability and viability in financial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Acceptance refers to the degree to which new developments or properties are accepted by potential buyers in the market."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 152}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINGENT LISTINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contingent Listings are properties that have accepted offers but are still subject to certain conditions before the sale is finalized."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LISTING HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Listing History provides a record of the dates and prices at which a property has been listed for sale, crucial for appraisal analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Listing History refers to the record of a property’s previous listings, including dates and prices, which provides insights for appraisal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 398}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RURAL PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rural Properties are real estate located in less densely populated areas, which may present unique challenges in comparative analysis due to fewer recent sales."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 391}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES PRICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Prices are the final prices at which properties are sold, which are used as a reference in the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA SOURCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Data Sources refer to the various origins of information used to substantiate the appraisal of a property, including market data and listing records."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDO PROJECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Condo Projects refer to real estate developments featuring condominium units, highlighting the emerging market trends and requirements for appraisals in these units."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 407}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ESTABLISHED CONDOMINIUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Established Condominium refers to a residential property type that has been in existence for a while, influencing appraisal processes based on historical market data."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 390}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBJECT SUBDIVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subject Subdivision denotes a housing development or area where the subject property is located, impacting its market value based on sales data from comparable properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 397}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT SALES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract Sales refer to property sales that are agreed upon but not yet closed, which can be used for appraisal comparisons under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 397}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPARABLE PROJECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comparable Projects are similar developments that can be referenced in the appraisal process to assess the value of the subject property based on available sales data."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 391}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UPGRADES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Upgrades refer to improvements made to a property that can enhance its value and marketability, and their impact must be analyzed in appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42fe7768b333d42fc15f00fc4e0ba0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 179}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 444}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"MLS, or Multiple Listing Service, is a service used by real estate brokers to disseminate listings of properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY-OWNED OR PRIVATELY MAINTAINED STREETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community-owned or privately maintained streets refer to roads that are not publicly owned and require specific agreements for maintenance and management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 209}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 510}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEIGHBORHOOD ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Neighborhood Analysis is a process by appraisers to evaluate the market dynamics and influences affecting property values within a specific area."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 410}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES COMPARISON ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Comparison Analysis is a method used by appraisers to determine a property's value by comparing it to similar properties that have recently sold."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 410}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBJECT NEIGHBORHOOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subject Neighborhood refers to the specific area being appraised, which is evaluated by the appraiser to understand the supply and demand dynamics affecting property values."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 410}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEIGHBORHOOD BOUNDARIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Neighborhood Boundaries are the limits that define the area subject to market influences and the evaluation of comparable properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 410}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGALLY ENFORCEABLE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legally Enforceable Agreement refers to a contract that outlines the responsibilities and rights of parties involved in maintaining shared property, such as streets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 209}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 510}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPAIRS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Repairs describe the actions required to maintain or restore property, especially in the context of ownership agreements for private streets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Repairs refer to the necessary work done to restore or enhance a property, which is subject to completion deadlines and conditions in the context of financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Repairs refer to the various actions taken to fix or improve properties, which are assessed for their impact on livability and structural soundness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed0db69e97fa62c70a7cb29c5e75fe07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00440a55cc64896de959c80a8727fbfc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 209}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 511}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES TO THE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties to the Agreement are the individuals or entities involved in the maintenance of the community-owned or privately maintained streets as outlined in a covenant."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 209}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 510}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUTORY PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statutory Provisions refer to the laws that govern the responsibilities of property owners regarding the maintenance and repair of private streets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d83092219c6a0be0948a52ad38b945a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 209}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 510}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTAMINATED SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Contaminated Site refers to any location where hazardous substances may have been released, potentially affecting property value and safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Contaminated Site refers to properties that have been affected by hazardous substances, which must be considered during property appraisals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contaminated Site refers to a location where hazardous substances have been released, which can adversely affect the surrounding environment and property values."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contaminated Site refers to a piece of land that has been polluted by hazardous substances, requiring careful assessment and remediation prior to property transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contaminated site refers to real estate locations with environmental issues that can influence appraisal decisions and loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefb0ad4148eab93b794bfdc3eb3eac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4de71275bc933c2c228984f601d0e0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HAZARDOUS SUBSTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hazardous Substance refers to any material that could pose a risk to health, property, or the environment, necessitating immediate disclosure during property transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hazardous Substances are materials capable of causing harm to human health or the environment, often influencing real estate marketability and appraisal values."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hazardous substance indicates materials that pose risks to health or the environment, affecting property transactions and appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4de71275bc933c2c228984f601d0e0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EFFECTIVE AGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Effective Age is a term used in appraisals to describe the estimated age of a property based on its condition and improvements, which may differ from its actual age."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 393}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROSS LIVING AREA (GLA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gross Living Area (GLA) is a measurement used in real estate to determine the total finished area of a residential property, relevant in appraisals and valuations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gross Living Area (GLA) refers to the total square footage of a property's living space, excluding areas not typically used for living purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JOINT DRIVEWAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A joint driveway is a common access way shared between two or more properties, which requires legal agreements regarding its use and maintenance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-REALTY ITEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-realty items refer to any items included in a transaction which are not part of the real property, such as furnishings or appliances, that may affect appraisal value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 301}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATION AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subordination agreements are legal documents outlining the priority of claims or liens against a property, often influencing mortgage transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sale price is the final agreed amount for which a property is sold, critical in determinations of value and appraisal considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 104}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 344}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSACTION TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transaction terms encompass all conditions affecting a sale, including price, financing, and contingencies, essential for assessing the overall agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 104}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 344}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EASEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Easement is a legal right allowing an individual or entity to use someone else's property for a specified purpose, often related to utilities or access."&lt;SEP&gt;"An easement is a legal right to use another person's land for a specific limited purpose, often relevant in property transactions involving shared resources like driveways."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUSTMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjustments refer to modifications made in an appraisal process to account for differences between comparable properties and subject properties, impacting value assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 393}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCING INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financing information includes detailed data on loan terms, rates, costs, and conditions that are essential for evaluating mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 86}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKETABILITY FACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Marketability factors are specific elements that influence the ease and speed with which a property can be sold in the current real estate market."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 394}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINOR CLERICAL ERRORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minor clerical errors refer to small, often insignificant mistakes in documents that do not affect the material terms of agreements or contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amendments are formal changes or additions made to an existing agreement, often affecting contracts but may not always require reappraising when non-material."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY LEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property leases are contractual agreements outlining the terms under which one party rents property from another, impacting value and market considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPOSED CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proposed changes refer to planned modifications to property use or structure that may influence an appraisal or sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 390}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL EVALUATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial evaluations refer to the detailed analysis of financial health related to property transactions, impacting appraisal reports and decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ESTIMATION PROCESSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Estimation processes involve the methods utilized by appraisers to determine property values based on various metrics and comparables."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f443d70c1b97ab92c6f9f441ec9ced99</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMERICAN NATIONAL STANDARDS INSTITUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The American National Standards Institute (ANSI) is a private non-profit organization that oversees and coordinates the development of voluntary consensus standards for various sectors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANSI STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ANSI Standards serve as guidelines for measuring and reporting gross living area in property appraisals, ensuring consistency and accuracy in assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SQUARE FOOTAGE-METHOD FOR CALCULATING ANSI STANDARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Square Footage-Method for Calculating ANSI standard is a specific guideline for determining the square footage of living areas in property appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDING SKETCHES OR FLOOR PLANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Building Sketches or Floor Plans are computer-generated representations required for appraisals, showing dimensions and layout of the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES COMPARISON APPROACH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Comparison Approach is a method used by appraisers to determine property value based on analysis of comparable sales, ensuring accurate market reflection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Sales Comparison Approach is a method used in property appraisal, involving comparisons with similar properties to determine value adjustments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUSTMENTS FOR BELOW-GRADE AREAS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjustments for below-grade areas involve evaluating the impact of non-gross living areas, such as basements, on a property's overall value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETURN TO MENU&quot;">
