</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL REQUIRING INTERIOR AND EXTERIOR INSPECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An appraisal requiring interior and exterior inspections involves evaluating a property both inside and outside, ensuring comprehensive assessment standards are met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDITIONAL STRUCTURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additional structures refer to any extra buildings or features on a property that are not considered part of the main living area in the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIOR AND EXTERIOR INSPECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interior and exterior inspections are thorough examinations of a property’s features, ensuring compliance with appraisal standards for lending purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ABOVE-GRADE ROOM COUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Above-grade room count refers to the measurement and evaluation of rooms that are located above the ground level in a property, which are typically included in the Gross Living Area."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BASEMENT &amp; FINISHED ROOMS BELOW-GRADE LINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Basement &amp; Finished Rooms Below-Grade line is a specific entry in appraisal reports used to indicate the contribution of basement areas to the property's overall value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINISHED ABOVE-GRADE AREAS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Finished above-grade areas are parts of a property that are completed and located above the ground level, essential for calculating Gross Living Area."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLOOR PLANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Floor Plans are detailed drawings that illustrate the layout and dimensions of a building or unit, essential for property appraisal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Floor plans are detailed layouts of a property, providing spatial arrangements and dimensions necessary for appraisals and market evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 402}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIMENSIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dimensions refer to the measurements of spaces within a property, critical for accurately reporting square footage in appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTERIOR WALLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Exterior walls are the outer walls of a building, which play a significant role in the structure's integrity and are included in appraisal measurements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABELS FOR EACH ROOM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Labels for each room are annotations included in floor plans to specify the function and identification of different areas within the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1eb0558635c4f1b731b5f38c1ed9bb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL REPORTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraisal Reports refer to documents that provide an opinion of market value for properties, crucial for mortgage lending processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 401}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VALUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Valuation is the analytical process of determining the current worth of a property, critical for real estate transactions and lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 402}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraisers are professionals who assess property value, ensuring compliance with established guidelines and ethical practices in appraisal reporting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 401}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROTECTED CLASS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Protected Class refers to groups of people whose rights are safeguarded from discrimination in housing and real estate practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 402}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDO OR CO-OP PROJECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Condo or Co-op Project refers to a type of residential property arrangement where units are owned individually while sharing ownership of common areas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 402}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GBA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GBA, or Gross Building Area, refers to the total constructed area of a building, including all spaces within the exterior walls."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 401}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SQUARE FEET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Square Feet is a unit of area measurement commonly used in real estate to quantify the size of a property or space."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 402}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPETITIVE PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Competitive Properties are similar real estate assets that are used as benchmarks for assessing the value of the subject property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 389}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADVERSE INFLUENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adverse Influences are negative factors that can reduce the desirability or market value of a property, such as proximity to unpleasant surroundings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 401}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES COMPARABLES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Comparables refer to similar properties that have recently sold and are used as benchmarks for pricing and valuing the subject property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 401}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSONAL INSPECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Personal Inspection is the act of physically examining a property to assess its condition, features, and other factors relevant to valuation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e98d878b21daedfefbf36b036612418f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 401}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USPAP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"USPAP stands for the Uniform Standards of Professional Appraisal Practice, which provides guidelines for appraisers to ensure consistent and ethical practices in property valuations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 396}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COASTAL TIDELAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Coastal Tideland refers to properties subject to specific land-use regulations designed to manage development and environmental concerns in coastal areas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WETLANDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wetlands are areas that are subject to zoning laws and regulations that impact property use and development potential, particularly in relation to environmental conservation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE/VIEW ADJUSTMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site/View Adjustments are necessary considerations taken by appraisers to ensure that the appraisal reflects the entire property's value based on actual size and comparables."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WELL AND SEPTIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Well and Septic refers to systems used for water supply and waste management on properties, with specific testing requirements in environmental contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOLAR PANELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Solar Panels are devices that convert sunlight into electricity and are discussed in the context of their ownership and installation agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Solar Panels are devices that convert sunlight into electricity, and can be owned, leased, or financed with respect to property ownership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Solar Panels are devices that convert sunlight into electricity, commonly used in residential and commercial energy systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Solar Panels are devices that convert sunlight into electricity, integral to the solar power system and often subject to financing and marketability appraisals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Solar Panels are renewable energy products considered in property appraisals, with implications for ownership and financing structures related to real estate investments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Solar panels are devices that convert sunlight into electricity and are subject to specific financing agreements that dictate their status as personal or real property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-645973893eaf0e8d2eb4a7822c3fe6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb9a9047b04f55e775ab1675823f162</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 412}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPARABLE SALES DATA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comparable Sales Data is critical for appraisals, assessing value through sales data from similar properties and ensuring accurate market representation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-CONFORMING PROPERTY USE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-conforming Property Use refers to properties using land in a manner that doesn't comply with current zoning regulations, affecting appraised value and marketability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL HAZARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Environmental Hazards are factors that can impact the value of properties, specifically in relation to health and safety considerations, particularly concerning well and septic systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGHEST AND BEST USE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Highest and Best Use is the optimal use of a property that maximizes its potential value under current zoning and land-use regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME ADJUSTMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Time Adjustments are modifications made during appraisals to account for changes in market conditions over time, ensuring accurate property valuations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 400}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES COMPARISON APPROACH TO VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Comparison Approach to Value is a fundamental valuation method that appraisers employ to determine property worth based on comparable sales trends."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCOPE OF WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Scope of Work refers to the specific tasks and responsibilities outlined in an appraisal assignment to ensure compliance with industry standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 393}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUSTED VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjusted Value is the modified worth of a property after accounting for differences between it and comparable properties in the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN-TO-VALUE CALCULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan-to-Value Calculations are financial assessments comparing the amount of a loan to the appraised value of a property, pivotal in mortgage underwriting decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compensation relates to the financial remuneration an appraiser may anticipate for their services, potentially influencing their appraisal outcome."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 400}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSPECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Inspection is the process used to evaluate properties for their condition and the presence of factors such as drilling or fracking activities that could affect value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inspection refers to the process of examining a property, particularly after repairs, to confirm that all work has been completed satisfactorily."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inspection refers to the process of examining a property’s physical state as part of the appraisal procedure to ensure all relevant factors are assessed accurately."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00440a55cc64896de959c80a8727fbfc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 394}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL INTEREST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial Interest pertains to any vested interest a party might have in a property transaction, potentially impacting the integrity of appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 400}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES DATA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Data refers to historical records of property transactions used in performing comparative analysis during the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 400}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUTURE ASSIGNMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Future Assignments indicate potential subsequent appraisal tasks that may be influenced by the outcomes of current property evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADVERSE EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adverse Effect describes negative impacts non-conforming property usage may have on the value and marketability of real estate."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bd684789b748cb20186f7859db539838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UCC-1 FINANCING STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A UCC-1 Financing Statement is a legal form that a creditor files to give notice that it has an interest in the personal property of a debtor, such as solar panels."&lt;SEP&gt;"UCC-1 Financing Statement is a financial document used to secure interests in solar panels and related property as recorded in applicable land records."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 412}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY LEASE PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Monthly Lease Payments refer to the consistent payments made by a borrower to access solar panels without owning them outright."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 120}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 363}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COLLATERAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Collateral refers to an asset that a borrower offers to a lender to secure a loan, in this case, possibly involving solar panels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAND RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Land Records are official documents that provide information about property ownership and rights, which are pertinent in determining the status of solar panels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Land Records are official documents where property transactions, including mortgages and deeds of trust, are recorded to verify ownership and financing details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 514}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOLAR POWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Solar Power refers to the energy generated by harnessing sunlight through the use of solar panels and related technology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Solar Power refers to the technology harnessing energy from the sun through solar panels and systems to provide electricity and reduce reliance on traditional power sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Solar Power refers to the technology that harnesses energy from the sun using solar panels for electricity generation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-645973893eaf0e8d2eb4a7822c3fe6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 412}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOLAR PANEL FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Solar Panel Financing encompasses various options available for consumers to acquire solar panels, including leases, direct purchases, and power purchase agreements (PPAs)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POWER PURCHASE AGREEMENT (PPA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) is a contract between a buyer and a seller for the purchase of electricity generated by solar panels, typically at a predetermined rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Power Purchase Agreement is a contract to purchase electricity from a renewable energy project, detailing the terms of energy supply and responsibilities related to equipment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb9a9047b04f55e775ab1675823f162</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 413}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNERSHIP STRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ownership Structure pertains to the arrangement of legal rights regarding who owns the solar panels, whether outright or through financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCING STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Financing Statement is a legal form used by creditors to secure an interest in the borrower's assets, such as solar panels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEBT PAYMENT-TO-INCOME RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Debt payment-to-income ratio (DTI) is a financial measure used to evaluate a borrower's ability to manage monthly payments and is affected by solar panel lease payments if certain conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 358}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PPA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PPA, or Power Purchase Agreement, is a contractual arrangement between a provider and user of solar energy detailing the terms of energy delivery and payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"PPA, or Power Purchase Agreement, is a financial contract in which a developer of a solar power system agrees to sell power to a buyer, influencing financial terms in property assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 412}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DTI RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The DTI ratio is a financial measurement used to evaluate a borrower's debt compared to their income, with implications for mortgage approval when solar panels are involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY STANDARDS ON ELECTRIC POWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Standards on Electric Power dictate the acceptable sources and standards for energy production within a given community, impacting properties with solar panels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSONAL FIXTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Personal Fixture refers to components such as solar panels that may be classified as personal property or real property based on ownership and financing terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 358}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENERGY PRODUCTION GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Energy Production Guarantee is a provision ensuring that the energy produced by solar panels meets specified thresholds, providing security to the borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy Production Guarantee is a term used in solar panel leasing agreements that ensures a certain level of energy output, affecting financing and compensation agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 358}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ALTERNATE SOURCE OF ELECTRIC POWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Alternate Source of Electric Power refers to backup or supplementary energy sources required for properties with solar panels to meet community standards and avoid disqualification from financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 182}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOTAL LOAN-TO-VALUE RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Total Loan-to-Value Ratio (TLTV) is a financial metric used to assess the risk of a loan relative to the value of the property, particularly in real estate transactions involving solar panel financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 412}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UCC FILING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL TERM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"UCC Filing refers to the process of recording a secured loan agreement against real property, which can include solar panels, ensuring the lender's interest is legally protected."&lt;SEP&gt;"UCC filing refers to a legal document submitted to secure loans through filing against real property or personal property in relation to solar panel agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb9a9047b04f55e775ab1675823f162</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIXTURE TO REAL ESTATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fixture to Real Estate describes items, such as solar panels, that are installed on a property but may have specific financing implications regarding ownership and valuation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOME WITH SOLAR PANELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Home with Solar Panels pertains to residential properties that are equipped with solar energy systems, influencing their marketability and value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 394}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFAULT ON FINANCING TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Default on Financing Terms refers to the failure to meet the obligations outlined in a financial agreement, which can lead to repossession of solar panels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 32}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMEOWNER’S INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Homeowner’s Insurance is a type of insurance policy that provides financial protection to homeowners covering potential losses to their property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3eb9a9047b04f55e775ab1675823f162</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 413}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISER INDEPENDENCE COMPLIANCE GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraiser Independence Compliance Guidelines set standards to ensure that appraisals are conducted without bias or conflict of interest in real estate transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3eb9a9047b04f55e775ab1675823f162</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 407}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELIGIBILITY FOR USE OF AN APPRAISAL WAIVER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Eligibility for Use of an Appraisal Waiver describes the conditions under which a borrower may skip a formal appraisal process in the lending context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3eb9a9047b04f55e775ab1675823f162</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 411}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL COLLATERAL EVALUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraisal Collateral Evaluation (ACE) is a system developed by Freddie Mac to streamline the appraisal process in mortgage lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal Collateral Evaluation is a technology-based approach used by lenders like Freddie Mac to determine property value without a full appraisal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-645973893eaf0e8d2eb4a7822c3fe6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb9a9047b04f55e775ab1675823f162</data>
