</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNER OCCUPIED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Owner Occupied refers to properties that are inhabited by the owner, distinguishing them from rental or investment properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Owner Occupied signifies properties where the owner lives in the residence, often affecting loan conditions and terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Owner occupied refers to properties where the owner resides, impacting their eligibility for various refinancing options and appraisal waivers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-645973893eaf0e8d2eb4a7822c3fe6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4de71275bc933c2c228984f601d0e0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 131}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH-NEED RURAL LOCATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High-Need Rural locations refer to areas identified by FHFA where certain properties may have specific appraisal waiver requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PIW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PIW, or Property Inspection Waiver, is a specific type of appraisal waiver offered by Fannie Mae for eligible properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACE/PIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ACE/PIA refers to Freddie Mac's Automated Collateral Evaluation and Property Inspection Alternative, providing appraisal waivers under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENOVATION MORTGAGE PRODUCTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renovation mortgage products are financial options that allow homeowners to finance the purchase and renovation of properties within a single mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renovation mortgage products are loan options designed for properties undergoing renovation, mentioned in the context of appraisal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-388d67b329a7c9987f1aa1ce87dad2a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
