<node id="&quot;1-UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1-unit properties refer to residential properties that consist of a single housing unit, applicable under specific mortgage and appraisal guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SECOND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Second is a type of financial assistance used in affordable housing programs to subsidize the sales price of properties for buyers, making housing more accessible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Second is a type of second mortgage designed to assist with home purchase financing, often associated with affordable housing initiatives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Second is a type of subordinate loan used to subsidize the sales price of a property for borrowers, often deferred and forgiven after a set period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 448}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DU - DESKTOP UNDERWRITER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DU stands for Desktop Underwriter, a technology platform used by lenders to assess mortgage loan applications and determine eligibility for products like appraisal waivers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL TYPE PIW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PIW stands for Property Inspection Waiver, an appraisal type that allows for certain transactions to proceed without a formal appraisal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPANCY OWNER OCCUPIED ONLY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Owner Occupied only refers to the occupancy requirement for properties eligible for the appraisal waiver, meaning they must be occupied by the owner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFESSIONAL INSPECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Professional Inspector refers to an accredited individual who conducts property inspections, ensuring they meet state licensing and insurance requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;50(A)(6) LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"50(a)(6) loans refer to a specific type of Texas home equity loan that has particular regulatory requirements around the use of appraisal waivers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION OR CONSTRUCTION-TO-PERMANENT TRANSACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction or Construction-to-Permanent Transactions involve financial arrangements for properties being built or transformed, which may also require appraisal waivers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 349}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEASEHOLD PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leasehold properties are those held under a lease agreement, and their eligibility for appraisal waivers is noted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 348}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADVERSE PHYSICAL PROPERTY CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adverse physical property conditions are negative attributes of a property that can impact its value and the need for appraisal processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-ARM'S LENGTH TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-arm's length transaction describes dealings between parties with a pre-existing relationship, which may affect how appraisals are approached."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 459}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REO PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"REO Property refers to real estate owned properties that are in possession of a lender after foreclosure, influencing underwriting and appraisal guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"REO Property refers to real estate owned properties, typically taken back by lenders after foreclosure, influencing subsequent sales and transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
