  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conventional Condominium Guidelines outline the approval criteria necessary for condominium properties related to appraisals and lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTIONAL COOPERATIVE GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conventional Cooperative Guidelines detail rules for approving cooperative properties in the context of appraisals and lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 329}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DETACHED CONDOMINIUMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Detached Condominiums are defined as condo units that are completely separate from other units, affecting how appraisals for such properties might be handled."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VA APPRAISALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"VA Appraisals refer to appraisals specifically ordered for properties in the context of VA loans, which have distinct transfer rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 105}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIGNIFICANT REMODELING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Significant Remodeling refers to major changes made to a property that could impact its valuation, thus affecting the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 390}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CUSTOMER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The customer refers to individuals or entities that request appraisals and engage with the lending process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 393}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE APPRAISAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Appraisal refers to the evaluation of a property's value conducted by a certified appraiser, which is critical in the lending process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Compliance Certificate is a document required from the original lender to show that the appraisal was ordered in compliance with regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Compliance Certificate is a document that confirms a manufactured home's adherence to HUD's safety standards and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 373}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AMC stands for Appraisal Management Company, which is responsible for overseeing the appraisal process and ensuring compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 347}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORIGINAL LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Original Lender is the financial institution that initially orders the appraisal and provides the mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 373}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INELIGIBLE APPRAISER LIST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Ineligible Appraiser List is a record maintained by Flagstar that identifies appraisers who cannot conduct appraisals for them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 351}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY REMODELING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Remodeling involves changes made to a property that can affect its value and thus its appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 13}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 159}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATE OF THE NOTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Date of the Note is the specific date on which the loan agreement becomes effective, influencing the appraisal's relevance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 273}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESALE RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Resale Restrictions are legal limitations placed on a property that affect its sale, determining how and when it can be sold after certain conditions are met, such as foreclosure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resale Restrictions are regulations that limit the sale of properties to maintain affordability, imposed by various organizations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resale Restrictions are stipulations that limit the sale of certain properties to maintain affordability and define eligibility criteria for purchasers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resale Restrictions are the conditions placed on properties that determine how they can be sold, especially in relation to foreclosures and subsidies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resale Restrictions refer to limitations placed on properties to ensure they are available to low-income or moderate-income families, which may involve pricing and occupancy criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resale Restrictions refer to the conditions placed on a property that affect its value and marketability during foreclosure or sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 465}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMEOWNERS ASSOCIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Homeowners Association (HOA) is an organization in a community that creates and enforces rules for property owners, including responsibilities for dues and voting rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Homeowners Association is a group that enforces rules and regulations for residential properties, managing common areas and services among unit holders of condominium projects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeowners Association refers to an organized body managing a planned unit development (PUD), responsible for maintaining community properties and enforcing regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 155}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOW-INCOME BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Low-Income Borrowers are individuals whose financial capabilities restrict them to affordable housing options, often benefiting from targeted programs and subsidies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 465}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODERATE-INCOME BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Moderate-Income Borrowers typically earn more than low-income borrowers but still require assistance in purchasing homes, often involved in programs with resale restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 465}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDOMINIUM PROJECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Condominium Project refers to a development consisting of multiple condo units, which can be either attached or detached, providing shared amenities and governance through a homeowners association."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Condominium Project refers to a type of housing community where units are owned individually but intrude common areas, relevant in mortgage discussions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DETACHED UNITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Detached Units are standalone residential structures within a condominium project, indicating separation from other units and emphasizes individual ownership of both the unit and the land."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSURANCE POLICIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Insurance Policies such as hazard, flood, liability, and fidelity insurance are crucial for protecting properties, ensuring both homeowners and common areas are covered against risks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;&lt;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Mortgage is a financial arrangement where a borrower secures a loan to purchase real estate, with the property itself serving as collateral."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROJECT REVIEW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Project Review refers to the evaluation process that ensures condominium projects meet necessary guidelines and requirements before financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDO-HOTEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Condo-Hotel is a type of property that functions as both a hotel and individual condos, where ownership and vacation rentals coexist, though not acceptable in many mortgage evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COVENANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Covenant is a formal agreement or promise in a deed, regarding the use of property, often dictating terms of ownership and occupancy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 465}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROUND LEASE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Ground Lease Agreement is a long-term lease where the tenant is allowed to develop on the land owned by the lessor, which can have implications for resale restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TITLE INSURANCE POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Title Insurance Policy protects property owners and lenders against losses from disputes over property ownership, essential in real estate transactions including condominiums."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEGMENTED OWNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Segmented Ownership refers to a situation where multiple individuals or entities share ownership of a property, common in certain types of real estate projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSIDY PROVIDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsidy Providers are entities such as nonprofit organizations and churches that offer financial assistance for properties with resale restrictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Subsidy Provider is the entity responsible for administering housing subsidies and managing compliance with affordable housing regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Subsidy Provider refers to an organization or program that offers financial assistance to help reduce the cost of purchasing or maintaining a property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGE-RELATED DEED RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Age-Related Deed Restrictions are conditions that apply to property occupants, typically requiring at least one occupant to be 55 years or older to qualify for certain housing programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 452}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMEREADY MORTGAGE LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HomeReady Mortgage Loans are specific mortgage products offered by Fannie Mae designed to provide accessible financing options for eligible borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 452}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFAULT OR REFINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Default or Refinancing refers to events where borrowers may face foreclosure or wish to refinance their mortgage under specific conditions laid out by subsidy providers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 452}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIXED-RATE OR ADJUSTABLE-RATE MORTGAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fixed-Rate or Adjustable-Rate Mortgages are types of mortgage loans that can be used by borrowers and are subject to the regulatory guidelines outlined by subsidy providers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 452}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELIGIBLE SUBSIDY PROVIDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Eligible Subsidy Providers are entities, such as nonprofit organizations and churches, responsible for overseeing and implementing resale restrictions on properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNIVERSITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Universities can act as Eligible Subsidy Providers, supporting housing initiatives through various programs for students and staff."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOUSING AGENCIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Housing Agencies are government entities that facilitate housing programs and assist in administering subsidy programs at local, state, or federal levels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER INCOME LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower Income Limits define the maximum allowable income for applicants under mortgage programs, impacting their eligibility for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 452}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICABLE CRITERIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Applicable Criteria are the specific qualifications and conditions that must be met by borrowers to participate in certain housing assistance programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSACTION TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transaction Types refer to the categories of real estate transactions, including purchase and refinance, that are subject to specific guidelines and restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ONE-UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"One-Unit Properties are residential properties designed to host a single family and often qualify for mortgage loans under subsidy programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"One-Unit Properties refer to residential structures designed to accommodate a single household, significant in mortgage approval processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TWO-UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Two-Unit Properties are buildings that contain two separate housing units, often used for residential income generation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Two-Unit Properties are residential structures housing two families, which may also qualify for specific underwriting guidelines in housing programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PUDs, or Planned Unit Developments, are communities that offer a mix of residential and communal living spaces, subject to specific mortgage eligibility criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUDs, or Planned Unit Developments, are types of real estate developments that include residential properties along with common areas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDOMINIUMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Condominiums, commonly referred to as condos, are individual residential units within a building or complex, with shared ownership of commonly owned areas and amenities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condominiums, or condos, are individual units within a property that are subject to specific housing regulations and guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 454}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CO-OPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Co-Ops, or cooperative housing, are buildings owned by a corporation where residents own shares in that corporation, allowing them to live in a unit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Co-ops, or cooperative housing, are buildings where residents own shares in the property, subject to eligibility for various housing programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 453}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THREE-UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Three-Unit Properties are residential buildings housing three separate families, also subject to specific mortgage guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOUR-UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Four-Unit Properties are residential structures designed for four families, subject to mortgage eligibility criteria defined by subsidy programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cfec8ddeaba989b347c8cc9daa583b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HO USING MARKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Housing market refers to the area of the economy concerned with the buying, selling, and renting of homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATE LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subordinate Lien is a legal claim on an asset that is ranked lower than other liens when it comes to claims on assets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 179}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 445}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Restrictions are rules or limitations placed on real estate that govern how the property can be used or transferred."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 453}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REDEMPTION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Redemption Period is a time frame after a foreclosure sale during which a borrower can reclaim their property by paying the required debt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Redemption Period is a time frame during which a borrower can reclaim their property after a foreclosure by paying the owed amount."&lt;SEP&gt;"Redemption Period is a timeframe during which a borrower can reclaim their property after foreclosure under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Redemption Period refers to a legally defined timeframe after a foreclosure during which the prior mortgagor may reclaim the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 475}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESALE PROCEEDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Resale Proceeds are the proceeds derived from the sale of a property, which may be subject to specific conditions and restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 465}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SECONDS MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Seconds mortgage is a financial product representing a subsidy amount that assists buyers in purchasing properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 461}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER CONTRIBUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower Contribution is the amount that a homebuyer is expected to financially commit toward the purchase of a home, usually expressed as a percentage of the purchase price."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 83}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET SALES PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Market Sales Price is the price at which a property is sold, typically influenced by current market conditions and appraised values."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATE LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subordinate Loan refers to a secondary loan taken out on a property that has a lower priority than the primary mortgage in terms of repayment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 463}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Value denotes the worth of a property or asset, which can fluctuate based on market conditions, appraisals, and transaction dynamics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLOSING COSTS/PREPAIDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Closing Costs/Prepaids are out-of-pocket expenses paid by a buyer before the loan is finalized, covering a range of transaction-related fees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 83}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOTAL COST TO BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Total Cost to Borrower encompasses all expenses that a buyer will incur in connection with obtaining a mortgage and completing an acquisition."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 83}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Rights refer to the legal rights that determine how a property can be used, owned, or disposed of, as governed by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 465}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOME MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Home Mortgage refers to a loan secured by the property being purchased, with specific lien priority and payment obligations detailed in the underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 463}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"REO (Real Estate Owned) refers to properties that have been foreclosed and are owned by a lender, in this case, Freddie Mac, after the foreclosure process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 477}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC LAND RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Land Records refer to the official records where terms of resale restrictions must be documented, ensuring discoverability in routine title searches."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 466}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESTRICTED PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Restricted Property refers to real estate that is subject to specific resale restrictions, impacting how the property can be sold or transferred."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 466}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AFFORDABLE HOUSING PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Affordable Housing Programs are initiatives designed to assist individuals in purchasing homes by providing financial support and maintaining housing affordability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Affordable Housing Programs are initiatives that provide financial support and resources to make housing more affordable for low- to moderate-income families."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 448}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST LIEN MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"First Lien Mortgage is the primary claim against a property in case of default, which takes priority over other liens or claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 463}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENABLING AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Enabling Authority refers to the governmental body or agency that has the power to impose regulations, such as resale restrictions, on properties within its jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Time Period refers to the specified duration within which certain legal actions, like a right of first refusal, must take place after a property is offered for sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 465}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXCESS PROCEEDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Excess Proceeds refer to the funds that may remain after a property sold in foreclosure fetches a price above the owed debt, impacting the distribution of funds among creditors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 477}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE HOLDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Mortgage Holder is a lender or financial institution that has granted a mortgage loan to a borrower and holds the property title until the loan is repaid."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 475}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARCHITECTURAL MATTERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Architectural Matters refer to considerations surrounding the design and structure of buildings, which may influence real estate transactions and property regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AESTHETIC MATTERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Aesthetic Matters encompass the visual and artistic aspects of property design that may impact value and desirability, particularly in housing markets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AFFORDABLE SECOND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Affordable Second refers to a financial product designed to subsidize the property sales price in affordable housing programs, beneficial for home buyers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 450}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOVERNMENT AGENCIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Government Agencies include municipal and state organizations that administer housing programs and resale restrictions to promote affordable housing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 448}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-PROFIT CORPORATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-Profit Corporations involved in affordable housing create programs that manage subsidy providers and help maintain affordable housing units."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 448}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANNED UNIT DEVELOPMENT (PUD)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Planned Unit Development (PUD) is a type of building development that combines residential and commercial properties, often used in housing programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Development (PUD) is a type of real estate development characterized by shared ownership and maintenance of community properties within specific zoning laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY APPRAISAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Appraisal is the evaluation of a property's value, particularly in relation to resale restrictions and market conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 396}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOME COUNSELING SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SERVICE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Home Counseling Services help potential buyers understand the process of purchasing a home and managing mortgages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraisal Requirements are standards that govern the evaluation of a property's worth in relation to mortgage lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal Requirements detail the necessary evaluations and inspections related to property valuation, crucial for loan approval and market assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal Requirements dictate the standards and processes for evaluating property value, particularly in the context of mortgages and loan approvals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal Requirements for Manufactured Homes encompass regulations ensuring a detailed valuation of manufactured homes and the necessity of conducting appraisals using specific forms and methods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 381}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET SALE PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Market Sale Price indicates the price at which a property would sell under normal market conditions, used for comparison with restricted prices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 450}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLING AND TRANSFER OF PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Selling and Transfer of Property encompasses the processes of selling a home and transferring ownership rights, subject to certain regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIZED SALES PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsidized Sales Price is the final price of a property after applying any subsidies, making it more affordable for eligible buyers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsidized Sales Price is the reduced price at which a property is sold after financial assistance is applied, aimed at making homes more accessible."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 450}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Terms outline the conditions and stipulations under which a mortgage is issued, including payment schedules and interest rates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 274}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME-BASED RESALE RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income-Based Resale Restrictions are guidelines that limit the selling price of a property based on the buyer's income to ensure ongoing affordability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income-based Resale Restrictions are conditions that limit the resale price of properties, ensuring affordability for low to moderate-income buyers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL ESTATE OWNED (REO)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Real Estate Owned (REO) refers to properties owned by a lender after foreclosure, often requiring specific handling protocols."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-PROFIT ORGANIZATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-Profit Organizations work to support affordable housing efforts by providing funding and guiding eligible home buyers through the purchasing process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALES RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sales Restrictions are regulations that prevent the sale of a property to ensure it remains affordable and accessible to targeted buyers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 381}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD-PARTY NON-PROFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third-Party Non-Profit organizations may be enlisted by subsidy providers to help administer affordable housing programs and manage resale restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAPITAL IMPROVEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Capital Improvements are upgrades or renovations made to a property that can increase its value, often subject to approval by subsidy providers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capital Improvements refer to enhancements made to a property that may be eligible for credit under certain subsidy programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-756642bc27ab7956732455451eb4ce71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
