  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ineligible Properties refers to various property types and conditions that do not meet the established guidelines for mortgage finance, which include certain limitations based on occupancy and usage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cefb0ad4148eab93b794bfdc3eb3eac7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 379}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCESSORY UNIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Accessory Unit refers to a secondary dwelling or structure on a residential property that can provide additional living space."&lt;SEP&gt;"Accessory Unit refers to additional living spaces within a property, such as granny units or in-law suites, which can affect property eligibility for financing."</data>
