</node>
<node id="&quot;LEASEHOLD ESTATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Leasehold Estate is a property interest held by a tenant under a lease agreement, which involves specific rights and obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leasehold Estate refers to a property type where the borrower holds rights to a real property through a lease, affecting mortgage eligibility and rights during a default."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leasehold Estate refers to the property rights held by a lessee under the conditions of a lease, affecting ownership and duration of property usage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY CONDEMNATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Condemnation refers to a legal process where property is taken for public use, potentially affecting the lease and mortgage rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 358}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER PRICE INDEX (CPI)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Consumer Price Index (CPI) is a measure that examines the average change over time in the prices paid by consumers for goods and services, which can influence lease agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Consumer Price Index (CPI) is an economic indicator that measures the average change over time in the prices paid by consumers for goods and services, influencing lease agreements tied to this index."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 116}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Terms refer to the various conditions and requirements set forth in a mortgage or lease agreement, impacting the borrower's obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY IMPROVEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Improvements refer to enhancements or alterations made to a property that increase its value and usability, relevant in the context of lease and mortgage agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Improvements refer to enhancements or modifications made to a property, affecting its lease and purchase terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFAULT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Default refers to the failure of a lessee to meet the obligations set forth in the lease agreement, which can lead to legal actions or termination of the lease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Default refers to the failure to fulfill a legal obligation, such as failing to make lease payments or comply with lease terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-LESSOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-lessor is an individual or entity that leases property from a lessor and sublets it to another party, managing the relationship and terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 359}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-LESSEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-lessee is an individual or entity that rents property from a sub-lessor, holding rights under the terms of the sub-lease agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 359}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VOTING RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Voting Rights refer to the entitlements given to members of a homeowners association to vote on decisions affecting the community."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 155}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEASE RENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lease Rents are payments made by the lessee to the lessor for the use of the property as specified in the lease agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 120}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 363}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELEASE OF RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Release of Rights refers to the legal termination or relinquishing of rights previously granted to a borrower or lessee under a lease agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 358}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAND TRUST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Land Trust is a legal entity that holds title to real estate for the benefit of individuals or organizations, often used in relation to conservation or development purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANNED UNIT DEVELOPMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Planned Unit Developments are designed communities created to provide a harmonious mix of residential, commercial, and recreational spaces, often having specific zoning and design guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 454}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INITIAL LAND VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Initial Land Value is the starting price set for land in the context of lease agreements and mortgages, which may be influenced by market trends and property appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BASIC RENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Basic Rent is the primary amount paid for the use of leasing property under the terms defined in a lease or sublease agreement, reflecting rental agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTERNAL INDEX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An External Index is a reference point, like the Consumer Price Index, used to adjust lease terms based on fluctuations in economic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An External Index is a reference used to adjust contractual terms, such as lease payments, based on changing economic conditions, ensuring fairness in agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 116}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Land refers to a specific piece of real estate or property that can be leased or purchased, forming the basis of real estate transactions discussed within the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Land refers to the property in question, which is subject to liens and whose value is assessed for mortgage purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leases are contractual agreements allowing one party to use and occupy property owned by another for a specified period and payment, critical for property transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUS OF PROPERTY IMPROVEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Status of Property Improvements refers to the current condition or state of enhancements made to a property that can influence its value and marketability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISED VALUE OF LAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraised Value of Land is the determined worth of a specific piece of land, as assessed by a professional for various real estate dealings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERCENTAGE INCREASE OR DECREASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Percentage Increase or Decrease relates to the annual adjustment of property values or rents based on market performance, crucial for lease agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 116}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORIGINAL APPRAISED VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Original Appraised Value is the initial estimated worth of a property set at the time of appraisal, serving as a benchmark for future transactions and leases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMS OF THE LEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Terms of the Lease refer to the provisions and conditions outlined in a lease agreement, dictating the rights and obligations of both the lessor and lessee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 358}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEASEHOLD INTEREST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leasehold Interest is a property interest that allows individuals to occupy land or buildings for a specific term while owning certain rights to use and improve the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leasehold Interest is the rights held by a lessee under a lease agreement, providing a legal claim to possess and use a property for a specific term."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOUSING MARKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Housing Market refers to the supply and demand dynamics of residential properties and housing which influences real estate transactions and mortgages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENT PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rent Payments are the periodic amounts paid by a lessee to a lessor in exchange for the use of leased property, central to lease agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUSTMENT OF THE LEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjustment of the Lease refers to modifications made to the terms or amounts relating to a lease agreement, often influenced by market factors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL TERM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual Term signifies the yearly duration for which certain lease conditions or payments are evaluated or re-negotiated, often impacting finance and contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIFE ESTATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Life Estate refers to a property occupied for the duration of a person's life, which presents eligibility issues for certain mortgage transactions, requiring title clearance prior to closing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LESSOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Lessor is the party who owns the property and grants the leasehold rights to another party in exchange for rent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LESSEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Lessee is the party who rents the property under the lease agreement, gaining temporary rights to use it while adhering to the lease terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 112}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROUND RENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ground Rent refers to the periodic payment made by the lessee to the lessor for the use of land in a leasehold agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgaging is the process of using a property as collateral to secure a loan, which involves specific provisions in lease agreements when applied to leasehold estates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBLEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sublease occurs when the original lessee rents out part or all of the property to another party, creating a legal intermediary rental agreement under the original lease."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 112}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Insurance in this context refers to policies that protect both the lessor's and lessee's interests regarding the leased property, typically required under lease terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 115}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPERATING EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Operating Expenses include costs incurred from the utilities, maintenance, and management of the property under the lease, affecting the financial obligations of the lessee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 115}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN CLOSING REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Closing Requirements refer to the stipulations that must be met for loans involving manufactured homes, including the need for a Manufactured Home Rider to be executed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 334}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Down Payment Requirements refer to the criteria defining the minimum amount of money that must be contributed by the borrower towards the purchase of a manufactured home."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 303}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSTITUTE FOR BUILDING TECHNOLOGY AND SAFETY (IBTS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Institute for Building Technology and Safety is an organization that provides services related to building safety and compliance, including verification letters for manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 386}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUD DATA PLATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The HUD Data Plate is a compliance certificate located inside manufactured homes that includes necessary information for appraisal and verification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The HUD Data Plate is a crucial document associated with manufactured homes, containing vital compliance information regarding the home's construction and safety standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 386}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANUFACTURED HOME RIDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Manufactured Home Rider is a legal document that accompanies a mortgage loan for a manufactured home, outlining specific terms and conditions for the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 334}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FANNIE MAE PERS APPROVED LIST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Fannie Mae PERS approved list is a registry of projects that meet Fannie Mae's eligibility criteria for manufactured homes within planned unit developments (PUDs)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 371}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EQUITY REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Equity Requirement refers to the necessary ownership stake a borrower must have in the land when financing a manufactured home."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 303}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPAIR ESCROWS FOR POSTPONED IMPROVEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Repair Escrows for Postponed Improvements refer to the funds allocated for future repairs or improvements on a manufactured home that are not allowable under current guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 371}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WARRANTY DEED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Warranty Deed is a legal document showing ownership of a property, necessary to demonstrate there are no outstanding liens against the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIONAL AUTOMOBILE DEALER ASSOCIATION OF MANUFACTURED HOUSING APPRAISAL GUIDE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The National Automobile Dealer Association of Manufactured Housing Appraisal Guide provides standards for appraising manufactured homes, influencing the equity contribution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 304}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN TO VALUE DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan to Value Determination is a financial ratio used to assess the amount of a loan against the value of an asset, crucial in mortgage financing for manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 371}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXISTING MANUFACTURED HOMES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Existing Manufactured Homes refers to previously sold manufactured homes that are being considered in purchase money transactions for financing loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIEN SEARCH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Lien Search is a process involving a review of property records to determine if there are any existing liens on the manufactured home and land."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PURCHASE MONEY TRANSACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Purchase Money Transactions are real estate transactions in which mortgage proceeds are used to finance the purchase of property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSFER OF OWNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transfer of Ownership refers to the process of legally selling and assigning ownership rights from one party to another, relevant in real estate transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Records are official documents that provide information about legal ownership and any encumbrances on a property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT STATEMENT REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Settlement Statement Requirements outline the necessary documents that the borrower must provide during the loan application process to validate their cash investment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 172}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 426}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CURRENT APPRAISED VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Current Appraised Value refers to the present market value of the land or property as determined by a professional appraiser."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH INVESTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cash Investment refers to the amount of money that a borrower contributes towards the purchase of land or a manufactured home, necessary for loan approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 48}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OUTSTANDING INDEBTEDNESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Outstanding Indebtedness refers to any remaining debt secured by liens on the property that must be settled before ownership can be transferred."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 474}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETAIL VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Retail Value refers to the market price at which a manufactured home can be sold, influencing loan and equity calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOME SOLD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Home Sold refers to the transaction involving the sale of a manufactured home, relevant for appraising value and determining equity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL GUIDE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appraisal Guide provides insights and standards for assessing the value of manufactured homes and is utilized in loan underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORM 1004C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Form 1004C is a specific appraisal form required by Fannie Mae for the valuation of manufactured homes, including detailed requirements for the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 381}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN APPLICATION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Application Date refers to the specific date when a loan application for a manufactured home is submitted, critical for determining eligibility and parameters of financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 301}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENCUMBRANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Encumbrance refers to a legal claim against a property, such as a lien or mortgage, that may affect ownership and financing options."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 464}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAXIMUM LTV OF 65%&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum LTV of 65% is a limitation on the Loan-to-Value ratio for cash-out transactions for manufactured homes, indicating the maximum loan amount permissible compared to property value."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 464}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OUTSTANDING LIENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Outstanding Liens denote any remaining debts secured by a property that must be settled or accounted for in financial transactions, particularly in refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 464}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY-OWNED STREET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A community-owned street refers to a roadway maintained by a community rather than a public entity, relevant for site requirements of manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 383}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATE AGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The State Agency is a governmental entity responsible for inspecting and approving modifications to manufactured homes if state regulations require such action."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 383}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPARABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comparability in the context of this text refers to the assessment of similar manufactured homes for appraisal purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 383}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The mortgage loan file contains necessary documentation and reports that support the appraisal and financing of manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 409}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODEL NAME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Model Name refers to the specific designation of a manufactured home, which is essential for its identification and appraisal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 409}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YEAR OF MANUFACTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Year of Manufacture indicates when a manufactured home was built, which affects its valuation and compliance with standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 409}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERIAL NUMBER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Serial Number is a unique identifier assigned to each manufactured home, crucial for tracking and appraisal purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 409}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT FOUNDATION SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Permanent Foundation System refers to the structural base that ensures the stability of manufactured homes, which must adhere to safety and local building codes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 386}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOIL CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Soil Conditions pertain to the physical properties of the land where a manufactured home is situated, impacting the requirements for foundation systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 383}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCAL AND STATE CODES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Local and State Codes are regulations that govern construction and safety standards which must be followed in the placement of manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 385}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEPTIC TANK OR SEWAGE SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Septic Tank or Sewage System is a necessary utility connection for manufactured homes to handle waste disposal in accordance with health regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 385}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPARATIVE SALES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Comparative Sales refers to similar properties that are used as benchmarks for evaluating the market value of a manufactured home during appraisal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 383}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSPECTION REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Inspection Report is a formal document that assesses the condition and safety of a manufactured home, which must be maintained in the mortgage loan file."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 409}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHATTEL MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chattel Mortgage is a type of financing that involves a secured interest in personal property, such as manufactured homes, which is distinct from real estate mortgages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 383}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACTORY-BUILT HOUSING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Factory-Built Housing refers to homes constructed in a factory setting and includes types such as modular, prefabricated, and panelized housing, which have distinct eligibility requirements for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Factory-Built Housing refers to homes constructed in a factory setting, which include manufactured homes and modular homes, subject to specific evaluations during appraisal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 384}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODULAR HOMES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Modular Homes are factory-built housing units that must conform to the International Residential Code, and are eligible for loan purchases by Fannie Mae if they meet state standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREFABRICATED, PANELIZED, AND SECTIONAL HOMES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Prefabricated, Panelized, and Sectional Homes are types of housing that can be financed under specific guidelines even if they do not meet certain federal construction and safety standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCAL BUILDING CODES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Local Building Codes are regulations governing the construction and safety standards that housing must meet in order to be legally classified as real property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MULTI-UNIT BUILDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Multi-Unit Buildings, such as condos and townhomes, may use modular construction techniques and must conform to local building codes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL RESIDENTIAL CODE (IRC)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The International Residential Code (IRC) is a set of regulations that govern the construction of residential buildings to ensure safety and compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUD'S FEDERAL MANUFACTURED HOME CONSTRUCTION AND SAFETY STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HUD's Federal Manufactured Home Construction and Safety Standards are regulations that govern the construction and safety of manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 371}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEED OF TRUST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Deed of Trust is a legal document that secures a loan by transferring the legal title of a property to a trustee until the loan is repaid."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 514}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHATTEL LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Chattel Lien is a legal right against personal property, which must not be used alongside a real property lien on land for manufactured home loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 242}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TITLE ENDORSEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Title Endorsements are additional provisions or amendments to an insurance policy that ensure the validity and marketability of a title before selling a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 371}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SINGLE REAL ESTATE TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Single Real Estate Transaction refers to the legal requirement that the purchase, conveyance, and financing of a property be documented as one cohesive transaction under state law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOUNDATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Foundation refers to the lower portion of a building that transfers its load to the ground, which must meet local building codes for factory-built homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 374}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHATTEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chattel refers to an item of personal property that is movable and can be used in transactions for financing, such as a manufactured home."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statutes are written laws enacted by a legislative body that govern the legal classification of manufactured homes as real property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUDICIAL DECISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Judicial Decisions refer to the interpretations of law made by courts that can affect the application and enforcement of statutes related to property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANUFACTURED HOUSING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Manufactured Housing is an industry segment that focuses on the production and financing of homes built in factories and then transported to sites for installation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 484}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE-BUILT HOUSING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site-Built Housing refers to conventional homes constructed on-site, as opposed to those built in a factory, and is subject to different regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 132}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 384}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDING CODE REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Building Code Requirements are standards that determine the design, construction, and occupancy of buildings to ensure public safety."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 485}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST-LIEN MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A First-Lien Mortgage is a loan secured by real property that holds priority over any other loans in terms of repayment in the event of a sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOME CLASSIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Home Classification refers to the legal determination of a dwelling's status, distinguishing between personal property and real property based on local laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT ATTACHMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent Attachment refers to the requirement for factory-built housing to be affixed to a foundation to qualify as real property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 374}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOUSING ELIGIBILITY GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Housing Eligibility Guidelines refer to the criteria that determine which types of properties qualify for financing through specific lenders like Fannie Mae."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIXED-USE PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mixed-Use Properties refer to real estate that incorporates various types of uses, such as residential and commercial, as defined under mortgage guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WATERFRONT PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Waterfront Properties refer to real estate located adjacent to water bodies, with specific considerations under zoning and appraisal guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 372}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARCEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parcel refers to a piece of real estate that must meet specific requirements regarding ownership and mortgage value impact."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 414}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDING CODES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Building Codes are regulatory standards that govern the construction and alteration of buildings to ensure safety and compliance with legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 380}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODULAR CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Modular Construction Techniques involve building structures using pre-fabricated units, allowing for efficiency and flexibility in construction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 380}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIXED-USE PROPERTIES GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
