<node id="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fannie Mae is a government-sponsored enterprise (GSE) known as the Federal National Mortgage Association. It supports mortgage lending in the United States by providing capital for loans, thereby helping to increase the availability of affordable housing. Fannie Mae aims to expand the secondary mortgage market by securitizing mortgages, promoting access to homeownership for low- and moderate-income households. The organization plays a significant role in the U.S. mortgage market, providing liquidity, stability, and affordability to housing finance. It establishes guidelines for mortgage lending, appraisals, and underwriting practices, ensuring the smooth flow of funds to mortgage lenders. Fannie Mae also provides financial products and services related to mortgage lending, home ownership, and enhancing the housing market. Additionally, Fannie Mae purchases mortgages, including loans secured by various types of housing, and sets requirements for appraisals, taxation, and income verification. The organization emphasizes the importance of liquidity in the mortgage market and aims to make home financing more accessible through its various programs and guidelines."</data>
