  <data key="d4">33.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LTV Ratio is a critical factor considered in cash-out refinance transactions for manufactured homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LTV ratio is a critical metric used to determine the overall risk and eligibility for a cash-out refinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LTV ratio is critical in assessing the risk of a cash-out refinance, determining the maximum allowable loan amount relative to property value."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LTV ratio is crucial in determining the terms of a cash-out refinance, thus linking the two entities in financial evaluation."</data>
