  <data key="d6">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLOSING COSTS are costs associated with the borrowing process that the LENDER may cover under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LENDER is responsible for closing costs and is allowed to contribute under certain conditions as stated in underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9640138f8accaa3b0962e60c94ddc9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lenders are required to follow underwriting guidelines to evaluate borrower eligibility and loan conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;INTEREST RATE BUYDOWN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lenders may facilitate interest rate buydowns to assist borrowers in reducing initial payment levels on mortgages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT ABATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payment abatement funds are provided to the lender for distribution, establishing a connection between lender and abatement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lenders must adhere to guidelines set by Fannie Mae when processing conventional loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lenders follow Freddie Mac's guidelines for underwriting conventional mortgage loans, indicating a regulatory relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;ESCROW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Escrow accounts are often managed by the lender for securing funds during real estate transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conventional underwriting guidelines provide the framework that lenders follow, indicating an operational relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lenders must adhere to conventional underwriting guidelines, showcasing a direct relationship in the financing process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lenders utilize conventional underwriting guidelines to evaluate borrower applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76dfd0d1478f77acd572a51bf4e3956a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE HISTORY VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LENDER requires MORTGAGE HISTORY VERIFICATION to assess the borrower's creditworthiness and eligibility for the mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;CREDIT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A LENDER assesses the BORROWER's CREDIT HISTORY to determine their creditworthiness and loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A LENDER provides a MORTGAGE for the borrowing of funds, creating a fundamental transactional relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lender is responsible for ensuring that the mortgage deal complies with all applicable laws and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lender is the entity providing the mortgage, responsible for assessing the borrower's financial information to approve the loan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN-LEVEL PRICE ADJUSTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lenders apply loan-level price adjustments based on the homeownership education completed by borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lender provides the closing disclosure to the borrower to detail the financial aspects of the mortgage refinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lender conducts an underwriting analysis to evaluate the borrower's financial situation, including income stability and payment history."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE REVENUE BONDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mortgage revenue bonds serve as financing instruments for lenders offering mortgage products, impacting their lending capabilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;CASH-OUT AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lender evaluates the cash-out amount in relation to the terms of the mortgage and any applicable restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;RESALE RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lenders must consider resale restrictions when underwriting loans secured by affected properties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POWER OF ATTORNEY (POA)&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The POA is utilized when a spouse or domestic partner acts on behalf of the borrower in a loan transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POWER OF ATTORNEY (POA)&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER’S SPOUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's spouse can act through a POA, linking personal relationships to legal obligations in the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POWER OF ATTORNEY (POA)&quot;" target="&quot;DOMESTIC PARTNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A domestic partner can also represent the borrower under a POA, indicating legal and financial responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT SALE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower may incur additional fees during a short sale, which can affect their financial obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT SALE&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Short sales represent a specific type of real estate transaction affecting the financial outcomes for the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT SALE&quot;" target="&quot;SIGNIFICANT DEROGATORY CREDIT EVENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Short sale is included as a significant derogatory credit event impacting eligibility assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT SALE&quot;" target="&quot;DEED-IN-LIEU&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both deed-in-lieu and short sale are alternatives to foreclosure, allowing borrowers to manage their mortgage difficulties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deed-in-lieu and short sale are both alternatives to foreclosure, offering borrowers options to avoid foreclosure impact on credit and finances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT SALE&quot;" target="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">21.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A short sale serves as an alternative to foreclosure, impacting credit but providing a potentially less damaging solution for borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"SHORT SALE is an alternative to FORECLOSURE which allows the sale of the home for less than the mortgage owed, thus avoiding foreclosure proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Short sale is a possible alternative to foreclosure and has its own recovery time guidelines within the context of derogatory events."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT SALE&quot;" target="&quot;DEED-IN-LIEU OF FORECLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both deed-in-lieu of foreclosure and short sale are alternatives to prevent foreclosure, often discussed in the same context of managing mortgage difficulties."&lt;SEP&gt;"DEED-IN-LIEU OF FORECLOSURE and SHORT SALE are alternative options to foreclosure that may have different waiting periods as per guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT SALE&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY LISTING AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PROPERTY LISTING AGREEMENTS may be required during the process of a SHORT SALE to facilitate the sale of the property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">31.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Assets refer to properties or resources owned by the borrower, impacting their financial evaluation during mortgage assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers' assets used for down payment or closing costs must be verified and considered in their financial profile."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Borrower must demonstrate ownership and access to various assets, indicating a relationship between them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower's financial assets and cash deposits must be verified to secure the mortgage, showing the importance of asset documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67964fc288da88f7bb3defef1f29177&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers need specific assets to qualify for loans, including foreign assets that meet Freddie Mac’s requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documentation requirements ensure that assets, including those from foreign institutions, meet specific criteria for financing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;CASH BACK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cash back is relevant to the asset calculations required for closing and reserves during mortgage transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Assets are evaluated according to underwriting guidelines to determine their eligibility for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;IRA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"IRA funds can be considered part of the assets for qualifying income purposes in mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;FINANCIAL ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Assets are considered financial assets when they are liquid and can be converted into income streams for mortgage lending."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8241f9b00004d342f0da796cabf2a5f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;NET DOCUMENTED ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Net Documented Assets are calculated by subtracting ineligible funds from total assets."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;VIRTUAL CURRENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Virtual currency is considered an ineligible asset that must be subtracted from total eligible assets."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac sets parameters for what constitutes eligible Assets in loan applications and calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY INCOME STREAM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Monthly Income Stream calculations depend on the evaluation of various Assets considered for loan qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;RETIREMENT ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Retirement Assets are a specific category of Assets that can contribute to a borrower's financial profile under Freddie Mac guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Retirement assets are a specific category of assets that the Borrower must have access to for qualification purposes, linking them together."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f67964fc288da88f7bb3defef1f29177&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;VERIFICATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The assets must be verified through a verification process, establishing a relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f67964fc288da88f7bb3defef1f29177</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;DEPOSITORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Assets can be held in a depository account, indicating a direct relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f67964fc288da88f7bb3defef1f29177</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSETS&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Assets can be utilized to cover the closing costs associated with a mortgage application."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">39.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Closing Disclosure must contain all fees and payments agreed to by the borrower, ensuring transparency in the transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower is responsible for the information contained in the Closing Disclosure related to their refinance transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower must receive a closing disclosure that outlines the terms and costs associated with the cash-out refinance loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower receives the closing disclosure that details the financial aspects of the mortgage loan they are signing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The closing disclosure must reflect gift funds, showing that the borrower's financial situation incorporates these funds."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;UNDISCLOSED SELLER CONTRIBUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Undisclosed seller contributions are often not disclosed on the Closing Disclosure and can affect eligibility for mortgages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Closing costs must be documented in the Closing Disclosure for the mortgage transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The closing disclosure itemizes closing costs associated with a loan, providing transparency to the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;PURCHASE TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Closing Disclosure outlines all financial details related to the purchase transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;APPRAISED VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The appraised value of the property must be reported in the Closing Disclosure to ensure accuracy in the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;GIFT OF EQUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The closing disclosure must list the gift of equity being provided in the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;GIFT LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">21.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A gift letter must be provided to the closing disclosure, indicating the necessity of documentation for the financial transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The closing disclosure must accurately reflect the details of the gift letter provided by the donor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The closing disclosure must reference the details outlined in the gift letter to document the gift accurately."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b456ca1fe500021a9d2ca86dedfd1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;ESCROW AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The escrow agent is responsible for ensuring the closing disclosure reflects the accurate transfer of funds and costs associated with the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;WIRE TRANSFER CONFIRMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A wire transfer confirmation must be included to verify the transfer of gift funds, establishing a transactional relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8a9ffcad15481c83b74cda33a0148728</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The closing disclosure is linked to the note date, specifying when a cash-out refinance must be documented."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY LISTING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The status of the property listing affects the closing disclosure details, ensuring compliance with sale conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;LTV RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loan-to-value (LTV) ratios must be calculated and disclosed through the closing disclosure to define mortgage terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Each transaction's details are summarized within the closing disclosure, which outlines the terms of the mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;FINAL CLEAR TO CLOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The final clear to close status must be reviewed alongside the closing disclosure to finalize the mortgage transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;SCRUTINY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Closing disclosures are subject to scrutiny by lenders to verify compliance with underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;PROCEEDS OF LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The closing disclosure needs to reflect how proceeds from the loan are utilized, including paying off existing obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;SETTLEMENT PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The settlement process concludes with the closing disclosure, detailing all funds involved in the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;REFINANCE TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Closing Disclosure outlines the terms and cash flow required for a refinance transaction, ensuring compliance with regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Closing Disclosure specifies the agreed-upon loan amount for the borrower, detailing all financial terms involved in the mortgage transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;CASH-OUT PROCEEDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The closing disclosure details how cash-out proceeds will be allocated and disbursed during the refinancing process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;TITLE SEARCH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Closing Disclosure must reference the results of the title search to confirm the absence of liens on the subject property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;FLAGSTAR BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Flagstar Bank mandates that mortgage insurance must be disclosed in the Closing Disclosure to maintain compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN ESTIMATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Closing Disclosure and Loan Estimate must include correct MI premiums and terms for compliance purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;FIRST PAYMENT LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both the Closing Disclosure and First Payment Letter need to properly disclose mortgage insurance details to the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;COMPARABLE SALES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Closing Disclosure provides necessary transaction details that help verify the information in the appraisal regarding comparable sales."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;APPRAISAL REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Closing Disclosure is integral to the appraisal report as it provides crucial financial details regarding the subject property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSING DISCLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;COMPARATIVE MARKET DATA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Comparative Market Data can inform the accuracy of transaction details found in the Closing Disclosure, aiding in the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea0854aedb400acc54c26d78db5065c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNDERWRITING MANAGER&quot;" target="&quot;REPAIR ESCROWS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The underwriting manager must approve all repair escrows as part of the loan approval process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d77c56c7ef7f25742c687f6ad137c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOA FEES&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower may have to pay HOA fees, which can affect their financial status and loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOA FEES&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payments may include HOA fees, impacting the borrower's financial commitments during the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOA FEES&quot;" target="&quot;DELINQUENT TAXES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both delinquent taxes and HOA fees represent obligations that may affect the financial standing of the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOA FEES&quot;" target="&quot;ESCROW ACCRUALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Escrow accruals may include HOA fees as part of the costs associated with maintaining property ownership."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOA FEES&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT ABATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payment of HOA fees can be involved in transactions relating to payment abatements, affecting the borrower's contributions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05495faf7d0cd92781a907bc384d2f21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSACTION&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower is an integral part of the transaction, directly impacting the outcome of the loan process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The transaction is directly related to the borrower's process of making a property purchase."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSACTION&quot;" target="&quot;REAL ESTATE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The real estate agent plays a key role in facilitating the transaction, ensuring it progresses smoothly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSACTION&quot;" target="&quot;FINANCING CONCESSIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Specific financing concessions are tied directly to the transaction to help reduce costs for the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSACTION&quot;" target="&quot;SETTLEMENT STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The transaction involves a settlement statement that outlines the original purchase price and, importantly, reflects conditions for repayment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REAL ESTATE AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The relationship between property sellers and real estate agents is essential, as the agent often represents the seller in transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REAL ESTATE AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Real estate agents assist borrowers in the process of purchasing property, including navigating gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8eefd188642258e1fb627891c7c2dbb6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REAL ESTATE AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Real estate agents may require tax returns for loan applications to ensure income verification and stability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ab9735c2b386c1cf372b9ba4a34fe4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBORDINATE LIEN HOLDER&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The subordinate lien holder's interests are legally tied to the borrower’s obligations, particularly in loan repayment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER’S SPOUSE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrower’s Spouse is often considered in mortgage applications as their financial situation may affect the overall loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TITLE POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The title policy is important for the borrower as it ensures the property title is clear and free of disputes during the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT SALE PROCESSING FEES&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These fees are incurred during a short sale process and are directly related to the borrower's financial obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower is responsible for making payments associated with their loan, linking them directly to the payment process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower’s payment history, including timely payments under resolution plans, is crucial for maintaining loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;PRINCIPAL AND INTEREST (P&amp;I)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payments made by the borrower include principal and interest (P&amp;I), which form part of their mortgage obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;COLLECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Collections indicate unpaid payments or obligations, reflecting negatively on a credit report."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payments are an obligation that borrowers must meet as part of their agreements with creditors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;TRIAL PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Timely payments during the trial period are essential for borrowers to successfully complete the modification process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Underwriters assess borrower payment histories to determine loan eligibility and risk.</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;LUMP SUM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lump sum payments relate to overall payments that borrowers must manage in the context of meeting financial obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers must fulfill specific contribution requirements for the down payment, sometimes using matched funds from nonprofit agencies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23ec06f9f4a15f1cb40e52e628766be9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">35.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Down Payment and Closing Costs need to be subtracted from total assets when calculating Net Documented Assets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both closing costs and down payments are financial components involved in obtaining a mortgage, linking them together."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both down payment and closing costs are essential financial components in mortgage transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing costs are related to the down payment as both are critical components of the mortgage transaction process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The guidelines for an Affordable Second specify that it cannot be used towards the Borrower’s closing costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d30aff8ce4b53c163b59f9369ea58842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67964fc288da88f7bb3defef1f29177&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;REAL ESTATE TAX CREDITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Real estate tax credits can help in managing the overall financial burden of the down payment required by the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-144555be48c11828e99c3a7c623170fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Down Payment is the initial upfront portion of the total amount that a borrower must contribute when purchasing a property, vital for loan approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower must provide a down payment as part of the mortgage requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower's down payment is a critical component required to secure a mortgage loan."</data>
  <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EQUITY CONTRIBUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The down payment can include equity contributions provided by the borrower, necessary for mortgage approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c315a6b793aa073b8f6cb2ffb42e4f97</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE EQUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Trade equity can be used as part of the down payment in a property transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-32546641e2f2fec0a52f658ed70fc338</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER’S OWN FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrower’s own funds are generally required for the down payment in compliance with minimum contribution requirements precluding the use of gift funds."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-164ff18d322608d7342cc1d0619c9f0f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;INVESTMENT PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Investments properties often have higher down payment requirements to mitigate lender risk, impacting borrower financial planning."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-164ff18d322608d7342cc1d0619c9f0f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;HOMEOWNERSHIP EDUCATION AND COUNSELING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Homeownership education and counseling can assist borrowers in locating funds for down payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY SECONDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Community Seconds are programs that can assist borrowers with their down payment requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conventional underwriting guidelines specify requirements for down payment contributions from borrowers."&lt;</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;NET DOCUMENTED ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The down payment is subtracted from the Net Documented Assets for accurate income calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc03d45e68c4df0463506aff2ba2a679</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ACCESS TO FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The down payment is a portion of the total funds required from the borrower, impacting their actual access to funds for loan approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc03d45e68c4df0463506aff2ba2a679</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;RESERVES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Down Payment and Reserves are financial requirements essential for loan closing and qualifying under Freddie Mac guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-446d02f0d6609ee8a932eea7a8d1302e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY SECOND&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Community Second can affect the necessary down payment by acting as a subsidy for the property’s sales price."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1da51e05e6600babe4a36494acdf7928</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;INCOME-BASED RESALE RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Income-based resale restrictions cannot be applied towards the Borrower's Down Payment as per the guidelines for obtaining an Affordable Second."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The down payment is subject to the specified down payment requirements established by Fannie Mae."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EQUITY REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's equity in the land can be credited towards their minimum down payment requirement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELINQUENT TAXES&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower may be responsible for delinquent taxes, impacting their eligibility for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN ORIGINATOR&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The loan originator facilitates the loan process for the borrower, establishing a direct link in the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN ORIGINATOR&quot;" target="&quot;FLAGSTAR BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The loan originator is responsible for ensuring that mortgage insurance is disclosed properly under Flagstar Bank's guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-995f33933031b2ea33803f61f1ece1b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN ORIGINATOR&quot;" target="&quot;INELIGIBLE APPRAISER LIST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The loan originator must ensure that the appraiser does not appear on Flagstar's ineligible appraiser list to maintain compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN ORIGINATOR&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The loan originator must ensure compliance with Fannie Mae guidelines during the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN ORIGINATOR&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The loan originator must adhere to Freddie Mac's standards while managing the appraisal and loan process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8d2d43086c2d67020db933397546a228</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONCURRENT FIRST LIEN MORTGAGE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower may be involved with a concurrent first lien mortgage, indicating multiple levels of financial obligation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECONDARY LIEN&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower may have to manage a secondary lien, potentially complicating the loan transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e857c204b7048098a278905f60d5302</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HELOC&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac has specific requirements regarding the documentation and use of HELOC in transactions involving real property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac requires HELOC payments to be factored into the housing expense-to-income ratio when there is an outstanding balance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2891670ed51dfc47bbb015af66f14dde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HELOC&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both MORTGAGE and HELOC are financial products that involve potential borrowing against secured properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both MORTGAGE and HELOC may be subject to qualifying and reserve requirements based on the borrower's financial profile."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC is a type of MORTGAGE that allows the borrower to access equity in their home, linking these entities in financial lending context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HELOC&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae's guidelines specify how HELOC payments must be included in monthly debt obligations for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HELOC&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"HELOC payments are associated with the mortgage debt and influence the borrower's overall financial obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HELOC&quot;" target="&quot;EXISTING LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"HELOCs can be considered as existing liens that may be paid off with cash-out refinance proceeds."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD-PARTY ASSET REPORTS&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac requires third-party documentation for asset verification, which is accepted under specific guidelines from Flagstar."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD-PARTY ASSET REPORTS&quot;" target="&quot;ASSET TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Different asset types are documented and reported through third-party asset reports outlined in guidelines from Freddie Mac."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD-PARTY ASSET REPORTS&quot;" target="&quot;OUTSTANDING LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Outstanding loans must be reported in third-party asset reports as part of the overall financial assessment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BANK PRINTOUTS&quot;" target="&quot;VERIFICATION OF DEPOSIT FORM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both bank printouts and verification of deposit forms serve as essential documentation for verifying financial information during underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSET DOCUMENTATION&quot;" target="&quot;VERIFICATION OF SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Asset documentation is necessary for verifying the source of funds, establishing credibility in the lending process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSET DOCUMENTATION&quot;" target="&quot;CASH-ON-HAND&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cash-on-hand is mentioned as not being an acceptable source of funds, indicating a restriction within asset documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66bee43127ef8c394af00a30febd1833</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSET DOCUMENTATION&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Asset Documentation refers to the provided paperwork that details a borrower's financial assets, used to verify their ability to secure a loan."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERIFICATION OF DEPOSIT FORM&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY BANK STATEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both the verification of deposit form and monthly bank statements serve to validate the borrower's financial standing during underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY BANK STATEMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;QUARTERLY STATEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both types of statements are critical in the underwriting process with specific timelines for their acceptance defined in the underwriting guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY BANK STATEMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Monthly Bank Statements provide key insights into a borrower's financial health and transaction history required during loan assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERIFICATION OF SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWED FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowed funds require verification to ensure that they do not conflict with the eligibility of the borrower's financial profile."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53373dd554a175653540f360348f32eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERIFICATION OF SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Verification of Source of Funds ensures that any funds presented by a borrower are legitimate and documented, crucial in the loan approval process."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWED FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;POOLED SAVINGS ARRANGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Pooled savings arrangements can be used for down payments while borrowed funds secured by assets can represent a return of equity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWED FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;RETIREMENT ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Vested funds from retirement accounts can be used, while borrowed funds can be secured by these financial assets."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWED FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;TRUST ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Trust funds can be used as an acceptable source if the borrower has immediate access, similar to secured borrowed funds."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWED FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;FINANCIAL ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowed funds can be secured using various financial assets such as stocks and bonds, reflecting their interconnection."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWED FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;REAL ESTATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Real estate can be used to secure borrowed funds, representing equity that can be leveraged for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9d7483a0c4012d30e50767206255bda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
