  <data key="d6">chunk-14fb0d3aaa293edfdf71f855df5bd9ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNDERWRITER&quot;" target="&quot;STATE-REGULATED FINANCIAL INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNDERWRITER works for the STATE-REGULATED FINANCIAL INSTITUTION to evaluate the BORROWER's financial documentation and eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNDERWRITER&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS STRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNDERWRITER must consider the BUSINESS STRUCTURE when evaluating stability and ordinary business income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNDERWRITER&quot;" target="&quot;DISBURSEMENT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The underwriter assesses documentation, including the application and tax returns, to determine the appropriate disbursement date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf6a394b54c040882b94d8dd97b886e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;INCOME SOURCES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Income represents the origin from which income sources may be derived and is necessary for qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec242ee203576a6a4b76efbe5458e782</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;MILITARY LEAVE AND EARNINGS STATEMENT (LES)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Military Leave and Earnings Statement (LES) serves as a verification method for income for military personnel applying for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec242ee203576a6a4b76efbe5458e782</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Borrower’s financial eligibility is assessed based on various income sources, directly relating the Borrower to the concept of income."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower's income needs to be verified through specific documentation as part of the loan application process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec242ee203576a6a4b76efbe5458e782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;NEW PRIMARY EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Income from new primary employment is critical for establishing financial stability in the mortgage qualification process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2eef4940eec1ef97062f77d3efe4074e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;FUTURE SALARY INCREASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Future salary increases from the current employer can be considered as part of the borrower's income for qualification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2eef4940eec1ef97062f77d3efe4074e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;STABLE MONTHLY INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Stable monthly income must be established based on various forms of income documentation such as RSU payouts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;CALENDAR YEARS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The assessment of income requires consideration of the borrower's earnings over specified calendar years."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;CHILD SUPPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Child support is recognized as a valid form of income for the Borrower in financial applications, hence the two are related with respect to income sources."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;DISABILITY BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Disability benefits can contribute to a Borrower's income, establishing a direct relationship between the two in the context of loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;WORKERS COMPENSATION BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workers Compensation Benefits are also classified under income sources that can impact a Borrower's financial qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC ASSISTANCE PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public Assistance Payments serve as potential income for the Borrower, linking these two elements in financial documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;TAX EXEMPT INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tax Exempt Income is categorized as a legitimate source of Income that individuals may report for verification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;TAX RETURN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Income reported in a Tax Return is essential for validating a Borrower’s financial status, hence linking these two concepts closely."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9bd9610961bbb8effa4b39adbc65bddc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;YTD INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"YTD income is a crucial component of the borrower's overall income profile that influences lending decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ed1a879d48c49b16f42ce89ae56d954</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's income is detailed in their tax returns, serving as a basis for assessing financial stability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ed1a879d48c49b16f42ce89ae56d954</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE K-1&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Schedule K-1 is used to document the receipt of income from partnerships, which can be included in a borrower's cash flow if stability is proven."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;GUARANTEED PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Guaranteed payments are categorized as income received by partners in a partnership, affecting the overall income statement of the business."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINANCED PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FINANCED PROPERTIES refer to the various properties secured under a MORTGAGE agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINANCED PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGES AND HELOCS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mortgages and HELOCs are relevant factors when considering additional financed properties for reserves calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINANCED PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;TOTAL # OF FINANCED PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The total number of financed properties influences the percentage requirements for reserves and guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME AND OVERALL CREDIT PROFILE&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTED SOURCES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DOCUMENTED SOURCES support the evaluation of the BORROWER's INCOME AND OVERALL CREDIT PROFILE for loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3cd8475962bfe1c2428c1ea6691488c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERCENTAGE OF UPB&quot;" target="&quot;RESERVES IN MONTHS OF PITIA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The reserves required are calculated based on the percentage of the UPB of financed properties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTOMATED CREDIT UNDERWRITING&quot;" target="&quot;DESKTOP UNDERWRITER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Automated Credit Underwriting includes systems like Desktop Underwriter, which assesses borrower information for loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTOMATED CREDIT UNDERWRITING&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN PRODUCT ADVISOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Desktop Underwriter and Loan Product Advisor are part of the automated credit underwriting process employed by lenders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESKTOP UNDERWRITER&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN PRODUCT ADVISOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Desktop Underwriter and Loan Product Advisor are tools assessing different maximum numbers of borrowers on a single loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both the Loan Product Advisor and Desktop Underwriter are tools used in the mortgage process, including for detached condominiums."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3fe3f1cf3ad46c315af5250198974ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3455e52007c02e364a735d4c4a7efa70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESKTOP UNDERWRITER&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Desktop Underwriter operates within the framework of underwriting guidelines to assess loans effectively."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3fe3f1cf3ad46c315af5250198974ab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESKTOP UNDERWRITER&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION-TO-PERMANENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Construction-to-Permanent loan process must interface with Desktop Underwriter to determine loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e252311920cec13b843fb034a4a69e94</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN PRODUCT ADVISOR&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loan Product Advisor assesses mortgages according to underwriting guidelines laid out for various borrowing scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3fe3f1cf3ad46c315af5250198974ab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;RESERVES IN MONTHS OF PITIA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PITIA is used to calculate the reserves required for mortgage financing, impacting lending decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-756818f22cafd11009f520745a0306df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PITIA expenses are part of the borrower's total debt obligations, affecting their financial assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"PITIA is included in the borrower's total monthly obligations for calculating the debt-to-income ratio."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PITIA includes principal, interest, taxes, insurance, and is part of the overall mortgage debt obligations for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;HOUSING EXPENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PITIA is part of the calculation for determining the total monthly housing expenses of the Borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-909c805f10bec3b9745cd64c1852b1fd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PITIA is factored into the overall financial assessment including Closing Costs for Borrower qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-909c805f10bec3b9745cd64c1852b1fd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Contract stipulates income that contributes towards PITIA calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-843cd03316121e01909837126fbbe24c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;ADDITIONAL RESERVES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation of Additional Reserves includes assessment of PITIA to ensure sufficient funds for the loan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-843cd03316121e01909837126fbbe24c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;RENTAL INCOME FROM THE SUBJECT PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rental income must offset the PITIA (Principal, Interest, Taxes, Insurance, and Association dues) of the subject property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PITIA payments can be offset by rental income from the investment property according to Freddie Mac guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental income can be used to offset the PITIA of the subject property, showing a direct financial relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b454650a6e8dde5a93325db30813c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PITIA&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PITIA is considered in the context of the loan purpose, which is limited to purchase and rate-term refinances for properties with ADUs."</data>
