</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;CREDIT REPORTING AGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The credit report is generated by the credit reporting agency and is essential for loan approvals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The underwriting guidelines are based on the information presented in the credit report."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting guidelines are influenced by the findings on a credit report, particularly regarding derogatory events and their timing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTED CREDIT INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Disputed credit information refers to inaccuracies in the credit report that borrowers must address."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN APPLICANTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loan applicants must provide a credit report that details their credit history when applying for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;HISTORICAL ACCOUNT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The historical account history highlighted in the credit report provides a timeline of the borrower's payment behavior."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The approval for a MORTGAGE LOAN is based on the evaluation of the BORROWER'S CREDIT REPORT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;ASSET VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The examination of the CREDIT REPORT is part of the broader ASSET VERIFICATION during the underwriting process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;DEROGATORY EVENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Credit reports record derogatory events such as bankruptcy and foreclosure, affecting creditworthiness and loan approval processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;WAITING PERIODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Credit reports must reflect waiting periods for derogatory events as they significantly influence the borrower’s loan eligibility status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;DELINQUENT CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DELINQUENT CREDIT is disclosed within the CREDIT REPORT and must be accurately reported during loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;DU FINDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CREDIT REPORT analysis directly affects DU FINDINGS, which determines mortgage eligibility based on credit history."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;DEBT-TO-INCOME RATIO (DTI)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DEBT-TO-INCOME RATIO (DTI) is calculated based on information in the CREDIT REPORT which includes debts and income for assessment of loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2b4494b2a290a96f3ee6a9d358a812a8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The credit report serves as a critical component in the mortgage file for verifying financial details of the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;PACE LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Credit Report must evaluate the Borrower's ability to handle the PACE loan related to solar panel financing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;APPRAISAL REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Credit Report is influenced by findings in the Appraisal Report, particularly in relation to collateral value."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6434821b2faf91ece4b375276017b775</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VALID CREDIT SCORE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWERS WITHOUT A CREDIT SCORE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers without a credit score must meet certain requirements, including having at least one borrower with a valid credit score."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VALID CREDIT SCORE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Valid Credit Score must be presented and verified to assess the borrower's creditworthiness for loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWERS WITHOUT A CREDIT SCORE&quot;" target="&quot;RENTAL HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rental history is an acceptable form of nontraditional credit for borrowers without a valid credit score."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWERS WITHOUT A CREDIT SCORE&quot;" target="&quot;CREDIT SOURCES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers without a credit score must provide alternative credit sources for loan consideration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWERS WITHOUT A CREDIT SCORE&quot;" target="&quot;SATISFACTORY PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers without a credit score must demonstrate satisfactory payment history through nontraditional means to qualify for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DU APPROVE/ELIGIBLE&quot;" target="&quot;LPA ACCEPT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both DU Approve/Eligible and LPA Accept are methods used to determine loan eligibility for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DU APPROVE/ELIGIBLE&quot;" target="&quot;AUS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"AUS is the automated underwriting system that requires a DU approve/eligible status for loan approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c392c46c8ab1fb7407628dd97c6f2c74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONFORMING LOAN LIMITS&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH BALANCE LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"High balance loans are ineligible when loans must meet conforming loan limits set by Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONFORMING LOAN LIMITS&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH BALANCE LOAN ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"High balance loan eligibility is determined in relation to conforming loan limits set by the agency guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOUSING-RELATED NONTRADITIONAL CREDIT&quot;" target="&quot;UTILITY PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Utility payments can be part of the housing-related nontraditional credit required for borrowers without traditional credit scores."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;S SATISFACTORY PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Satisfactory payment history is essential for demonstrating reliability when a borrower lacks a credit score."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT-ORDERED ASSIGNMENT OF DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's payment history is relevant both before and after the court-ordered assignment of debt."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;GARNISHMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Garnishments, if present, influence the borrower's payment history and overall financial evaluation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;RENTAL INCOME DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rental income documentation requires a history of rental income which helps in qualifying the borrower for investment property loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-10ce55972cf12e21fd77796ab69a96ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;FIRST CONTACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rental history is evaluated to establish the reliability of rental income for underwriting assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-10ce55972cf12e21fd77796ab69a96ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT SOURCES&quot;" target="&quot;CREDIT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Credit sources and credit history are both necessary for establishing a borrower's creditworthiness in the loan application process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A borrower’s credit history is essential for evaluating their credit score and loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit History consists of the borrower's previous borrowing and repayment activities, which are crucial for assessing eligibility for mortgage products."</data>
  <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED USER TRADELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"AUTHORIZED USER TRADELINES must accurately reflect the BORROWER's CREDIT HISTORY for them to be considered valid in underwriting decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Eligibility Requirements outline the necessary conditions that Borrowers must meet to qualify for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility requirements are criteria that borrowers must meet to qualify for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ae330f51f478e78f1b91957f17dcdec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">26.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Borrower must meet certain eligibility requirements related to the mortgage, including age and ownership of assets."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MORTGAGE must align with the Eligibility Requirements as determined by Fannie Mae’s guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"The terms of the MORTGAGE dictate certain ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS that must be met by the BORROWER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-452a34dee684e3a93929cc44930deb38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f01d27887cb1edc56efdd9355e2cbba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Eligibility requirements are part of the underwriting guidelines needed for the Borrower to proceed with a mortgage application."&lt;SEP&gt;"UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES set the standards for the ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS related to mortgages and loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-452a34dee684e3a93929cc44930deb38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT STATUS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Eligibility Requirements dictate how the CURRENT STATUS is assessed regarding missed payments and credit worthiness."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTED RESOLUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Eligibility requirements include a documented resolution of any prior credit events as part of loan approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;SIGNIFICANT DEROGATORY CREDIT EVENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Significant derogatory credit events impact the eligibility requirements that borrowers must meet for loan approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae establishes eligibility requirements that borrowers must meet for loans secured through their system."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;MAXIMUM LTV, CLTV, OR HCLTV RATIOS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Eligibility requirements often include maximum loan-to-value ratios as part of the criteria for financing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPANCY TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Eligibility requirements vary based on occupancy types, affecting the conditions under which financing is approved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS are determined by the CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES, which dictate the mortgage approval process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3f01d27887cb1edc56efdd9355e2cbba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;VOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A lease agreement and a Verification of Rent (VOR) can both serve as supporting documents for rental history in nontraditional credit cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;FAIR RENTAL DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lease is used to determine the net rental income and fair rental days for reporting purposes on Schedule E."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;ADU RENTAL ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A lease must be used to determine the net rental income, supported by the ADU rental analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lease must be supported by an ADU rental analysis to validate the rental income projected."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The mortgage file must contain documentation regarding the lease to determine net rental income."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mortgage file must contain the lease to support the rental income calculations for tax purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;ZONING AND LAND USE REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compliance with zoning and land use requirements is necessary for the legality of the lease for rental purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-81edfb1496d26226dca5f3238aa461cd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;ACCESSORY DWELLING UNIT (ADU)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lease is required to determine the net rental income generated by the ADU."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BORROWER is directly involved as a party in the LEASE, underpinning their obligations and rights under it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lease must be obtained from the Borrower and must meet certain requirements, ensuring its validity for calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;MINIMUM INCOME DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lease must adhere to minimum income documentation requirements to be valid and properly executed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;REPAIR COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lease must account for any repair costs when determining net rental income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-151a292558f7e1fe4b393da7f73632a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;TERM LEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term lease sets the conditions under which rental income is calculated and documented, influencing stability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7a01c4d224477788cf5c6bfd6ccc84e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;DEBT PAYMENT-TO-INCOME RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lease payments for solar panels can be excluded from the DTI ratio if certain conditions are met, linking lease agreements to financial assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;ENERGY PRODUCTION GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An energy production guarantee within a lease agreement provides compensation related to the performance of solar panels."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL FIXTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Solar panels financed under a lease may be classified as personal fixtures, depending on the terms of the lease agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY CONDEMNATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Provisions regarding PROPERTY CONDEMNATION are included within the LEASE to safeguard the rights and interests of leaseholders."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lease includes provisions related to property condemnation to protect the interests of stakeholders involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;CONSUMER PRICE INDEX (CPI)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LEASE may include adjustments based on the CONSUMER PRICE INDEX (CPI), linking economic factors to lease terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;RELEASE OF RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LEASE may include provisions about the RELEASE OF RIGHTS, affecting the entitlements of the involved parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LEASE may require a RELEASE OF RIGHTS under certain conditions, detailing the legal stipulations affecting the parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-LESSOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SUB-LESSOR grants rights to the SUB-LESSEE, establishing a direct relationship through the LEASE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-LESSEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SUB-LESSEE is a party to the LEASE, indicating their rights and responsibilities as affected by the original lease terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY IMPROVEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PROPERTY IMPROVEMENTS are included in the lease terms, affecting the overall valuation and use of the leased property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ca2c4d1778a11943201b4e917c15322</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;LEASEHOLD MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The terms and conditions of a Lease are fundamental to establishing a Leasehold Mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;RENT PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rent payments are structured according to the terms set out in the Lease, directly impacting financial obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;TERMS OF THE LEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The terms of the lease define the relationship between the parties involved and the obligations related to lease payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b81be5b6336b17987b5cd27bc0cf519d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;LEASEHOLD ESTATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">20.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lease creates the leasehold estate, establishing their direct interrelation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lease outlines the terms under which the leasehold estate is granted, making them directly related."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;SUBLEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A sublease is an agreement structured under the original lease, forming a relationship between the two entities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lease must adhere to specific underwriting guidelines established by lenders and insurers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;LESSOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lessor is the party that enters into the lease agreement with the lessee, highlighting their direct relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;LESSEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lessee is the individual or entity that holds the lease, engaging directly with the lessor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mortgage provisions relate directly to the terms stipulated in the lease agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;DEFAULT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Default clauses are inherent in the lease, determining the consequences of non-compliance by the lessee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;UTILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Utilities are often included as part of the obligations outlined in the lease agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE&quot;" target="&quot;INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Insurance provisions are typically required elements in the lease to protect the lessor's interests."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a008bee56d46d46fc9de7e014d26695</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACCOUNT NUMBER&quot;" target="&quot;NATURE OF OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An account number is a specific identifier tied to the nature of an obligation, which relates to loans and financial responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACCOUNT NUMBER&quot;" target="&quot;HISTORICAL ACCOUNT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The historical account history is related to the account number, providing a record of payment behavior."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NATURE OF OBLIGATION&quot;" target="&quot;OUTSTANDING BALANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Outstanding balance indicates the current amount owed on an obligation, which is related to the nature of the obligation itself."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341a8217a86a20f7b3a1712ac24de48f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OUTSTANDING BALANCE&quot;" target="&quot;LAND CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The outstanding balance of a land contract must be paid off using the proceeds from the mortgage loan during refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OUTSTANDING BALANCE&quot;" target="&quot;PRELIMINARY TITLE SEARCH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A preliminary title search ensures there are no outstanding balances or liens that could affect the financing of the mortgage loan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OUTSTANDING BALANCE&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loan payments are made to reduce the outstanding balance of the mortgage loan over time, impacting overall debt management."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACTIVE MILITARY ALERTS&quot;" target="&quot;FLAGSTAR BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FLAGSTAR BANK contacts applicants with active military alerts before issuing a commitment letter."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACTIVE MILITARY ALERTS&quot;" target="&quot;EXTENDED FRAUD ALERTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both extended fraud alerts and active military alerts affect how lenders process loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT INQUIRIES&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN APPLICANTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loan applicants must provide explanations for all credit inquiries listed in their credit reports."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT INQUIRIES&quot;" target="&quot;CREDIT REPORTING AGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The credit reporting agency lists all credit inquiries made within a certain time frame."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit reporting agency records all credit inquiries made and provides them in the credit report."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDITOR&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A borrower must provide documentation to the creditor showing the terms of debt repayment and payment history."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COLLECTIONS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Collections on the borrower's credit history must be evaluated as part of their financial profile during the underwriting process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Collections reflect on the borrower's credit history impacting their eligibility negatively if significant unpaid debts are found, affecting lending decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OBLIGATION&quot;" target="&quot;CREDIT DATA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Obligations are recorded as part of the credit data, which informs lenders of the borrower’s financial responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPORTING AGENCY&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Credit Reporting Agency provides essential information about the borrower's credit history, significantly affecting their eligibility for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT DATA&quot;" target="&quot;CREDIT REPORT TRADE LINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Credit report trade lines represent individual accounts within the credit data that reflect a borrower's credit history."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f359b1edc6f123eca67b08265c9b89e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSCRIPTS&quot;" target="&quot;IRS FORM 4506 C&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"IRS Form 4506 C is required for obtaining transcripts needed for tax verification, linking these two entities closely."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4f5775363168aa3256002e8b909c2f52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSCRIPTS&quot;" target="&quot;TAX RETURN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tax returns are needed to generate transcripts for verification, highlighting their interconnectedness in tax processing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4f5775363168aa3256002e8b909c2f52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSCRIPTS&quot;" target="&quot;IRS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.8</data>
  <data key="d5">"Transcripts are documents issued by the IRS summarizing tax returns for verification of financial status."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Positive RENTAL PAYMENT HISTORY can be factored into the BORROWER's credit assessment, potentially influencing loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHENTICATION OF RENTAL PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The AUTHENTICATION OF RENTAL PAYMENT HISTORY validates the BORROWER's monthly payments, affecting loan assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DU/LPA&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DU/LPA provides feedback that informs the UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES, affecting how lenders evaluate borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DU/LPA&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DU/LPA evaluates the rental history of the BORROWER as part of the mortgage assessment process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DU/LPA&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FREDDIE MAC oversees the guidelines that DU/LPA follows for underwriting processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DU/LPA&quot;" target="&quot;NON-OCCUPANT CO-BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DU/LPA assesses the acceptability of loans with non-occupant co-borrowers, influencing mortgage insurance decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DU/LPA&quot;" target="&quot;VERBAL VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Verbal verification is necessary for obtaining DU/LPA reports during the underwriting process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6261b628a88157f5bd4a959ee8fdb8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPOSITORY&quot;" target="&quot;IN-FILE MERGED REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An IN-FILE MERGED REPORT consolidates data from multiple CREDIT REPOSITORIES to create a comprehensive view of a borrower's credit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CREDIT REPOSITORY&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A MORTGAGE is reported to a CREDIT REPOSITORY, which plays a role in tracking the borrower's credit activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31dff4bfbf6291a2db9c4969e0f5cbe0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BORROWER needs to meet MORTGAGE REQUIREMENTS for loan approval, including asset verification and rental history."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MORTGAGE REQUIREMENTS are specified within the CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES that must be met for loan approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;JUNE 2, 2020&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MORTGAGE REQUIREMENTS changed for applications on or after JUNE 2, 2020, affecting borrower eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHECKING, SAVINGS AND INVESTMENT ACCOUNTS&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD-PARTY SERVICE PROVIDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Data from a THIRD-PARTY SERVICE PROVIDER is used to assess the BORROWER'S CHECKING, SAVINGS AND INVESTMENT ACCOUNTS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHECKING, SAVINGS AND INVESTMENT ACCOUNTS&quot;" target="&quot;ASSET VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ASSET VERIFICATION involves examining CHECKING, SAVINGS, AND INVESTMENT ACCOUNTS of the BORROWER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSET VERIFICATION REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ASSET VERIFICATION REPORT is used to evaluate the LOAN PAYMENT HISTORY of the BORROWER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSET VERIFICATION REPORT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER’S SAVINGS ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ASSET VERIFICATION REPORT must include the BORROWER’S SAVINGS ACCOUNT for comprehensive financial assessment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN PAYMENT HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;REFINANCED MORTGAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Evaluation of LOAN PAYMENT HISTORY is important when assessing REFINANCED MORTGAGES."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RISK CLASS&quot;" target="&quot;RISK ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"RISK CLASS is determined as part of the RISK ASSESSMENT process based on the financial behavior of the BORROWER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERIFICATION SERVICE&quot;" target="&quot;ASSET VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The VERIFICATION SERVICE aids in the process of ASSET VERIFICATION necessary for mortgage underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER’S CHECKING ACCOUNT&quot;" target="&quot;ASSESSMENT REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The asset verification report includes data from the BORROWER'S CHECKING ACCOUNT for risk assessment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN&quot;" target="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The NOTE DATE is critical for determining the relevant mortgage timeline for the MORTGAGE LOAN."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Closing costs can be financed with the new mortgage loan during cash-out refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN&quot;" target="&quot;INTEREST RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The interest rate directly affects the terms and costs associated with the mortgage loan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The mortgage loan is the financial product that the borrower acquires to purchase or refinance the subject property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN&quot;" target="&quot;REHABILITATION COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rehabilitation costs can influence the mortgage loan amount as they are considered part of the acquisition costs during refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fb1c993d98cbaba5a6755fc57b9ff69</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;SEASONING PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The note date is crucial in determining the required seasoning period for refinancing, creating a procedural relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9da80c7f63e32b0d7dc6df2ae9032546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY ACQUISITION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The note date is crucial in documenting the timing of property acquisition as it may affect refinancing qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05020d8707d581b6c2d0c1b184d17f01</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT START DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The timing of the Employment Start Date is critical and must align with the NOTE DATE for the mortgage process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3f01d27887cb1edc56efdd9355e2cbba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;DELIVERY DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DELIVERY DATE must be scheduled appropriately in relation to the NOTE DATE as part of the mortgage process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3f01d27887cb1edc56efdd9355e2cbba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT OFFER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The timing of the EMPLOYMENT OFFER should be structured relative to the NOTE DATE for mortgage processing compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3f01d27887cb1edc56efdd9355e2cbba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The note date is critical as it establishes the timeline for employment verification requirements for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2eef4940eec1ef97062f77d3efe4074e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICATION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documentation requirements pivot around both the application date and note date as key timeframes in the mortgage process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a173c08400538977a1dc5397bceda0a6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower must ensure all required documents are submitted by the note date to finalize the mortgage process, connecting both entities closely."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a173c08400538977a1dc5397bceda0a6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RISK ASSESSMENT&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN PAYMENT HISTORY REPORTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LOAN PAYMENT HISTORY REPORTS provide information critical to the RISK ASSESSMENT of a mortgage loan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN PAYMENT HISTORY REPORTS&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LOAN PAYMENT HISTORY REPORTS are a component of the CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES for evaluating BORROWER eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BORROWER must undergo the CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING PROCESS to secure a mortgage loan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-212cbc70c3f0e59feb09b85b04e1c40f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SERVICER&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SERVICER manages the MORTGAGE, handling payments and interactions with the BORROWER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAYMENT PLAN&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BORROWER must follow a REPAYMENT PLAN to resolve missed payments and bring the mortgage current."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAYMENT PLAN&quot;" target="&quot;REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A REPAYMENT PLAN is a method to reinstate the mortgage by addressing missed payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAYMENT PLAN&quot;" target="&quot;LOSS MITIGATION PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The loss mitigation program encompasses various strategies, including repayment plans, to help borrowers avoid foreclosure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAYMENT PLAN&quot;" target="&quot;TIMELY PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Timely payments are a requirement for maintaining repayment plans, critical for obtaining favorable loan conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAYMENT PLAN&quot;" target="&quot;MODIFICATION PLAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A repayment plan can be part of a modification plan, allowing borrowers to adjust terms and manage payments more effectively."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAYMENT PLAN&quot;" target="&quot;TRIAL PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Trial periods confirm borrower compliance with terms of the repayment plan before formal approval of modifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REINSTATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;REPAYMENT TO SERVICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"REINSTATEMENT involves making missed payments to the SERVICER to restore the mortgage to good standing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REINSTATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;INTEREST TO DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"INTEREST TO DATE must be settled as part of the REINSTATEMENT process when bringing the mortgage current."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORBEARANCE&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT STATUS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FORBEARANCE allows the CURRENT STATUS of the mortgage to show as not delinquent despite missed payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORBEARANCE&quot;" target="&quot;STUDENT LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Forbearance is a status that can be applied to student loans, affecting repayment obligations for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61ba5485d92daa30adf4ee02bfab7d8a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORBEARANCE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers may enter forbearance on their loans, potentially affecting their repayment obligations and financial standing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61ba5485d92daa30adf4ee02bfab7d8a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORBEARANCE&quot;" target="&quot;DEFERMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both deferment and forbearance are options available to borrowers to temporarily pause payments on their loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1a05e768a9b64dd897dab3f97a6c234a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORBEARANCE&quot;" target="&quot;REPAYMENT PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Forbearance is a temporary relief option included within broader repayment programs for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1a05e768a9b64dd897dab3f97a6c234a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTEREST TO DATE&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT MORTGAGE ACCOUNT STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"INTEREST TO DATE must be reflected accurately in the CURRENT MORTGAGE ACCOUNT STATEMENT for verification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERIFICATION OF MORTGAGE&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT MORTGAGE ACCOUNT STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"VERIFICATION OF MORTGAGE is based on the information found in the CURRENT MORTGAGE ACCOUNT STATEMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;REPAYMENT TO SERVICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SOURCE OF FUNDS must be documented for any REPAYMENT TO SERVICER to ensure they are legitimate and acceptable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT MORTGAGE ACCOUNT STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CURRENT MORTGAGE ACCOUNT STATEMENT must verify the SOURCE OF FUNDS used in any repayment plan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;THE BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The source of funds for deposits must be clearly identifiable as part of the Borrower's financial documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-452a34dee684e3a93929cc44930deb38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;LUMP-SUM DISTRIBUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lump-sum distribution proceeds must not incur penalties and must comply with the established source of funds requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source of funds must be well documented when applying for a lump-sum distribution to ensure compliance with regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-452a34dee684e3a93929cc44930deb38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The source of funds is a critical factor in determining the Borrower's capability to secure a mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-452a34dee684e3a93929cc44930deb38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SOURCE OF FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Source of Funds validates the origin of monetary deposits presented by borrowers in loan applications, ensuring legitimacy."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAYMENT TO SERVICER&quot;" target="&quot;TABLE 3&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"TABLE 3 lists conditions related to REPAYMENT TO SERVICER that borrowers must fulfill after missed payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TABLE 3&quot;" target="&quot;NET RENTAL INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Table 3 outlines the process for calculating net rental income or loss, impacting financial assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1- TO 4-UNIT RESIDENTIAL PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MORTGAGE is secured by the 1- TO 4-UNIT RESIDENTIAL PROPERTY in question."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-105c313a28b49198d2d2b78db6e7529b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae guidelines include the evaluation of foreclosure events for determining loan eligibility and risk factors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;SIGNIFICANT DEROGATORY CREDIT EVENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Foreclosure is also a significant derogatory credit event, contributing to higher default risk."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE REFINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Foreclosure status directly impacts the options available for mortgage refinancing for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;DEED-IN-LIEU&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Deed-in-lieu is considered an alternative to foreclosure and has similar implications on credit history and waiting periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;LOSS MITIGATION PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loss mitigation programs aim to prevent foreclosure by offering alternatives like loan modifications and repayment plans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;DEED-IN-LIEU OF FORECLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">29.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A deed-in-lieu of foreclosure is a process that occurs instead of a foreclosure, linking them as options in distressed property scenarios."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both foreclosure and deed-in-lieu of foreclosure involve significant derogatory credit events and have related recovery periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deed-in-lieu of foreclosure is a part of the foreclosure process, providing an alternative way to transfer ownership back to the lender."&lt;SEP&gt;"Foreclosure and deed-in-lieu of foreclosure affect how resale restrictions are managed and valued post-transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;CHARGE-OFF OF MORTGAGE ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Foreclosure typically leads to charge-offs on mortgage accounts due to loan default."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;WAITING PERIODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Waiting periods are established for foreclosure actions, indicating required durations before re-engaging in certain financial activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd0f34ee8edcf779e6ff94578f8ab9c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;HOUSING COUNSELING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Housing counseling aims to prevent foreclosure by addressing financial issues impacting homeowners."&lt;</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fe6ee5848653e2ade85b8c44b7433dac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;REDEMPTION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The redemption period is relevant to foreclosure as it specifies a timeframe for the borrower to reclaim the property, connecting their processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The redemption period is significant in the context of foreclosure, affecting the treatment of resale restrictions afterward."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6d048ce21946dbbaf2025fa9d108f909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;REO&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"REO properties are those that have gone through foreclosure, and Freddie Mac discusses guidelines related to these properties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d635e8ee0ac48c5c8906a09d9d6759ba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY APPRAISAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A property appraisal must account for conditions like foreclosure, which can affect the property’s future market conditions and resale restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-787de407af176e62ce6eb517b2dd1d21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEED-IN-LIEU&quot;" target="&quot;SIGNIFICANT DEROGATORY CREDIT EVENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Deed-in-lieu is regarded as a significant derogatory event in determining loan qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS MITIGATION PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;REPRESENTATIVE PLAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loss mitigation programs may include repayment plans to help manage borrower defaults."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS MITIGATION PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower engages with loss mitigation programs to prevent foreclosure and explore resolution options."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS MITIGATION PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae provides guidelines for loss mitigation programs to help borrowers under financial distress including foreclosure alternatives."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRIAL PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;REPRESENTATIVE PLAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The trial period is part of the repayment plan, where timely payments are essential to qualify for further modifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRIAL PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;3-MONTH REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 3-month requirement is critical during the trial period, reflecting borrower commitment to modified loan terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3-month requirement must be satisfied during the trial period to qualify for specific loan modifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRIAL PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;MODIFICATION PLAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Trial periods are necessary for modification plans wherein borrowers must show timely payments for eligibility of mortgage adjustments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7482b9f302a8cac2d717810389222b99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT DEFERRAL&quot;" target="&quot;REPRESENTATIVE PLAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A payment deferral can be part of a representative plan, allowing borrowers to temporarily postpone payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8fbac57b62fb040bd0302d8a94d9f65</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
