  <data key="d6">chunk-3ae330f51f478e78f1b91957f17dcdec</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tax returns are part of the employment verification process essential for assessing Borrower eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ae330f51f478e78f1b91957f17dcdec</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers need to submit signed federal income tax returns to establish their income history for loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tax Returns provide a comprehensive overview of a borrower's income history and financial standing essential for mortgage assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower needs to provide tax returns to qualify for the mortgage, which includes verifying their income from self-employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-332ea40a8706fdd85456078cf47232fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE CREDIT CERTIFICATES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tax returns must be provided to support the borrower's income claims when applying for mortgage credit certificates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;INTEREST INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interest income must be reflected in the borrower's tax returns to be considered during the mortgage evaluation process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;DIVIDEND INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dividend income must also be documented in the borrower's tax returns to establish eligibility for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;THREE-YEAR CONTINUANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tax returns can provide evidence for income that demonstrates the required three-year continuance for stable income sources."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC ASSISTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documentation regarding public assistance may need to be included in tax returns to corroborate the borrower's income claim."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e28f33ddf3b335e19135327f9afb2b07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;TAX FILING YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The tax filing year determines the applicable tax returns that must be analyzed for borrower income verification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE E&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule E is part of the tax returns that report the income and expenses related to rental properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule E is specifically part of tax returns that details rental income and related expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 1&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule 1 is included within the tax returns and may outline additional income sources relevant to the borrower's financial profile."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER'S FEDERAL INDIVIDUAL INCOME TAX RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's federal tax returns provide a comprehensive view of their income and financial situation over the past years."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ed1a879d48c49b16f42ce89ae56d954</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;TAX DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tax documentation, including tax returns, is essential in verifying the borrower's income for underwriting purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ed1a879d48c49b16f42ce89ae56d954</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;IRS FORM 4506 C&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"IRS Form 4506 C is used to obtain copies of tax returns, establishing a direct connection with the submission of tax returns."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a173c08400538977a1dc5397bceda0a6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;MOST RECENT FINANCIAL STATEMENT(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tax returns for the last one or two years are required alongside most recent financial statements in evaluating borrower eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a173c08400538977a1dc5397bceda0a6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;FLAGSTAR BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FLAGSTAR BANK needs tax returns to document income for applicants."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;W2&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"W2s are required along with tax returns to verify an individual's income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;1099&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"1099 forms are also required alongside tax returns for income documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;TAX ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"TAX RETURNS are recorded and associated with each taxpayer's tax account."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b8e57f220eeefd0215ac958c381bc47</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DU FINDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;LPA FINDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DU findings and LPA findings are both assessments conducted during the underwriting process, affecting qualification and requirements for borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"LPA findings and DU findings are both evaluation measures used in underwriting to assess borrower qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALIMONY&quot;" target="&quot;CHILD SUPPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Alimony and child support can be considered acceptable stable income if they are expected to continue for a specified period after the mortgage application."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both alimony and child support are considered liabilities that need to be reported and can affect a borrower's debt-to-income calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALIMONY&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac guidelines require alimony payments to be documented as a negative income figure if they are to be considered in debt calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALIMONY&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae mandates that alimony be listed as a liability on the borrower's application for loan processing purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALIMONY&quot;" target="&quot;SOCIAL SECURITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Social Security may play a role in verifying income streams, including alimony payments for loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALIMONY&quot;" target="&quot;SEPARATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A separation agreement may detail alimony terms if the divorce is incomplete, indicating ongoing financial responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALIMONY&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A legal agreement often specifies the terms of alimony, establishing a formal obligation and payment structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALIMONY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court records provide official evidence of alimony agreements and payments, which are crucial for income verification during mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILD SUPPORT&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to alimony, Freddie Mac requires that child support payments be documented when calculating a borrower's liabilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILD SUPPORT&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae requires the borrower’s child support obligations to be provided in documentation for accurate loan assessment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILD SUPPORT&quot;" target="&quot;SEPARATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A separation agreement can provide terms for child support if the divorce is not finalized, thus establishing a financial obligation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILD SUPPORT&quot;" target="&quot;AGE OF CHILDREN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The age of children is a factor in determining the duration and stability of child support payments required from a borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILD SUPPORT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court records can detail child support agreements, verifying the amounts and conditions necessary for mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9004bef6d0a745fff75d973c6b90ef4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BRIDGE LOAN&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A bridge loan allows the borrower to secure financing for a new home while collateralized by their current home, involving specific underwriting criteria."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BRIDGE LOAN&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac outlines specific requirements regarding bridge loans, which borrowers must meet to qualify for financing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY DEBT OBLIGATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's monthly debt obligations are reviewed by the underwriter to assess loan eligibility and payment capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower's monthly debt obligations include various recurring payments that need to be considered for loan qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY DEBT OBLIGATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED USER ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Monthly debt obligations must be computed considering authorized user accounts when assessing the borrower’s financial health."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY DEBT OBLIGATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;RECURRING OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Recurring obligations must be considered as potential monthly debt obligations in debt-to-income calculations for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY DEBT OBLIGATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;CASH FLOW ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cash flow analysis must account for all monthly debt obligations, influencing loan qualification decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY DEBT OBLIGATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;CASHED CHECKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cashed checks provide evidence of payment that might be considered in assessing the borrower's monthly debt obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORIZED USER ACCOUNTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Authorized user accounts on a borrower's credit report can influence the assessment of their creditworthiness during loan underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business debts in the borrower's name may be excluded from consideration if the obligations meet specific criteria defined in the guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac guidelines allow for exemptions in handling business debt when specific criteria are met, providing flexibility for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae has similar guidelines to Freddie Mac concerning business debt, determining its impact on the borrower's qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COUNTY&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower must ensure that there are no tax liens filed against them in the county where the property is located."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COUNTY&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae guidelines stipulate regulations contingent on the county where the property is located, impacting loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COUNTY&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac guidelines take into account county-specific regulations that affect the borrower’s loan application and approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT REMINDER&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payment reminders from the IRS serve as proof that the borrower is adhering to their tax installment agreement, which is vital for underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHARGE-OFFS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Charge-offs on the borrower's credit report can impact their eligibility for loan approval and need to be reviewed by the underwriter."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2 TO 4-UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae has particular requirements regarding the treatment of collections and charge-offs related to 2 to 4-unit properties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a021e31a2283c93026e9b4e4159dcdf6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2 TO 4-UNIT PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conventional underwriting guidelines include specific criteria for 2 to 4-unit properties, establishing a direct relationship with these property types."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91cf1d5ee6d1d8b224c54c5417b6eaee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REAL ESTATE TAX PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY TAX BILL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The real estate tax payment is derived from the property tax bill which reflects the taxes owed on the property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY HOUSING EXPENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mortgage payments are a key component of a borrower's monthly housing expense, affecting overall debt obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;INTEREST EXPENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interest expenses are part of the mortgage payment that affects the borrower's overall financial obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MORTGAGE PAYMENT is a key component of the borrower's total monthly obligations when qualifying for a loan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY TAX BILL&quot;" target="&quot;LOCAL ASSESSOR'S OFFICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The local assessor's office determines the current tax rate which is reflected in the property tax bill."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY TAX BILL&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIAL ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Special assessments are additional costs that may be included in the property tax bill if they are not included in annual tax payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY TAX BILL&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT TAX BILL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The current tax bill is an updated statement of the property tax bill that may affect payment calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY TAX BILL&quot;" target="&quot;EXISTING PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Existing properties have property tax bills that must be calculated from historical assessments and current values."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY TAX BILL&quot;" target="&quot;HOMESTEAD EXEMPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The homestead exemption can reduce the amount due on the property tax bill for qualified properties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL ASSESSMENT&quot;" target="&quot;RECALCULATED TAXES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Recalculated taxes may include special assessments that must be factored into property tax evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX ABATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY HOUSING EXPENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tax abatements can be used to reduce monthly housing expenses if supported by proper documentation and follow-up requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELINQUENCY&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A history of delinquency for the borrower affects the consideration of their monthly debt obligations and eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35b11a1ced8de5c90f65c0b1344222c2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
