  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STUDENT LOANS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Student loans are part of the borrower's financial obligations and must be considered in their payment history and qualification processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STUDENT LOANS&quot;" target="&quot;DEFERRED INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Deferred installment debt can include student loans, impacting the overall financial evaluation of the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STUDENT LOANS&quot;" target="&quot;INCOME-DRIVEN REPAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Income-Driven Repayment plans are alternatives for borrowers managing their student loans, affecting payment obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income-driven repayment plans adjust the payment amounts for borrowers based on their income, influencing student loan management."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61ba5485d92daa30adf4ee02bfab7d8a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STUDENT LOANS&quot;" target="&quot;DISCHARGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The discharge of student loans indicates a borrower no longer has to repay those debts, impacting financial responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61ba5485d92daa30adf4ee02bfab7d8a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GARNISHMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Garnishments must be included in the borrower's monthly debt obligations, affecting their financial qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NON-MORTGAGE DEBTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's ability to qualify for loans may be influenced by non-mortgage debts paid by others, which impact their financial standing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NON-MORTGAGE DEBTS&quot;" target="&quot;OUTSTANDING DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Outstanding debt can include non-mortgage debts, influencing the overall debt evaluation for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFERRED INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Deferred installment debt counts as part of the borrower's recurring monthly debt obligations affecting qualification for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFERRED INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;OUTSTANDING DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Outstanding deferred installment debt is part of the borrower's debt obligations affecting qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFERRED INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER'S PAYMENT LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's payment letter may document expected payments for deferred installment debts required for qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CURRENT PRIMARY RESIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;EXECUTED BUYOUT AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The executed buyout agreement is part of an employer relocation plan that takes responsibility for the borrower's current primary residence's outstanding mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINGENT LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT-ORDERED ASSIGNMENT OF DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contingent liabilities are relevant in the context of court-ordered assignments, affecting the borrower's obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINGENT LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY SETTLEMENT BUY-OUT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A property settlement buy-out can lead to contingent liability, as the borrower may still have financial obligations under the mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61ba5485d92daa30adf4ee02bfab7d8a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT-ORDERED ASSIGNMENT OF DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower may be affected by court-ordered assignment of debt, which involves outstanding debt assigned to another party while still holding liability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT-ORDERED ASSIGNMENT OF DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;OUTSTANDING DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Outstanding debt can be subjected to court-order assignments that impact the borrower's liability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUFFICIENT RESERVES&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower must have sufficient reserves to facilitate the financial requirements associated with the buyout agreement and expenses related to their buying process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUFFICIENT RESERVES&quot;" target="&quot;LPA RESPONSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LPA response outlines the requirement for sufficient reserves as part of the borrower's overall evaluation for loan qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY PAYMENT AMOUNT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The monthly payment amount is essential in calculating the borrower's obligations and determining qualification for mortgages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORBEARANCE AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The forbearance agreement documents the payment amount for deferred debts that the borrower needs to provide for qualification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3500178db8c114017db2f8c6f93e2791</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Installment debt is a part of the borrower's recurring monthly debt obligations if it affects their ability to meet credit requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae outlines the treatment of installment debt in determining the borrower's recurring monthly debt obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac's guidelines indicate that installment debt must be considered for borrowers with multiple payments remaining."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSTALLMENT DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE ASSUMPTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mortgage assumptions may alter the impact of existing installment debt on the borrower's financial standing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lease payments are considered a recurring monthly debt obligation for the borrower regardless of the lease term left."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac includes lease payments as recurring monthly debt obligations in borrower assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEASE PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;DEFAULT ON FINANCING TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Default on Financing Terms can occur if Lease Payments for Solar Panels are not met, affecting financial obligations and ownership rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2c659b65edef4a5e599f9445602b752</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;401K&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"401K loans are collateralized by the borrower's financial assets but do not count against their monthly debt obligations if properly documented."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IRA&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loans secured against an IRA can impact the borrower's asset reserves but are excluded from monthly debt obligations if documented."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IRA&quot;" target="&quot;ACCESS TO FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Access to funds in an IRA is crucial to assess its usability for loan purposes under the guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c392c46c8ab1fb7407628dd97c6f2c74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IRA&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae includes IRA accounts among the eligible assets for loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c392c46c8ab1fb7407628dd97c6f2c74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IRA&quot;" target="&quot;NET DOCUMENT ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"IRA accounts can be classified as net document assets when calculating income eligibility for loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49e500168a0590aef42a229f4ea93fe3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IRA&quot;" target="&quot;INTERNAL REVENUE SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The IRA must be recognized by the Internal Revenue Service (IRS), thereby showcasing a clear relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f67964fc288da88f7bb3defef1f29177</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IRA&quot;" target="&quot;RETIREMENT INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Distributions from an IRA are recognized as a form of retirement income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CD&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CDs can serve as collateral for loans without affecting the borrower's debt obligations, as long as documentation is provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE DEBT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mortgage debt obligations are part of the borrower's financial responsibilities when owning properties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-455b5668460db6760959b99f4a51a667</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN ANALYSIS&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac's guidelines play a key role in the loan analysis process during mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN ANALYSIS&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae's criteria influence the loan analysis and underwriting process for mortgage approvals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CASH BACK&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY MORTGAGE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cash back from transactions may affect the required monthly mortgage payments and related calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CASH BACK&quot;" target="&quot;CASH-OUT AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cash back is limited to a certain percentage of the cash-out amount available to the borrower during refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f76dd878d76d1e8bdf5fb1cac46447ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY MORTGAGE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;RELATED EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Monthly mortgage payments are related to the overall financial obligations of the borrower, which include related expenses like taxes and insurance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY MORTGAGE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;OBLIGATED NOTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The obligated note is directly related to the monthly mortgage payment that must be made by the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY MORTGAGE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;GUIDELINE RESERVES REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Monthly mortgage payments must comply with guideline reserves requirements to ensure financial stability for lenders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPEN 30-DAY CHARGE ACCOUNT&quot;" target="&quot;GUIDELINE RESERVES REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Guideline reserves requirements consider open charge accounts as part of the overall financial assessment for borrowers during underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELATED EXPENSES&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Related expenses must be considered alongside the mortgage when evaluating a borrower's financial responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MULTIPLE FINANCED PROPERTY COUNT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's financial status is assessed in part by the count of multiple financed properties they possess."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MULTIPLE FINANCED PROPERTY COUNT&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The multiple financed property count is a factor within the conventional underwriting guidelines for evaluating borrower risk."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GUIDELINE RESERVES REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower must meet specific guideline reserves requirements to qualify for a mortgage loan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b58c2a47b041d2502022392c611f405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL HOUSING PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower's monthly rental housing payment must be evaluated as part of their financial obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61ba5485d92daa30adf4ee02bfab7d8a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
