  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Equity Compensation often involves publicly traded stock that must be verified for loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14fb0d3aaa293edfdf71f855df5bd9ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERFORMANCE-BASED VESTING&quot;" target="&quot;EQUITY COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Equity Compensation often involves Performance-Based Vesting mechanisms that dictate how benefits are disbursed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14fb0d3aaa293edfdf71f855df5bd9ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CALENDAR YEARS&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE K-1&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule K-1 reporting requires documentation for the most recent two calendar years, demonstrating a time-based connection."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-76dfd0d1478f77acd572a51bf4e3956a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CALENDAR YEARS&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTED HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A documented history must span multiple calendar years to demonstrate income stability, connecting these concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-76dfd0d1478f77acd572a51bf4e3956a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;YTD PAYSTUB&quot;" target="&quot;INCOME CONTINUANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"YTD Paystub is important in verifying that Income Continuance is stable and ongoing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14fb0d3aaa293edfdf71f855df5bd9ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BROKERAGE OR BANK STATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Borrower is required to provide brokerage or bank statements to validate the transfer of shares or funds."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d411e3f303846f3eb00356498af7761f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME CONTINUANCE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Borrower's income must be likely to continue for the purpose of loan approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14fb0d3aaa293edfdf71f855df5bd9ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCOME CONTINUANCE&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTED TERMS OF INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DOCUMENTED TERMS OF INCOME are critical in determining the INCOME CONTINUANCE for retirement income verification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60ae7a36306412ca14db54586048b8bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EQUITY COMPENSATION&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Borrower's financial profile may include Equity Compensation components as part of their income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14fb0d3aaa293edfdf71f855df5bd9ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EARNINGS VERIFICATION&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Earnings verification is critical for assessing the Borrower's financial status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14fb0d3aaa293edfdf71f855df5bd9ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;YEAR-TO-DATE PAYSTUB&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"YEAR-TO-DATE PAYSTUBs are used to document funds from the Borrower's earnings over the given period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d411e3f303846f3eb00356498af7761f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TIME-BASED VESTING PROVISIONS&quot;" target="&quot;PAYOUTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payouts are dependent on the time-based vesting provisions of the Restricted Stock Units (RSUs)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d411e3f303846f3eb00356498af7761f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHARES&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Borrower's eligibility often depends on the number of shares they have received from their employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d411e3f303846f3eb00356498af7761f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHARES&quot;" target="&quot;BROKERAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Brokerage accounts are often used to manage shares, including the transfer of vested RSU shares or cash equivalents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHARES&quot;" target="&quot;CASH EQUIVALENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Shares distributed as cash equivalents represent an alternative form of payout that can affect the borrower's income calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSFER OF SHARES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The transfer of shares typically involves associated funds to be documented for accurate financial tracking."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d411e3f303846f3eb00356498af7761f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;CASH EQUIVALENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Funds can be transferred as cash equivalents from vesting shares, providing liquidity to the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BORROWER's FUNDS must be documented and verified as part of the mortgage qualification process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-023647e2d4d4ed50a6e5f501c055a8b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-PROVIDED STATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;YEAR-END PAYSTUB&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These documents are critical for verifying the borrower's income and ensuring accurate financial assessment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYOUTS&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSER OF SHARES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payouts of RS or RSU involve the transfer of shares to the Borrower indicating receipt of vested income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d411e3f303846f3eb00356498af7761f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYOUTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payouts from RSUs directly affect the borrower's overall financial situation and ability to repay loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYOUTS&quot;" target="&quot;CASH EQUIVALENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payouts can be received either in shares or as cash equivalents, offering flexibility for the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERIFICATION SERVICE PROVIDER&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The verification service provider is responsible for confirming the borrower's employment and income, which is critical for the loan process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERIFICATION SERVICE PROVIDER&quot;" target="&quot;VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Verification plays a critical role in confirming the borrower’s financial and employment status through the service provider."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CASH EQUIVALENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cash Equivalent is used in income calculations for the Borrower based on shares that are distributed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERIFICATION&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Underwriting guidelines dictate the verification process to ensure all income documentation is adequately assessed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STOCK PRICE&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICATION RECEIVED DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The stock price at the application received date is used to calculate the borrower's income from RSU shares distributed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95d0c65d8599d7d0f56b6359c8d77e68</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION RECEIVED DATE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Application Received Date affects calculations related to the income of the Borrower from RS or RSU distributions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION RECEIVED DATE&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Application Received Date is important in Fannie Mae's calculations for determining income stability of the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION RECEIVED DATE&quot;" target="&quot;CONFIRMATION DATE OF RETURN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The confirmation date of return must be tracked and noted as part of the application process for the borrower to ensure eligibility for loan approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION RECEIVED DATE&quot;" target="&quot;PRE-LEAVING INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Pre-leaving income is evaluated at the application received date to determine income eligibility prior to any temporary absences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER&quot;" target="&quot;LEADER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The seller needs to ensure compliance with community standards and financing guidelines when selling properties with solar panels."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-37ec0ad59b15ed4e4c83850695f40593</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEASONAL JOB INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Seasonal Job Income is considered stable income for qualifying the Borrower when a two-year history is provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEASONAL JOB INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae's guidelines reference Seasonal Job Income when assessing borrower qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEASONAL JOB INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY LEAVES OF ABSENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Seasonal Job Income may be impacted by records of Temporary Leaves of Absence when assessed for stability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Leaves of Absence can impact the stability of Seasonal Job Income for qualifying purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECONDARY EMPLOYMENT INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Secondary Employment Income can be used to qualify the Borrower if documented over the last two years."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECONDARY EMPLOYMENT INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae outlines conditions under which Secondary Employment Income can be considered in borrower assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECONDARY EMPLOYMENT INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;PART-TIME INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Secondary Employment Income can overlap with Part-Time Income when assessing borrower's total income sources."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY LEAVES OF ABSENCE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Temporary Leaves of Absence are relevant in the context of evaluating the Borrower's employment situation and income stability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY LEAVES OF ABSENCE&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae guidelines include regulations concerning Temporary Leaves of Absence for evaluating income stability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;52-WEEK AVERAGE STOCK PRICE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 52-week average stock price is necessary for calculating monthly income based on vested shares for the Borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRE-TAX&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Pre-Tax income figures are relevant for calculating the income of the Borrower from RS or RSU distributions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TWO-YEAR HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Two-Year History is a critical factor in determining the stability of income for the Borrower from various employment sources."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TWO-YEAR HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;GUARANTEED PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A TWO-YEAR HISTORY of receiving GUARANTEED PAYMENTS is required to validate the BORROWER's income from partnerships or LLCs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;12-MONTH HISTORY&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A 12-Month History can provide evidence for income qualification under certain circumstances for the Borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART-TIME INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part-Time Income is considered as a potential form of income for the Borrower, subject to certain documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART-TIME INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;VARIABLE INCOME SECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part-Time Income is evaluated under the guidelines of the Variable Income Section for borrower qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VARIABLE INCOME SECTION&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Variable Income Section outlines eligibility requirements that can affect the Borrower's overall income assessment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VARIABLE INCOME SECTION&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae utilizes the Variable Income Section to assess different types of income eligibility for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15bd1add6397f9fb7a5eda377f3403cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Temporary leave impacts the borrower's income during their absence from work, which is a critical factor in mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SHORT-TERM DISABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Short-term disability is one of the conditions that qualifies as a temporary leave that affects the borrower's income during the absence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave is mentioned as a specific instance of temporary leave, which can impact a borrower's income and documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;VERIFICATION OF BORROWER'S INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Verification of borrower's income must include assessments of income alterations due to temporary leave situations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Temporary leave may affect financial stability, which in turn can impact a borrower's capability to cover closing costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERIFICATION OF BORROWER'S INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Verification of the borrower's income is essential to determine eligibility during and after temporary leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TIP INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower has received tip income for the last two years, indicating a consistent source of income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tip income is a part of the borrower's financial profile, and its documentation is necessary to qualify them for a mortgage.</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT-TERM DISABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTATION FROM CURRENT EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documentation from the current employer is necessary to confirm income details related to short-term disability during the borrower's absence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTATION FROM CURRENT EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave requires specific documentation from the current employer to confirm the situation and the borrower's intention to return."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIQUID RESERVES&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Liquid reserves may be used to supplement the borrower's income when temporary income is lower than regular employment income, impacting loan approval and closing costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efc5b39715a3cc6b0751b8cfe29a66e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNEMPLOYMENT BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Unemployment Benefits are a form of income that may help in evaluating the financial stability of a borrower during periods of income loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unemployment benefits may be considered acceptable income for the borrower if properly documented and received consistently."</data>
  <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNEMPLOYMENT BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Union workers may receive unemployment benefits during downtime when not working, which can be included as income verification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNEMPLOYMENT BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;GOOD STANDING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A borrower receiving unemployment benefits must be a union member in good standing to qualify for certain loans."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;" target="&quot;SKILLED TRADES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Union workers are typically skilled tradespersons who may work in various skilled trades like electricians and plumbers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae provides guidelines for verifying employment for workers in short-term job assignments, often involving union workers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac has specific criteria for verifying employment for borrowers in industries where union workers frequently switch employers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;" target="&quot;ELECTRICIANS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Electricians are a specific category of skilled tradespeople who often belong to unions for job placements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;" target="&quot;PLUMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Plumbers are also categorized among the skilled trades represented by unions, facilitating their employment opportunities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;" target="&quot;ROOFERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Roofers are included in the skilled trades category under union workers, similar to electricians and plumbers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;" target="&quot;LONGSHOREMAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Longshoremen typically rely on unions for job placement, similar to other skilled trades workers like electricians and plumbers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;" target="&quot;STAGEHAND&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Stagehands often work in temporary positions facilitated by unions and are classified under union workers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNION WORKERS&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORKER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Construction workers may be unionized and benefit from union support in securing job placements and income verification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORM 4137&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower can document unreported tip income using Form 4137, which establishes tax liability on such income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-444e5ed0aa3891f1dfc3371133a3be60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYSTUBS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers must provide paystubs for income verification when applying for loans."</data>
