<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">35.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"RENTAL INCOME is considered part of the borrower's total monthly income, impacting their financial qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower's ability to present rental income directly affects their qualification for mortgage loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower's rental income is critical to evaluating their financial stability and loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"The borrower’s ability to generate rental income is critical for qualifying for loans and evaluating financial stability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8864c52069485823a39babaa2b2005e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae's guidelines dictate how rental income is calculated for borrower qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;FORM 1007&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FORM 1007 is a document used for reporting and calculating rental income for qualification purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Form 1007 is utilized to calculate rental income for properties, linking it directly to the reporting of rental income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;FORM 1025&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FORM 1025 serves a similar purpose as FORM 1007 in the context of rental income qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Form 1025 is used in the context of verifying rental income, thus closely related to the concept of rental income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;GROSS RENTAL INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"GROSS RENTAL INCOME influences the calculation of RENTAL INCOME, affecting the borrower's financial profile."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES dictate how RENTAL INCOME is assessed in evaluating borrower eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"RENTAL INCOME impacts the overall financial considerations tied to the borrower's MONTHLY OBLIGATIONS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT LEASE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The current lease agreement directly determines the rental income received from the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"The current lease agreement is a crucial document in determining the rental income for the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;NET RENTAL INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Net rental income is derived from the rental income after accounting for expenses such as losses and maintenance costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"RENTAL INCOME comprises the gross income reported, which becomes part of the NET RENTAL INCOME after deductions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb02bde5abfff1b16d83434416df7465</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rental income is calculated after accounting for maintenance expenses, which reduce the overall income from rental properties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;GROSS RENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Gross rent is a source of rental income for the property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE E&quot;">
  <data key="d4">54.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SCHEDULE E is used to document rental income, which is critical in assessing overall income for loan purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"SCHEDULE E is used to report income from rental properties, making it a key component in evaluating total rental income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule E is a tax form used to report rental income and related expenses, establishing a direct connection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule E is specifically used to report rental income, thereby directly relating to the concept of Rental Income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule E is used to calculate net rental income, directly defining the income from rental activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule E is used to document rental income and associated expenses for investment properties, reflecting financial performance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-10ce55972cf12e21fd77796ab69a96ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea98d6086733276bdd5c19993c4deb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8864c52069485823a39babaa2b2005e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79943296a1fa68394820a29e269db689</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY MANAGEMENT EXPERIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A history of property management experience is necessary for utilizing rental income under specific qualifying conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property management experience can enhance the ability to generate rental income, impacting underwriting decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10ce55972cf12e21fd77796ab69a96ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSACTION TYPE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rental Income is connected to various transaction types in real estate financing, affecting how properties are qualified."&lt;SEP&gt;"The type of transaction determines how rental income can be applied and calculated for qualifying purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;EXTENDED PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An extended period where rental properties are out of service affects the calculation and reporting of rental income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1578b8b51044019bfff38a69eecab0be</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;INVESTMENT PROPERTY PURCHASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rental income generated from the investment property is crucial for assessing its financial viability as part of the investment property purchase."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8864c52069485823a39babaa2b2005e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;REAL ESTATE OWNED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Income from real estate owned contributes to the overall rental income, affecting the borrower's financial assessment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8864c52069485823a39babaa2b2005e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;PURCHASE DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The purchase date of the investment property is significant for determining when rental income generation begins"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8864c52069485823a39babaa2b2005e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
