</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORM 1025&quot;" target="&quot;CALCULATING MONTHLY NET RENTAL INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Form 1025 is also utilized for the calculation of monthly net rental income in property transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-48dc06181f6c67399f82ff0110257532</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORM 1025&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FORM 1025 serves a similar purpose as FORM 1007 in assessing the borrower's financial stability and rental income documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8864c52069485823a39babaa2b2005e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GROSS RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT LEASE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Gross rental income is determined based on the current lease agreement's terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GROSS RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;NET RENTAL INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Net rental income is calculated as a percentage of gross rental income after accounting for losses and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GROSS RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;VACANCY LOSSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Vacancy losses directly affect the calculation of gross rental income, reducing the amount received."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GROSS RENTAL INCOME&quot;" target="&quot;ONGOING MAINTENANCE EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Ongoing maintenance expenses also reduce the effective gross rental income that can be calculated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CALCULATED RENTAL NET CASH FLOW&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CALCULATED RENTAL NET CASH FLOW can be used to offset the borrower's mortgage obligations when the property is a rental."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78e642bbbbe6e4f896abe6c8dfd4bab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SCHEDULE 1&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE E&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule 1 and Schedule E are typically filed together on income tax returns and are relevant for income verification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7c7059ebd575d1369f6649db3e25ee4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SCHEDULE 1&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT LEASE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The current lease agreement may provide information relevant to Schedule 1 for tax purposes, indicating additional rental context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1fc933db1bd6fd3476c94d029ad8540</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
