  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The total obligations on mortgages or notes are subtracted from business cash flow adjustments during mortgage evaluation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS CASH FLOW ADJUSTMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;DEPRECIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Depreciation can be added back to business cash flow when evaluating mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS CASH FLOW ADJUSTMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;AMORTIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Amortization may also affect business cash flow adjustments considered for qualifying for a mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SCHEDULE K-1&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SCHEDULE K-1 documents the stable income distributions from a partnership or LLC that can be considered by the BORROWER when calculating cash flow."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
