  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The presence of fluid assets is crucial for managing obligations on mortgages or notes during the evaluation process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d14191b10a7b641a859301abcf2d9873</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;QUICK RATIO&quot;" target="&quot;LIQUIDITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"QUICK RATIO is used to assess the liquidity of a business, ensuring it can cover its current liabilities without relying on inventory."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Quick Ratio is a financial metric used to assess liquidity, measuring a company's ability to meet short-term obligations without relying on inventory."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;QUICK RATIO&quot;" target="&quot;EARNINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"QUICK RATIO provides insight into the business's capacity to withdraw EARNINGS without jeopardizing liquidity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;QUICK RATIO&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS LIQUIDITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business liquidity can be assessed using the quick ratio, establishing an analytical relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"The quick ratio measures business liquidity, indicating its importance for financial health."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-76dfd0d1478f77acd572a51bf4e3956a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKING CAPITAL RATIO&quot;" target="&quot;CURRENT RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ratios are used to assess business liquidity, each serving different types of businesses depending on their inventory reliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKING CAPITAL RATIO&quot;" target="&quot;LIQUIDITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"WORKING CAPITAL RATIO is another metric for evaluating a business's liquidity, particularly for those that do not rely heavily on inventory."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKING CAPITAL RATIO&quot;" target="&quot;EARNINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"WORKING CAPITAL RATIO assesses the ability of a business to generate EARNINGS while maintaining adequate liquidity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKING CAPITAL RATIO&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS LIQUIDITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The working capital ratio is used to assess a business's liquidity, creating a direct relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-76dfd0d1478f77acd572a51bf4e3956a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIQUIDITY&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS LIQUIDITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Liquidity assessments in general apply to business liquidity, ensuring businesses can meet current liabilities with their available cash flow."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GUARANTEED PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;OWNER'S SHARE OF BUSINESS INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Guaranteed payments are considered as a part of the owner's share of income when qualifying for cash flow."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-398938dbff78b05d0c3830d36e6918b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GUARANTEED PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BORROWER must have a consistent history of receiving GUARANTEED PAYMENTS to qualify additional income in cash flow analysis."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27c5b5517eef234cf0db585936ec28f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GUARANTEED PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;IRS SCHEDULE K-1&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Guaranteed payments for partners may be reported on an IRS Schedule K-1, establishing a connection in reporting income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-76dfd0d1478f77acd572a51bf4e3956a</data>
