<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The down payment requirements for manufactured homes are defined by Fannie Mae guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;EQUITY REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Equity requirements directly influence the down payment requirements for financing manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSTITUTE FOR BUILDING TECHNOLOGY AND SAFETY (IBTS)&quot;" target="&quot;HUD DATA PLATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"IBTS verification letters can serve as an alternative to HUD Data Plates for compliance evidence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f55695b58ffd5e2ba42b42a2ed0cdbf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HUD DATA PLATE&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conventional underwriting guidelines require verification of details from the HUD Data Plate for manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HUD DATA PLATE&quot;" target="&quot;PERMANENT FOUNDATION SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Verification of the permanent foundation system must be referenced in conjunction with the HUD Data Plate requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WARRANTY DEED&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower needs to provide a warranty deed that shows there are no outstanding liens against the property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WARRANTY DEED&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSFER OF OWNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The warranty deed is necessary to document the transfer of ownership of the property in loan transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXISTING MANUFACTURED HOMES&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower may seek to purchase existing manufactured homes, affecting the equity contribution in the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIEN SEARCH&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Property records are utilized in conducting a lien search to verify liens against the land and manufactured home."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CASH INVESTMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The borrower must document their cash investment, which is essential for the loan approval process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ebee13ef54f5a678a952e514a3a25998</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORM 1004C&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Form 1004C is necessary to appraise manufactured homes and is required documentation for borrowers seeking loans for such properties."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN APPLICATION DATE&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Closing costs must be calculated based on criteria established before the loan application date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENCUMBRANCE&quot;" target="&quot;OUTSTANDING LIENS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Outstanding liens can create encumbrances on the manufactured home, affecting its marketability and loan options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Outstanding liens represent encumbrances that must be addressed during refinancing processes for manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENCUMBRANCE&quot;" target="&quot;MAXIMUM LTV OF 65%&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Encumbrance of a manufactured home affects its maximum allowable LTV ratio when refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6c568dd7273250cbc578b2e15944d1bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN FILE&quot;" target="&quot;INSPECTION REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The inspection report must be kept as part of the mortgage loan file to ensure compliance with underwriting standards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN FILE&quot;" target="&quot;MODEL NAME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The appraiser is required to include the model name of the manufactured home in the mortgage loan file for documentation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN FILE&quot;" target="&quot;YEAR OF MANUFACTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The year of manufacture must be documented within the mortgage loan file as part of the appraisal process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN FILE&quot;" target="&quot;SERIAL NUMBER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The appraiser must record the serial number of the manufactured home in the mortgage loan file for identification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOCAL AND STATE CODES&quot;" target="&quot;SEPTIC TANK OR SEWAGE SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Connection to a septic tank or sewage system must comply with local and state codes for manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b93ae0daff9b29376c9af8da1cb0522</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORY-BUILT HOUSING&quot;" target="&quot;SITE-BUILT HOUSING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Factory-built housing is treated similarly to site-built housing under eligibility requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MODULAR HOMES&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae purchases loans secured by modular homes that comply with the International Residential Code."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MODULAR HOMES&quot;" target="&quot;INTERNATIONAL RESIDENTIAL CODE (IRC)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Modular homes must be built under the International Residential Code for eligibility with Fannie Mae."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MODULAR HOMES&quot;" target="&quot;MULTI-UNIT BUILDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Multi-unit buildings may incorporate modular construction techniques, subject to adherence to local building codes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREFABRICATED, PANELIZED, AND SECTIONAL HOMES&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae also purchases loans secured by prefabricated, panelized, or sectional housing under specific eligibility guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREFABRICATED, PANELIZED, AND SECTIONAL HOMES&quot;" target="&quot;LOCAL BUILDING CODES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Prefabricated homes must conform to local building codes in the area where they are located."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MULTI-UNIT BUILDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;HOUSING ELIGIBILITY GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Multi-unit buildings constructed using modular techniques must adhere to housing eligibility guidelines to be financed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEED OF TRUST&quot;" target="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A mortgage must be secured by a perfected lien on both the manufactured home and the land."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FOUNDATION&quot;" target="&quot;PERMANENT ATTACHMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Permanent attachment to a foundation is a requirement for manufactured homes to be classified as real property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHATTEL&quot;" target="&quot;FIRST-LIEN MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A first-lien mortgage must secure real property, differentiating it from chattel property in financing manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTES&quot;" target="&quot;JUDICIAL DECISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Judicial decisions and statutes both play a role in determining how manufactured homes are classified under state law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOUSING ELIGIBILITY GUIDELINES&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Housing eligibility guidelines dictate the criteria under which Fannie Mae will purchase loans for manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0031128e81eed5883f39146514f546</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIXED-USE PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae has specific guidelines for mixed-use properties which they accept under certain residential conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIXED-USE PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac also has guidelines for mixed-use properties that align with Fannie Mae's requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIXED-USE PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;BUILDING CODES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mixed-use properties must adhere to local building codes in their construction and operation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARCEL&quot;" target="&quot;SECURITY PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Security property can consist of multiple parcels, which must be conveyed in their entirety and adequately described in the loan file."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUILDING CODES&quot;" target="&quot;MODULAR CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Modular construction techniques must conform to local building codes for building approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECURITY PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Security property evaluations are governed by underwriting guidelines which ensure compliance with lending standards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3e0ec6e1adaeb678f542089515e77ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;FINAL TITLE POLICY REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Environmental protection considerations are included in the final title policy requirements, ensuring legal and environmental compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Environmental protection guidelines are interconnected with environmental assessments to ensure compliance and risk management."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TYPE E PUD PROJECT&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Type E PUD projects are specifically classified by Fannie Mae, which recognizes established developments with community oversight."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TYPE F PUD PROJECT&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac does not impose additional guidelines on Type F PUD Projects, indicating a regulatory relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Type F PUD projects are acknowledged by Freddie Mac as new projects requiring adherence to specific guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TYPE F PUD PROJECT&quot;" target="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fannie Mae's guidelines on PUD projects align with the specifications of Type F PUD projects, indicating a regulatory relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIABILITY INSURANCE&quot;" target="&quot;FLAGSTAR BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Flagstar Bank has specific guidelines regarding liability insurance, particularly defining requirements for Type E and F projects."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIABILITY INSURANCE&quot;" target="&quot;RISK MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Risk management practices in property development often involve liability insurance to safeguard against potential legal claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIABILITY INSURANCE&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Liability Insurance safeguards against potential future losses that may arise from borrowing activity impacting the financial standing of the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINAL TITLE POLICY REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;ALTA 9 RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Final title policy requirements must include compliance with ALTA 9 restrictions, ensuring proper documentation and protection for owners."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MORTGAGE GUIDELINES&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conventional underwriting guidelines will influence the mortgage guidelines set for properties undergoing evaluation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e26a3be3838ff40fb61edfe66e0268a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TYPE E OR TYPE F PUD&quot;" target="&quot;DETACHED DWELLING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Type E or Type F PUD does not require a review if the subject property is a detached dwelling, showing a conditional relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POSTPONED OR INCOMPLETE IMPROVEMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;REPAIR ESCROWS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Repair escrows are available for properties with postponed or incomplete improvements as long as specific requirements are met, showing a structural relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POSTPONED OR INCOMPLETE IMPROVEMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac has guidelines for handling postponed or incomplete improvements, indicating an oversight relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHARED WELL AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;WATER SOURCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A recorded shared well agreement is necessary for properties with a water source provided by a shared well, indicating a regulatory requirement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAIR ESCROWS&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPANCY PERMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"New construction and existing properties requiring repair escrows should not impact the ability to obtain an occupancy permit, indicating a procedural relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAIR ESCROWS&quot;" target="&quot;REPAIR LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Repair escrows are dependent on the established repair limits, showing a financial relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBJECT PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;WATER SOURCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subject properties must have an approved water source if using a shared well, reflecting a property regulation relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAIR LIMITS&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Repair limits are specified under Conventional Underwriting Guidelines, showing that they directly inform the conditions for repair escrows."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATE LAWS&quot;" target="&quot;REDEEMTION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"State laws dictate the terms of the redemption period after foreclosure, establishing a legal relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5dd59acfc6b78474b4cbf40ec7d05399</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ESCROW HOLDBACK AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;FLAGSTAR BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Flagstar Bank is responsible for holding all repair escrows, including those outlined in the Escrow Holdback Agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d77c56c7ef7f25742c687f6ad137c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ESCROW HOLDBACK AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSING DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The escrow holdback agreement specifies that repairs must be completed within 180 days of the closing date, linking timelines directly to contractual agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-00440a55cc64896de959c80a8727fbfc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINIMUM CREDIT SCORES&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines include requirements for Minimum Credit Scores that borrowers must meet."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d77c56c7ef7f25742c687f6ad137c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOUBLE-WIDE MANUFACTURED HOME&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Guidelines for conventional underwriting specify requirements for double-wide manufactured homes involving underwriting criteria."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d77c56c7ef7f25742c687f6ad137c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPAIRS AND IMPROVEMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLETION OF IMPROVEMENTS&quot;">
