  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;ACCEPTABLE SOURCES OF FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Acceptable Sources of Funds highlight the recognized ways in which a borrower can authenticate their financial resources for loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENT CERTIFICATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Document Certifications are formal affirmations made by the borrower regarding the authenticity of their submitted documents during the loan process."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;ACCOUNT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Account History is critical in demonstrating a borrower's financial stability by showcasing their past transactions and balances during evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;COVENANTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Covenants outline the conditions and terms connected to the borrower's mortgage agreements necessary for understanding obligations during loan servicing."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;ADJUSTMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Adjustment Period refers to a specified time frame in which the rates applicable to a borrower's mortgage may be altered based on market conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;BARRED CREDITORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Barred Creditors are entities that cannot claim damages against the borrower, impacting financial evaluations in lending scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;COBORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Coborrower is someone who shares the borrowing responsibility with the primary borrower, which may affect credit assessments and loan terms."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER CONTRIBUTION REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Borrower Contribution Requirement denotes the minimum amount of personal funds a borrower is expected to invest in a property purchase during mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;LOAN PARAMETERS FOR EMPLOYMENT(RELATED ASSETS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loan Parameters for Employment-Related Assets provide specific criteria for evaluating the borrower's income-producing assets during qualification."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTS REQUIRED TO COMPLETE A LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documents Required to Complete a Loan specify the myriad of documentation and forms that need to be collected from the borrower for successful approval."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;ACTIVE LOANS&quot;">
