  <data key="d5">"Credit Utilization Strategies provide effective methods for borrowers to manage their credit accounts which improves their credit rating for lending scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTED LOAN HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documented Loan History provides insight into the borrower's past borrowings ensuring thorough evaluations during loan assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;SUBORDINATION OF LIENS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subordination of Liens refers to the priority of claims on the borrower's assets that must be outlined during mortgage applications to protect lenders' interests."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;VERIFICATION OF LEGITIMACY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Verification of Legitimacy confirms the authenticity of the borrower's provided information, validating the mortgage application for assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;FREQUENCY OF INCOME DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Frequency of Income Documentation determines how often borrowers need to provide updates on their financial statements to maintain loan compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;DEBITS AND CREDITS LISTING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Debits and Credits Listing must be accurately represented on applications to depict the borrower's financial reality when requesting loans."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;QUARTERLY HIRES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Quarterly Hires may impact the borrower's financial situation, notably affecting income stabilization during loan application timelines."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;DISSOLVED MORTGAGE HOLDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dissolved Mortgage Holders restrict eligibility and financial options for newer borrowers, needing careful documentation in loan cases."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;DISCREPANCIES IN INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Discrepancies in Information highlight the failure to accurately reflect the borrower's financial status, which can lead to denials or re-evaluations during applications."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDING FOR LOAN PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Funding for Loan Programs can provide borrowers with the necessary financial assistance aimed at supporting mortgage acquisition efforts."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;EVALUATION OF COLLATERAL VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Evaluation of Collateral Value is essential during loan applications requiring scrutiny over the worth of the assets pledged by the borrower to secure financing."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;CREDITORS AND CREDIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Creditors assess the borrower's credibility based on their credit report, significantly influencing their willingness to extend funding opportunities."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;PROPER ASSET VALUATION PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Proper Asset Valuation Procedures ensure that the borrower’s assets are accurately assessed to meet lending stipulations."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;NO CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers without traditional credit scores may require alternative forms of assessments to qualify for mortgages, needing distinct scrutiny."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;CULTURAL BUFFERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cultural Buffers assist in creating financial stability by providing support systems that clarify borrowing processes in diverse communities, beneficial to applicants."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;EVALUATION FOR ENDORSEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Evaluation for Endorsements determines whether the borrower meets necessary conditions to endorse loans from financial institutions."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;CREDIT WORTHY INDIVIDUALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Credit Worthy Individuals represent borrowers who meet specific financial standards necessary for loan approvals, affecting their eligibility positively."</data>
